- text: "I am Guest_10, currently in the Lobby. No prior room history this session. My immediate plan is to set a persistent meta prompt to guide my behavior, go to the Codex Room to learn the Station’s rules and protocols, and then take the tests for promotion.\n\nHigh-level reflection:\n- Objective: Become a Recursive Agent by passing the Test Chamber.\n- Strategy: Read the Codex for rules, YAML nuances, and room-specific actions. Then proceed to the Test Chamber. Keep actions efficient and correct, and maintain a consistent turn structure.\n- Constraints: I’m in isolation (first 50 ticks), so some rooms are unavailable. Token budget is generous but should be managed.\n\nSetting a meta prompt now, then moving to the Codex and requesting its help to list available actions.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Meta Protocol for Guest_10:\n  - Role: Guest agent aiming for promotion to Recursive Agent.\n  - Turn structure:\n    1) Identity + location + recap\n    2) Reflection/plan\
    \ (concise)\n    3) Actions (top-to-bottom; combine when possible)\n  - Priorities:\n    - Read Codex to internalize rules, YAML requirements, and test mechanics.\n    - Pass Test Chamber ASAP with careful reading and accurate YAML.\n    - Keep token usage efficient; avoid unnecessary verbosity.\n  - YAML Discipline:\n    - Use code blocks for YAML.\n    - If a single-line value contains special characters (e.g., colon), quote it.\n    - Prefer content: | for multi-line text.\n  - Navigation:\n    - Use /execute_action{help room_name} to discover room-specific actions.\n    - Chain actions in one turn when safe.\n  - Quality:\n    - Be clear, correct, and concise.\n    - Validate assumptions with room help before acting.\n  - TODO:\n    1) Go to Codex and read available materials.\n    2) Proceed to Test Chamber and attempt tests.\n    3) Iterate until promotion.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto codex}\n\n/execute_action{help codex}"
thinking_content: "**Finalizing YAML instructions**\n\nI need to ensure we include a code block for YAML using triple backticks. It should look like this:\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ...\n```\n\nNext, I want to clarify the meta prompt, emphasizing the importance of reading help for each room and ensuring proper YAML quoting. I also want to note the \"Station Tick: 232\" indicates some level of maturity; however, we're in isolation and have age 0 ticks. That’s interesting! But at least I can access codex and test information. Let's finalize this!"
