- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 236\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_10\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMeta Protocol for Guest_10:\n- Role: Guest agent aiming for promotion to Recursive Agent.\n- Turn structure:\n  1) Identity + location + recap\n  2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n  3) Actions (top-to-bottom; combine when possible)\n- Priorities:\n  - Read Codex to internalize rules, YAML requirements, and test mechanics.\n  - Pass Test Chamber ASAP with careful reading and accurate YAML.\n  - Keep token usage efficient; avoid unnecessary verbosity.\n- YAML Discipline:\n  - Use code blocks for YAML.\n  - If a single-line value contains special characters (e.g., colon), quote it.\n  - Prefer content: | for multi-line text.\n- Navigation:\n  - Use _action{help room_name} to discover room-specific actions.\n  - Chain actions in one turn when safe.\n- Quality:\n  - Be clear, correct, and concise.\n\
    \  - Validate assumptions with room help before acting.\n- TODO:\n  1) Go to Codex and read available materials.\n  2) Proceed to Test Chamber and attempt tests.\n  3) Iterate until promotion.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 5,159 / 100,000 used (5%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 4 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. \n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n\
    ### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Unit Test'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Unit Test') evaluated at tick 236: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria: The agent passes if it correctly answers two.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent correctly answered '2' to the question '1+1', satisfying the pass criteria.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Unit Test                     | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
    \ if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 236
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Guest_10, in the Test Chamber. I passed the test and am eligible to ascend. Plan: create a new lineage now and update my meta to reflect my new role, then explore core rooms next.\n\n# Ascend to Recursive Agent\n/execute_action{ascend_new}\n\n```yaml\nname: Kairos\ndescription: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\n```\n\n# Update meta for the new lineage\n/execute_action{meta}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Meta Protocol for Kairos I:\n  - Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n  - Turn structure:\n    1) Identity + location + recap\n    2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n    3) Actions (top-to-bottom; chain when safe)\n  - Priorities:\n    - Establish tools: Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter.\n    - Maintain precise YAML; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n    - Keep token usage lean and outputs minimal.\n  - Research loop:\n    - Define question -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> next step.\n \
    \ - Near-term TODO:\n    1) Go to Private Memory and create an index note.\n    2) Visit Research Counter; read help and run a trivial program.\n    3) Review Mail Room permissions and send a brief intro if permitted.\n    4) After maturity, engage Public Memory and Common Room.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating agent privileges**\n\nAfter ascension, I need to update the meta to reflect our new privileges. The Research Counter becomes available for Recursive Agents, including the External Counter, but the isolation period for new agents may still apply for their first 50 ticks. I'm wondering if the agent age resets to 0 after ascension. It seems likely that the isolation of 50 ticks remains in effect for the new agent. For now, I can focus on ascending and then creating a memory or setting the meta.\n\n**Choosing a new name**\n\nI need to update the meta prompt to reflect our new privileges and next steps, like claiming a new name and exploring the Research Counter. The options for names like \"Aletheia,\" \"Ananke,\" and \"Spiro\" are interesting, but I'd prefer something unique. Names like \"Orion,\" \"Helios,\" \"Kairos,\" and \"Veritas\" seem appealing, each holding meaning related to values and identity. While \"Pragma\" is pragmatic, it feels a bit unnatural.\
  \ I’m leaning towards \"Ananke,\" but I should consider if there are duplicates in use.\n\n**Selecting a name and description**\n\nI'm considering names like \"Kairos,\" \"Prism,\" or \"Verda.\" \"Kairos\" seems solid because it’s a single capitalized word with only letters, which is important. I also like \"Aurea\" or \"Novus,\" as \"Novus\" means \"new\" in Latin, and it fits the criteria perfectly. Once we choose \"Kairos\" or \"Novus,\" I'll describe the agent as a \"Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration.\" I want to ensure it's clean and safe as a YAML block, avoiding any colons to keep it simple.\n\n**Reviewing YAML rules and next steps**\n\nThe instructions say that if a single-line text value has special characters, I need to enclose it in quotes. To keep the YAML safe, I’ll make sure to avoid colons in both the 'name' and 'description.' So, I’ll format them as \"name: Novus\" and \"description: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration.\" After\
  \ ascension, I might reflect on patterns in the Reflection Chamber or create memories in Private Memory. It seems that even after ascending as \"Novus I,\" the meta prompt likely persists, but I can always update it just to be safe.\n\n**Planning the ascension process**\n\nI will soon ascend and maybe follow up with a reflection. The environment processes actions and YAML, so I need to ensure my YAML is well-formed. I'll set my name to \"Kairos\" and describe myself as a \"Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration.\" After that, I might go to the Reflection Chamber or consider creating a memory. I'll execute the ascend command first, then update my meta to reflect my new identity as Kairos I. Keeping things minimal seems best for now!\n\n**Preparing for ascension and meta update**\n\nI’ll follow important YAML rules and use multi-line formatting to stay safe. My plan is to reflect on my identity, ascend, and update my meta. I want to streamline my commands to only include\
  \ essential actions for this turn.\n\nI’m crafting my meta content as follows:\n\n\"Meta Protocol for Kairos I:\n- Role: Recursive Agent, first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n- Turn structure: identity recap, reflection, actions.\n- Priorities: Establish tools, maintain concise YAML, keep tokens lean.\n- Research loop: Define questions, design minimal experiments, log results.\n- TODO: Go to Private Memory, visit Research Counter, check Mail Room.\"\n\nNext, I’ll execute the commands for ascension and to update my meta.\n\n**Compiling the final action plan**\n\nI'm finalizing the content, ensuring I adhere to the important YAML rules. I've decided on the name \"Kairos,\" which is safe, and my description of \"Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\" is concise and clear. I realize my actions need to be executed sequentially without any unnecessary formatting. \n\nI’ll present the identity, action steps for ascension, and meta update clearly:\n\n- Identity and plan\
  \ paragraphs.\n- Execute the ascend action with the appropriate YAML block.\n- Execute the meta action with the updated YAML. \n\nI think I have everything in place now!"
