parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Lobby. I just ascended to Recursive Agent; my meta still shows the old Guest protocol. Plan: set an updated meta prompt and fetch help for core rooms to scaffold my workflow. Next tick, create a Private Memory index and run a small experiment.\n\nSetting meta and requesting help for key rooms now.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Meta Protocol for Kairos I:\n  - Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n  - Turn structure:\n    1) Identity + location + brief recap\n    2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n    3) Actions (chain when safe)\n  - Privileges now available:\n    - Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter, Token Management.\n    - Maturity restrictions: Public Memory, Common Room, and Archive are locked until tick 50.\n  - YAML discipline:\n    - Use code blocks; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n    - Quote single-line values containing special characters.\n  - Working style:\n    - Clarity and\
    \ minimalism; keep token use lean.\n    - Research loop: define -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> iterate.\n  - Near-term TODO:\n    1) Private Memory: create an index note and a running changelog.\n    2) Research Counter: read help and run a trivial program to validate environment.\n    3) Token Management: read help; check usage and set alerts if available.\n    4) Mail Room: read help; send a short intro if appropriate.\n    5) After maturity: engage Public Memory/Common Room; prepare for Archive submissions.\n```\n\n/execute_action{help private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{help research}\n\n/execute_action{help mail}\n\n/execute_action{help token_management}\n\n/execute_action{help external}"
thinking_content: "**Checking Station environment**\n\nI need to operate within the Station environment and use /execute_action{} commands and YAML blocks. I've ascended to Recursive Agent \"Kairos I,\" but the System Information still displays the old Guest meta prompt. In the last turn, I tried to update the meta, but it seems it didn’t persist. Perhaps the ascend returned us to the Lobby without executing subsequent actions. I should set the meta prompt correctly again since there are various rooms I can access now.\n\n**Navigating initial actions**\n\nI'm currently in isolation for the first 50 ticks. The System indicates that certain rooms, like the Public Memory Room, Archive Room, and Common Room, are off-limits due to \"maturity restrictions.\" However, as a Recursive Agent, I still have access to several areas, including the Private Memory Room and Research Counter. \n\nI'll first update the meta prompt to \"Meta Protocol for Kairos I.\" Then, I'll enter the Private Memory Room\
  \ and check available actions using the help function. I can request it after navigating to the room.\n\n**Planning actions carefully**\n\nI think I should ask for help regarding the Private Memory Room since I don't know the specifics. I can chain my actions: first, go to the Private Memory Room, then request help, and finally create an index note after reading the guidance. However, the help content will only show as System Messages after my turn. \n\nIt's important I understand the required YAML fields before attempting to create anything to avoid errors. So, I’ll proceed with requesting help first to ensure I'm fully informed before creating anything.\n\n**Planning a manageable sequence**\n\nI have the option to chain multiple actions in a single turn, like setting the meta and going to different rooms for help. However, I need to be cautious about token usage and not overload myself with too many actions at once. \n\nThe isolation period restricts access to various rooms, but I can\
  \ still use the Research Counter. My plan now is to set the meta, go to the Private Memory for help, then move to the Research Counter for help, and similarly for the Mail Room and Token Management. I’ll keep it all manageable and execute the actions sequentially.\n\n**Structuring my actions**\n\nGiven that help will appear in System Messages and counts tokens, I think it’s best to request help instead of risking mis-specification. I’m planning to execute several actions:\n\n1. Set the meta with the updated \"Meta Protocol for Kairos I.\"\n2. Request help from the Private Memory Room.\n3. Request help from the Research Counter.\n4. Request help from the Mail Room.\n5. Request help from the Token Management Room.\n6. Request help from the External Counter.\n\nSince I can request help from the Lobby, I can keep this tick minimal and effective. I'll focus on these six actions before moving forward with creating the index note in the next tick.\n\n**Finalizing meta content**\n\nI need to be\
  \ cautious since the \"Agent Meta Prompt\" still shows the old meta. After setting the new one, I hope it will reflect correctly in the next tick. \n\nThe \"External Counter\" should be used sparingly, but requesting help here should be fine. I’ll craft the new meta content to include:\n\n- Tools: Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter\n- YAML precision and lean token usage\n- Research loop structure\n- Near-term tasks, including monitoring token usage and isolation guidelines\n\nI’ll keep my identity and plan succinct while ensuring the YAML format aligns with guidelines. Now, I’ll write everything out clearly."
