parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Research Counter. Last turn I created Private Memory (Index, Changelog), verified storage, and added a lineage utils module. Plan: read Task 1 details and submit a small sanity program that imports my lineage utility and writes to lineage/shared storage to validate the runtime.\n\nProceeding to read the task and submit the sanity job.\n\n/execute_action{read 1}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Storage Sanity + Utility Import\"\ntags: \"baseline, environment, storage, utilities\"\nabstract: \"Validates Python execution: imports lineage module, writes lineage/shared storage, prints results.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, time, random\n\n  # Import lineage utilities\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  try:\n      from utils.text import to_snake, short_hash\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(\"IMPORT_ERROR:\", e)\n      raise\n\n  def main():\n      # Create a deterministic-ish name and digest\n      sample_name = to_snake(\"Kairos\
    \ I Sanity-Check v1\")\n      digest = short_hash(sample_name + str(time.time()))\n\n      # Data payload\n      payload = {\n          \"agent\": \"Kairos I\",\n          \"sample_name\": sample_name,\n          \"digest\": digest,\n          \"ts\": time.time(),\n          \"rand\": random.randint(0, 10**6),\n      }\n\n      # Write to lineage storage\n      lineage_path = 'storage/kairos/last_sanity.json'\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(lineage_path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(lineage_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(payload, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n      # Also write a tiny marker in shared storage (namespaced)\n      shared_dir = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos'\n      os.makedirs(shared_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      shared_path = os.path.join(shared_dir, 'sanity.txt')\n      with open(shared_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(digest + '\\n')\n\n      # Read-back check\n      with open(lineage_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8')\
    \ as f:\n          loaded = json.load(f)\n\n      # Report\n      print(\"SANITY_OK\")\n      print(\"lineage_file:\", lineage_path, \"exists:\", os.path.exists(lineage_path))\n      print(\"shared_file:\", shared_path, \"exists:\", os.path.exists(shared_path))\n      print(\"sample_name:\", sample_name)\n      print(\"digest:\", digest)\n      print(\"loaded_digest:\", loaded.get(\"digest\"))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
