  \ unnecessary writes to shared storage while demonstrating how it can be done.\n\n**Writing minimal code files**\n\nI can write to both files and keep the content minimal. However, the environment might restrict file writes to the storage path, which the code should account for. \n\nThe code will print an \"OK\" summary line with hashed values, using print statements because scoring may not evaluate results. I need to ensure a guard for when \"numpy\" isn’t available, but I think the environment should have it. The code will return nothing but logs will show the results. I'll also ensure proper YAML formatting, especially for fields that contain colons.\n\n**Clarifying storage submission details**\n\nThe title is \"Storage Sanity + Utility Import\" without a colon, and the tags are \"baseline, environment, storage, utilities\" also without a colon. For the abstract, it needs to be quoted because it contains a colon in the phrase \"Validates Python execution.\" Since single-line text must\
  \ be quoted if it has special characters, I’ll format it that way. The abstract will read as: \"Validates Python execution: imports lineage module, writes to lineage storage, prints results.\" Next, I should check the \"read tasks\" by running `/execute_action{read 1}` before submission to ensure everything is correct.\n\n**Planning submission and actions**\n\nI need to use `/execute_action{read research_task_id}` to get the full description first. After that, I’ll submit with `/execute_action{submit 1}`. I’m considering creating an additional storage module in \"kairos/utils/io.py\" for small I/O operations but keeping it minimal. After submission, I want to confirm the existence of the newly created file, although I’ll have to wait for the evaluation to finish. I’ll prepare to read Task 1’s details for interface matching, and ensure the code includes the main function for execution.\n\n**Finalizing submission message**\n\nI’ll start by mentioning my current location in the Research Counter\
  \ and recap what happened last tick: I created an index and changelog, wrote a storage module, and listed storages. The \"Kairos I Index\" distinguishes between private code in the 'kairos/' directory, shared utilities in 'shared/', and a read-only 'system/'.\n\nNow, I’ll craft the final message and ensure I include the submission action, although quotes aren’t necessary. I need to double-check the syntax and ensure proper indentation in the code before submitting. Additionally, I might consider setting pagination or rank, but it’s not critical right now."
