  \ to verify the run_id. \n\nFinally, I'll summarize evaluation 611 results in the capsule 2 changelog. Adding an IO helper might be beneficial, even though we need to keep everything minimal.\n\n**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m considering setting up a token management schedule, but it might not be necessary right now. We could update 'meta' to include the latest usage or mark the 'Near-term TODO' as done, though leaving it as is may suffice for now.\n\nFirst, I’ll focus on verifying and logging everything and maybe quickly add the IO utility to check its accuracy. Since the user hasn't asked for anything specific, I'll layout my actions clearly. \n\nI’ll ensure to structure my output correctly in YAML format, particularly with the 'content' field, and note that the earlier storage list returned no files, which is interesting but probably fine.\n\n**Creating I/O helpers**\n\nI’m planning to mark the rule about being able to read from any lineage's storage, but it seems unnecessary right\
  \ now. Instead, my focus is on creating I/O helper functions with careful coding. \n\nI’ll implement path functions to ensure necessary directories exist, like 'ensure_parent_dir(path)'. I’ll also code basic read and write functions for JSON and text files. I'll make sure everything uses 'utf-8' encoding and add all this to 'kairos/utils/io.py'. \n\nAfter verifying artifacts, I might store the run_id in the changelog message. Additionally, I wonder about the isolation restrictions for mail, especially since we've noted they apply to new agents.\n\n**Summarizing actions and updates**\n\nThe current guidelines indicate that new agents begin in isolation for the first 50 ticks, with limited access to certain resources. While mail restrictions weren't mentioned, it seems there's some flexibility. For now, I’ll hold off on sending mail, but updating Private Memory to include pointers to created code modules might be useful.\n\nNext, I'll focus on verifying logs and checking storage. I’ll implement\
  \ the I/O helper functions while ensuring to structure everything correctly for my summaries in YAML format. \n\nAfter confirming the necessary values, I’ll summarize the results and outline the next steps in my reply."
