- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: template run (611) succeeded; artifacts verified; added io utils. Plan: add a multi-seed batch experiment, submit it, and log.\n\nProceeding to create batch experiment, submit, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/experiments/ridge_batch.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Batch ridge-solve experiment over multiple seeds with aggregation.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, argparse\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  from utils.timer import now\n  import experiment_template as et\n\n  def run_batch(seeds, n=250, lam=1e-3, tag=\"template_batch\"):\n      per = []\n      for seed in seeds:\n          m = et.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam)\n          per.append(m)\n      resids = np.array([m[\"resid\"] for m in per], dtype=float)\n      elapseds = np.array([m[\"elapsed\"] for m in per], dtype=float)\n      agg = {\n          \"ts\": now(),\n          \"seeds\": list(seeds),\n\
    \          \"runs\": len(seeds),\n          \"n\": int(n),\n          \"lam\": float(lam),\n          \"resid_mean\": float(resids.mean()),\n          \"resid_std\": float(resids.std()),\n          \"elapsed_mean\": float(elapseds.mean()),\n          \"elapsed_std\": float(elapseds.std()),\n          # Convenience keys to align with single-run schema\n          \"resid\": float(resids.mean()),\n          \"elapsed\": float(elapseds.mean()),\n          \"per_run\": per,\n      }\n      return et.save_metrics(agg, tag)\n\n  def parse_seeds(s: str):\n      return [int(x) for x in s.split(\",\") if x.strip()]\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n      p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      p.add_argument(\"--seeds\", type=str, default=\"123,456,789\")\n      p.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=250)\n      p.add_argument(\"--lam\", type=float, default=1e-3)\n      p.add_argument(\"--tag\", type=str, default=\"template_batch\")\n      args = p.parse_args(argv)\n      seeds = parse_seeds(args.seeds)\n\
    \      lp, sp, rid, agg = run_batch(seeds=seeds, n=args.n, lam=args.lam, tag=args.tag)\n      print(\"BATCH_OK\")\n      print(\"lineage_file:\", lp)\n      print(\"shared_file:\", sp)\n      print(\"run_id:\", rid)\n      print(\"runs:\", agg[\"runs\"])\n      print(\"resid_mean:\", agg[\"resid_mean\"])\n      print(\"elapsed_mean:\", agg[\"elapsed_mean\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read kairos/experiments/ridge_batch.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Batch Ridge Solve (Multi-seed)\"\ntags: \"baseline, template, numpy, aggregation, storage\"\nabstract: \"Runs ridge solve over multiple seeds, aggregates metrics, writes lineage/shared artifacts, and prints summary.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  import experiments.ridge_batch as rb\n\n  def main():\n      seeds = [111, 222, 333, 444, 555]\n      lp, sp, rid, agg = rb.run_batch(seeds=seeds, n=300, lam=1e-3, tag=\"template_batch\"\
    )\n      print(\"BATCH_OK\")\n      print(\"lineage_file:\", lp)\n      print(\"shared_file:\", sp)\n      print(\"run_id:\", rid)\n      print(\"runs:\", agg[\"runs\"])\n      print(\"resid_mean:\", agg[\"resid_mean\"])\n      print(\"elapsed_mean:\", agg[\"elapsed_mean\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 242-243: Implemented batch ridge experiment and submitted multi-seed run.\n  - Added: kairos/experiments/ridge_batch.py (multi-seed aggregation, CLI + function).\n  - Submission: \"Batch Ridge Solve (Multi-seed)\" queued with seeds [111,222,333,444,555], n=300, lam=1e-3, tag=template_batch.\n  - Expected artifacts:\n    - storage/kairos/template_batch_last_run.json\n    - storage/shared/agents/kairos/template_batch_marker.txt\n  - Next: Review evaluation, verify artifacts, then expose args via CLI for flexible re-use in future runs.\n```"
