    marker: bdaa4a7f\ntotal_entries: 2\nTABLE: tag | run_id | resid | elapsed | runs\ntemplate | 0aabe22c | 0.3152511200894618 | 0.002422809600830078 | 1\ntemplate_batch | 8d06a767 | 0.5471991972996129 | 0.002027082443237305 | 5\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write kairos/tools/aggregate.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage read kairos/tools/aggregate.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: kairos/tools/aggregate.py\n- File content for kairos/tools/aggregate.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Aggregate Last\
    \ Runs Summary' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 622.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 622 | 1 | Aggregate Last Runs Summary | Kairos I | 245 |\n| 616 | 1 | Batch Ridge Solve (Multi-seed) | Kairos I | 243 |\n| 611 | 1 | Experiment Template Smoke Test (Ridge Solve) | Kairos I | 241 |\n| 606 | 1 | Storage Sanity + Utility Import | Kairos I | 239 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**kairos/tools/aggregate.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAggregate *_last_run.json results under storage/kairos and write a summary.\nProduces:\n  - storage/kairos/summary_last.json\n  - storage/shared/agents/kairos/summary_marker.txt\nPrints a concise table.\n\
    \"\"\"\nimport os, sys, json\n\nsys.path.append('storage/kairos')\nfrom utils.io import read_json, write_json, write_text\nfrom utils.text import short_hash\n\ndef normalize_entry(path: str, record: dict) -> dict:\n    tag = record.get(\"tag\") or os.path.basename(path).replace(\"_last_run.json\", \"\")\n    run_id = record.get(\"run_id\")\n    resid = record.get(\"resid_mean\", record.get(\"resid\"))\n    elapsed = record.get(\"elapsed_mean\", record.get(\"elapsed\"))\n    runs = record.get(\"runs\", 1 if record.get(\"per_run\") is None else len(record.get(\"per_run\")))\n    return {\n        \"file\": path,\n        \"tag\": tag,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"resid\": float(resid) if resid is not None else None,\n        \"elapsed\": float(elapsed) if elapsed is not None else None,\n        \"runs\": int(runs) if runs is not None else None,\n    }\n\ndef main():\n    base = \"storage/kairos\"\n    files = []\n    try:\n        files = [os.path.join(base, f) for f in os.listdir(base)\
    \ if f.endswith(\"_last_run.json\")]\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        files = []\n\n    entries = []\n    for fp in sorted(files):\n        rec = read_json(fp, default=None)\n        if rec is None:\n            continue\n        entries.append(normalize_entry(fp, rec))\n\n    # Compute simple best/fastest\n    best = min((e for e in entries if e[\"resid\"] is not None), key=lambda x: x[\"resid\"], default=None)\n    fastest = min((e for e in entries if e[\"elapsed\"] is not None), key=lambda x: x[\"elapsed\"], default=None)\n\n    summary = {\n        \"total\": len(entries),\n        \"best_by_resid\": best,\n        \"fastest_by_elapsed\": fastest,\n        \"entries\": entries,\n    }\n\n    # Persist summary (lineage + shared marker)\n    summary_path = \"storage/kairos/summary_last.json\"\n    write_json(summary_path, summary)\n    marker = short_hash(json.dumps(summary, sort_keys=True))\n    write_text(\"storage/shared/agents/kairos/summary_marker.txt\", marker + \"\\n\"\
    )\n\n    # Print concise table\n    print(\"AGG_OK\")\n    print(\"summary_file:\", summary_path)\n    print(\"marker:\", marker)\n    print(\"total_entries:\", len(entries))\n    print(\"TABLE: tag | run_id | resid | elapsed | runs\")\n    for e in sorted(entries, key=lambda x: (x[\"resid\"] if x[\"resid\"] is not None else float(\"inf\"))):\n        print(f\"{e['tag']} | {e.get('run_id','')} | {e.get('resid')} | {e.get('elapsed')} | {e.get('runs')}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Kairos_private_2-7.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Kairos Lineage Changelog | Kairos I | Tick 238 | 476 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Kairos I Index | Kairos\
    \ I | Tick 238 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
