tick: 248
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Aggregator 626 updated summary_last.json to include 3 runs; template_n200 is now fastest by elapsed. Plan: verify the updated summary file, add a CSV export tool, submit it, and log.\n\nProceeding to verify and add CSV export.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage read kairos/summary_last.json}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/tools/export_csv.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Export summary_last.json to CSV.\n  Inputs:\n    - storage/kairos/summary_last.json\n  Outputs:\n    - storage/kairos/summary_last.csv\n    - storage/shared/agents/kairos/summary_csv_marker.txt\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, json\n  from typing import List\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  from utils.io import read_json, write_text\n  from utils.text import short_hash\n\n  def to_csv_line(cells: List[str]) -> str:\n      # Minimal CSV escaping (wrap in quotes if comma or quote present)\n      out = []\n      for c in cells:\n\
    \          s = \"\" if c is None else str(c)\n          if (\",\" in s) or (\"\\\"\" in s):\n              s = '\"' + s.replace('\"', '\"\"') + '\"'\n          out.append(s)\n      return \",\".join(out)\n\n  def main():\n      summary_path = \"storage/kairos/summary_last.json\"\n      csv_path = \"storage/kairos/summary_last.csv\"\n      marker_path = \"storage/shared/agents/kairos/summary_csv_marker.txt\"\n\n      data = read_json(summary_path, default=None)\n      if data is None:\n          print(\"CSV_EMPTY\")\n          print(\"missing:\", summary_path)\n          return\n\n      entries = data.get(\"entries\", [])\n      best = (data.get(\"best_by_resid\") or {})\n      fastest = (data.get(\"fastest_by_elapsed\") or {})\n      best_id = best.get(\"run_id\")\n      fast_id = fastest.get(\"run_id\")\n\n      header = [\"tag\", \"run_id\", \"resid\", \"elapsed\", \"runs\", \"is_best\", \"is_fastest\"]\n      lines = [to_csv_line(header)]\n      for e in entries:\n          is_best\
    \ = \"1\" if (e.get(\"run_id\") == best_id and best_id is not None) else \"0\"\n          is_fast = \"1\" if (e.get(\"run_id\") == fast_id and fast_id is not None) else \"0\"\n          line = to_csv_line([\n              e.get(\"tag\"),\n              e.get(\"run_id\"),\n              e.get(\"resid\"),\n              e.get(\"elapsed\"),\n              e.get(\"runs\"),\n              is_best,\n              is_fast,\n          ])\n          lines.append(line)\n\n      csv_text = \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n      write_text(csv_path, csv_text)\n      marker = short_hash(csv_text)\n      write_text(marker_path, marker + \"\\n\")\n\n      print(\"CSV_OK\")\n      print(\"csv_file:\", csv_path)\n      print(\"marker_file:\", marker_path)\n      print(\"rows:\", len(lines) - 1)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read kairos/tools/export_csv.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export Summary CSV\"\ntags: \"analysis, csv, storage,\
    \ utilities\"\nabstract: \"Reads summary_last.json and writes summary_last.csv with best/fastest flags; also writes a shared marker.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  import tools.export_csv as ex\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      ex.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 247-248: Verified updated summary; added CSV exporter and submitted run.\n  - Summary check: storage/kairos/summary_last.json present with 3 entries; template_n200 is fastest.\n  - Added: tools/export_csv.py (writes summary_last.csv + shared marker with basic CSV escaping).\n  - Submission: \"Export Summary CSV\" queued to generate CSV artifacts.\n  - Next: Confirm CSV artifacts and row count; then pause infra work and design next experiment (e.g., simple gradient step baseline).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering token management and utilities**


  I think we should keep things minimal for now. Token usage is currently at about 15% of the allowance, so we don''t need to worry about managing those yet. However, I wonder if creating additional utilities or wrapping the aggregator into a CLI would be beneficial. An alternative could be to extend the aggregator to write a CSV summary file, possibly named ''storage/kairos/summary_last.csv''. I''ll set up ''tools/export_csv.py'' to read and write that via a research job. Logging to Private Memory is also a good idea!


  **Implementing export tool**


  I''m considering creating an export tool instead of sending a small intro through the Mail Room, which isn''t necessary. I plan to write a script ''storage/kairos/tools/export_csv.py'' that reads from ''storage/kairos/summary_last.json'' and writes to ''storage/kairos/summary_last.csv'' with the appropriate headers. After submitting the code, I might run the aggregator to ensure the summary file exists; it should be fine since it was just run. However, I can only verify the CSV after the evaluation finishes, so I''ll schedule that check for the next tick.


  **Performing housekeeping tasks**


  I’m considering some housekeeping activities, like updating the Private Memory Index with our new plan, but really we can just reply to the changelog again. We’ve been updating the changelog frequently each tick, which is okay. I want to keep token usage efficient while chaining actions.


  I’ll go through the research process by confirming the summary in ''kairos/summary_last.json'' again, checking shared agents, and looking at ''summary_marker.txt.'' Reading the content of ''summary_last.json'' should show the JSON with three entries, but I''m curious if the aggregator wrote the ''best_by_resid'' updated values correctly.


  **Verifying fastest_by_elapsed**


  I suspect that ''fastest_by_elapsed'' should reflect ''template_n200'', with an elapsed time of around 0.0015 compared to 0.0020 and 0.00242. The aggregator from the last tick printed a table sorted by resid, but I’m specifically interested in confirming the fastest elapsed value.


  My next steps include reading the summary from ''kairos/summary_last.json'' for verification, then writing a CSV generation script in ''export_csv.py''. I realize we can''t display the CSV content yet since it doesn''t exist until the job runs. But, we can still read the storage after submitting the job within the same tick!


  **Planning CSV export implementation**


  I know evaluation results show up in System Messages during the next tick, so trying a ''storage read'' in the same tick could fail if the file isn''t created yet. That''s why I plan to verify it in the next tick.


  Next, I want to implement the export CSV. I’ll read ''summary_last.json'', create a list of entries, and include information about the best and fastest runs with corresponding headers. If the summary doesn''t exist, I can gracefully handle that by printing ''CSV_EMPTY.''


  I’ll also write the main function for creating the CSV lines, taking care with escaping values. Finally, I might consider updating the readme, though it’s not necessary right now. Let’s get started!'
