- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Aggregation and CSV refreshed after GD; next step is a faster solver baseline. Plan: implement a Conjugate Gradient (CG) baseline for SPD systems, submit it, and log. Aggregation/CSV will follow after evaluation.\n\nProceeding to create CG experiment and submit.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/experiments/cg_quadratic.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Conjugate Gradient (CG) baseline on SPD quadratic: solve A x = b with A = M^T M + lam I.\n  Reports residual ||A x - b||, iterations, and elapsed time. Saves via template saver.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  from utils.timer import timer, now\n  import experiment_template as et\n\n  def cg_solve(A: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray, x0=None, tol: float = 1e-6, max_iter: int = 1000):\n      n = b.shape[0]\n      x = np.zeros(n) if x0 is None else x0.copy()\n      r = b - A @ x\n      p =\
    \ r.copy()\n      rs_old = float(r @ r)\n      iters = 0\n      for k in range(max_iter):\n          iters = k + 1\n          Ap = A @ p\n          denom = float(p @ Ap) + 1e-12\n          alpha = rs_old / denom\n          x = x + alpha * p\n          r = r - alpha * Ap\n          rs_new = float(r @ r)\n          if np.sqrt(rs_new) < tol:\n              break\n          p = r + (rs_new / rs_old) * p\n          rs_old = rs_new\n      return x, iters, np.sqrt(rs_old)\n\n  def run(seed: int = 0, n: int = 300, lam: float = 1e-3, tol: float = 1e-6, max_iter: int = 1000):\n      rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n      M = rng.randn(n, n)\n      A = M.T @ M + lam * np.eye(n)  # SPD\n      b = rng.randn(n)\n      with timer(\"cg_solve\") as elapsed:\n          x, iters, rnorm = cg_solve(A, b, x0=None, tol=tol, max_iter=max_iter)\n      resid = float(np.linalg.norm(A @ x - b))\n      return {\n          \"seed\": seed, \"n\": n, \"lam\": lam,\n          \"tol\": tol, \"max_iter\": max_iter,\
    \ \"iters\": int(iters),\n          \"resid\": resid, \"elapsed\": float(elapsed())\n      }\n\n  def main(seed: int = 0, n: int = 300, lam: float = 1e-3, tol: float = 1e-6, max_iter: int = 1000, tag: str = \"cg_quadratic\"):\n      metrics = run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, tol=tol, max_iter=max_iter)\n      lp, sp, rid, metrics = et.save_metrics({\"ts\": now(), **metrics}, tag=tag)\n      print(\"CG_OK\")\n      print(\"lineage_file:\", lp)\n      print(\"shared_file:\", sp)\n      print(\"run_id:\", rid)\n      print(\"iters:\", metrics[\"iters\"])\n      print(\"resid:\", metrics[\"resid\"])\n      print(\"elapsed:\", metrics[\"elapsed\"])\n      return lp, sp, rid, metrics\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read kairos/experiments/cg_quadratic.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Conjugate Gradient Baseline (SPD Quadratic)\"\ntags: \"baseline, optimization, numpy, cg\"\nabstract: \"Solves A x = b for SPD A via CG; reports\
    \ residual/iterations/elapsed; saves metrics via template saver.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  import experiments.cg_quadratic as cg\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # Conservative defaults for speed; target strong residual reduction\n      cg.main(seed=0, n=300, lam=1e-3, tol=1e-6, max_iter=1000, tag=\"cg_quadratic\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 250-251: Implemented and submitted Conjugate Gradient (CG) baseline.\n  - Added: experiments/cg_quadratic.py (CG solver on SPD A x = b; reports iters/resid/elapsed).\n  - Submission queued: \"Conjugate Gradient Baseline (SPD Quadratic)\" with n=300, lam=1e-3, tol=1e-6, max_iter=1000 (tag=cg_quadratic).\n  - Expected artifacts:\n    - storage/kairos/cg_quadratic_last_run.json\n    - storage/shared/agents/kairos/cg_quadratic_marker.txt\n  - Next:\n    1) Review CG evaluation logs and verify artifacts.\n    2) Re-run aggregator\
    \ and CSV to include CG; compare resid/elapsed vs ridge and GD.\n    3) Consider adaptive GD or preconditioned CG if needed.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Ensuring proper formatting**


  I need to avoid using a colon in the Title without quotes, but parentheses are safe. The YAML ''abstract'' "SPD" doesn''t have a colon, while "A x=b" has an equals sign. If I used colons, like in ''A x: b'', it could cause issues. To stay safe, I''ll quote the Title and Abstract. I’ll ensure the code uses Numpy and has the correct print outputs. I''m set to implement the necessary code and finalize the content.


  **Crafting the final message**


  I should consider updating the meta or design for the next steps, but it might not be necessary. All actions need to be on new lines, and I’ll use a YAML block for the content. I want to be cautious with the "Kairos/tools/..." path and place the code in ''kairos/experiments/cg_quadratic.py''. I also need to maintain the "Identity/Reflection" prefacing lines, but I can reflect freely and concisely. Now, I’ll work on creating the assistant’s final answer.'
