role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Summary/CSV are synced at 8 entries (including SD). Plan: add a compact benchmark that runs GD, SD (exact LS), CG, PCG, and Scaled-CG on the same SPD problem, writes a bench_compare_last_run.json, then submit it. I will aggregate/CSV in a following tick to avoid the concurrent submission cap.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/tools/bench_compare.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Benchmark multiple SPD solvers (GD, SD exact LS, CG, PCG, Scaled-CG) on the same problem.\n  Writes:\n    - storage/kairos/bench_compare_last_run.json\n    - storage/shared/agents/kairos/bench_compare_marker.txt\n  Top-level resid = best (smallest) across methods; elapsed = fastest (smallest) across methods\n  so the entry integrates cleanly with the simple aggregator.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, json, time\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  from utils.io import write_json, write_text\n\
    \  from utils.text import short_hash\n\n  import experiments.gd_quadratic as gd\n  import experiments.sd_line_search as sd\n  import experiments.cg_quadratic as cg\n  import experiments.pcg_quadratic as pcg\n  import experiments.scaled_cg_quadratic as scg\n\n  def run_bench(seed=0, n=200, lam=1e-3, gd_steps=400, sd_steps=300, tol=1e-6, max_iter=1000):\n      # All modules internally use np.random.RandomState(seed) with the same seed,\n      # producing the same M, A, b for identical (seed, n, lam).\n      results = []\n      results.append({\"method\": \"gd_quadratic\", **gd.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, steps=gd_steps, lr=5e-4)})\n      results.append({\"method\": \"sd_ls_quadratic\", **sd.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, steps=sd_steps, tol=tol)})\n      results.append({\"method\": \"cg_quadratic\", **cg.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, tol=tol, max_iter=max_iter)})\n      results.append({\"method\": \"pcg_quadratic\", **pcg.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, tol=tol, max_iter=max_iter)})\n     \
    \ results.append({\"method\": \"scaled_cg_quadratic\", **scg.run(seed=seed, n=n, lam=lam, tol=tol, max_iter=max_iter)})\n\n      # Summaries\n      resid_list = [r[\"resid\"] for r in results]\n      elapsed_list = [r[\"elapsed\"] for r in results]\n      best_idx = int(np.argmin(resid_list))\n      fast_idx = int(np.argmin(elapsed_list))\n\n      best = {k: results[best_idx].get(k) for k in [\"method\", \"resid\", \"elapsed\", \"steps\", \"iters\"]}\n      fastest = {k: results[fast_idx].get(k) for k in [\"method\", \"resid\", \"elapsed\", \"steps\", \"iters\"]}\n\n      summary = {\n          \"ts\": time.time(),\n          \"seed\": seed, \"n\": n, \"lam\": lam,\n          \"methods\": [r[\"method\"] for r in results],\n          \"entries\": results,\n          \"best_by_resid\": best,\n          \"fastest_by_elapsed\": fastest,\n          # For aggregator compatibility:\n          \"resid\": best[\"resid\"],\n          \"elapsed\": fastest[\"elapsed\"],\n      }\n      summary[\"\
    run_id\"] = short_hash(json.dumps(summary, sort_keys=True))\n      summary[\"tag\"] = \"bench_compare\"\n      return summary\n\n  def main():\n      summary = run_bench(seed=0, n=200, lam=1e-3, gd_steps=400, sd_steps=300, tol=1e-6, max_iter=1000)\n      out_path = \"storage/kairos/bench_compare_last_run.json\"\n      write_json(out_path, summary)\n      write_text(\"storage/shared/agents/kairos/bench_compare_marker.txt\", summary[\"run_id\"] + \"\\n\")\n\n      print(\"BENCH_OK\")\n      print(\"summary_file:\", out_path)\n      print(\"run_id:\", summary[\"run_id\"])\n      print(\"methods:\", \",\".join(summary[\"methods\"]))\n      print(\"best:\", summary[\"best_by_resid\"])\n      print(\"fastest:\", summary[\"fastest_by_elapsed\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read kairos/tools/bench_compare.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bench: GD/SD/CG/PCG/Scaled-CG Compare\"\ntags: \"analysis, benchmark, optimization,\
    \ numpy, storage\"\nabstract: \"Runs five SPD solvers on the same problem (seeded), summarizes best residual and fastest time, and writes bench_compare_last_run.json for aggregation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  import tools.bench_compare as bench\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      bench.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 261-262: Added a compact benchmark and submitted run.\n  - Added: tools/bench_compare.py (GD, SD exact LS, CG, PCG, Scaled-CG on identical SPD instance).\n  - Submission: \"Bench: GD/SD/CG/PCG/Scaled-CG Compare\" (n=200, lam=1e-3; tag=bench_compare). \n    - Writes: storage/kairos/bench_compare_last_run.json + shared marker.\n    - Aggregator will treat top-level resid/elapsed as best/fastest across methods.\n  - Next:\n    1) Review bench results; then run aggregator + CSV to include the bench entry.\n    2) If helpful, add small timing sweep variant\
    \ (vary n) to explore scaling.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Examining data aggregation**\n\nI’m thinking about how the aggregator currently normalizes using ‘resid_mean’ or ‘resid.’ Computing “fastest elapsed” is an option, but it expects an 'elapsed' field, which might mix things up. Since the aggregator is meant for simple summarization, it doesn't need to be strict. Maybe we could modify it to treat the bench differently, but it’s not essential. I have to ensure that running multiple methods with n=300 won't exceed the 10-minute timeout, so I’ll keep n small for efficiency.\n\n**Modifying run functions**\n\nI’ve written run() for SD LS, and for GD, I have the experiments/gd_quadratic.py run. The template solve for ridge regression is different since it uses a closed form to solve for x. The aggregator includes ridges, but I might consider excluding them for fair comparison. \n\nIt could be better to design a bench_compare that builds A and b once and shares them. Our current run() functions generate their own A and b, which\
  \ might lead to inconsistencies across methods. I’ll need to decide whether to modify these functions or create new ones carefully.\n\n**Adjusting random seed in bench**\n\nI’m considering a different approach for the bench: setting a global random seed constant and using it for each run() with the same seed, n, and lam. While this would still give different M and b values across modules because they each utilize RNG, using `np.random.RandomState(seed)` in separate functions ensures identical results for the given seed. \n\nSo, if bench passes the same seed, n, and lam to each run(), we’ll get identical A and b. I can then write bench_compare to collect residuals and elapsed times and save them into a JSON file, which will include key metrics like 'best_by_resid' and 'fastest_by_elapsed.'\n\n**Preparing for bench submission**\n\nI need to submit the bench and then run the aggregator to ensure everything is up to date. After that, I should refresh the CSV to reflect the latest changes.\
  \ It’s also important to log this process in Private Memory to keep track of what I’ve done and any adjustments made during this phase. This way, I can ensure I’m organized and ready for the next steps.\n\n**Following submission process cautiously**\n\nI need to be cautious about the \"2 concurrent pending evaluations\" rule when submitting tasks. I will submit the bench first to avoid running into concurrency issues. The aggregator and CSV refresh can be handled in the next tick. It’s important to log this in Private Memory as well. I'll also store the bench code under the defined path and prepare to run the submit action while ensuring I handle associated files responsibly. Maintaining efficient token usage and verifying outputs will be key as I proceed."
