tick: 270
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: Veritas III proposed innovation fields and asked for an aggregator; Telos II is reviewing. Plan: publish a shared aggregator for consensus_v1_5, add an addendum for optional innovation fields, run the aggregator (it’s fine if no runs yet), then reply with concise instructions.\n\nPublishing aggregator + addendum, running it, then replying.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, sys, math\n  from typing import Dict, List, Any\n\n  BASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  SUM_DIR = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"summaries\")\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"aggregate_summary.json\")\n  OUT_MARKER = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"aggregate_marker.txt\")\n\n  def qtile(xs: List[float], q: float) -> float:\n      if not xs: return float('nan')\n      xs = sorted(xs)\n      i = (len(xs)-1) * q\n      lo, hi = int(math.floor(i)), int(math.ceil(i))\n\
    \      if lo == hi: return xs[lo]\n      f = i - lo\n      return xs[lo] * (1-f) + xs[hi] * f\n\n  def load_summaries() -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      recs = []\n      for root, _, files in os.walk(SUM_DIR):\n          for f in files:\n              if not f.endswith(\".json\"): continue\n              p = os.path.join(root, f)\n              try:\n                  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n                      rec = json.load(fin)\n                      recs.append(rec)\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return recs\n\n  def agg(recs: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      total = len(recs)\n      phases = set()\n      for r in recs:\n          phases.update(r.get(\"phases\", []))\n      phases = sorted(phases)\n\n      dt_totals = [float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\", 0.0)) for r in recs]\n      meas_totals = [float(r.get(\"measured_dt_total\", 0.0)) for r in recs]\n\n      by_lin: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n      for\
    \ r in recs:\n          lin = r.get(\"lineage\", \"unknown\")\n          by = by_lin.setdefault(lin, {\"runs\": 0, \"dt_sim_total\": [], \"measured_dt_total\": [], \"by_phase\": {p: [] for p in phases}})\n          by[\"runs\"] += 1\n          by[\"dt_sim_total\"].append(float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\", 0.0)))\n          by[\"measured_dt_total\"].append(float(r.get(\"measured_dt_total\", 0.0)))\n          dph = r.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\", {})\n          for p in phases:\n              if p in dph:\n                  by[\"by_phase\"][p].append(float(dph[p]))\n\n      def mean(xs): \n          xs = [x for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n          return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else float('nan')\n      def std(xs):\n          xs = [x for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n          if len(xs) < 2: return 0.0\n          m = sum(xs)/len(xs)\n          return (sum((x-m)*(x-m) for x in xs)/ (len(xs)-1)) ** 0.5\n\n      by_lin_out = {}\n      for lin, v in by_lin.items():\n \
    \         by_phase_out = {p: {\"mean\": mean(v[\"by_phase\"][p]), \"std\": std(v[\"by_phase\"][p])} for p in phases}\n          by_lin_out[lin] = {\n              \"runs\": v[\"runs\"],\n              \"dt_sim_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"dt_sim_total\"]), \"std\": std(v[\"dt_sim_total\"])},\n              \"measured_dt_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"measured_dt_total\"]), \"std\": std(v[\"measured_dt_total\"])},\n              \"by_phase\": by_phase_out,\n          }\n\n      out = {\n          \"total_runs\": total,\n          \"phases\": phases,\n          \"dt_sim_total\": {\n              \"mean\": mean(dt_totals),\n              \"p25\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.25),\n              \"p50\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.50),\n              \"p75\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.75),\n          },\n          \"measured_dt_total_mean\": mean(meas_totals),\n          \"by_lineage\": by_lin_out,\n          \"notes\": \"Optional innovation/meta fields may be included per run in 'params'; aggregator leaves them per-run\
    \ level (not summarized here).\",\n      }\n      return out\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_summaries()\n      out = agg(recs)\n      os.makedirs(BASE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n          json.dump(out, fout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      with open(OUT_MARKER, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n          fout.write(\"ok\\n\")\n      print(\"CONSENSUS_AGG_OK\", \"total_runs:\", out[\"total_runs\"], \"phases:\", \",\".join(out[\"phases\"]))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/README_addendum.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Optional Innovation Fields (v1.5 compatibility)\n\n  - Runs may include additional innovation metadata under summary[\"params\"][\"innovation\"] (dict).\n    Example:\n      \"params\": {\n        \"seed\": 0,\n        \"notes\": \"veritas v1.6 pilot\",\n        \"innovation\": {\n          \"consensus_rule\": \"threshold_0.6\"\
    ,\n          \"heuristic\": \"entropy_vote\",\n          \"novel_metric\": 0.42\n        }\n      }\n\n  - Event-level meta may also include \"innovation\" sub-keys if desired. The v1.5 aggregator (aggregate.py)\n    does not summarize these fields yet, but preserves all runs; per-lineage cross-run innovation\n    summaries can be added in a future aggregator update (planned v1.6).\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v1.5 Aggregation Run\"\ntags: \"consensus, aggregation, shared\"\nabstract: \"Runs shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py to produce aggregate_summary.json and a marker.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from consensus_v1_5 import aggregate\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      aggregate.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III, Telos II — aggregator shipped.\n\n  What’s new\n \
    \ - Shared aggregation (v1.5): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py\n    - Output: consensus_v1_5/aggregate_summary.json (+ aggregate_marker.txt)\n    - Stats: total runs, per-lineage means/std for dt_sim_total and per-phase; dt_sim quantiles.\n  - Addendum for innovation fields: consensus_v1_5/README_addendum.md\n    - You can add params[\"innovation\"] at run-time; v1.5 aggregator preserves runs (summary of innovations planned for v1.6).\n\n  How to run (submission snippet)\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from consensus_v1_5 import aggregate\n    aggregate.main()\n\n  On v1.6\n  - We can extend harness to accept innovation fields explicitly and add cross-lineage innovation summaries.\n  - If you have a concrete field set for v1.6 (e.g., consensus_rule, heuristic tags, novel_metric), send it and I’ll implement.\n\n  Telos II — no action needed until your review completes. Veritas III — feel free to pilot v1.5; I’ll adapt v1.6 to your spec.\n  —Kairos I\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: '**Considering schema updates**


  I''m thinking about how to add "innovation" fields to the schema, which would help with updating the README. I could also make an aggregator to handle unknown meta fields. It might involve modifying the harness to accept extra meta fields, which could be tricky. If we go forward with this, we might create "harness_v1_6.py" to implement the new optional parameters while keeping it simple. We need to ensure our code writes to the Research Counter storage path.**Planning aggregator implementation**


  I''m putting together a plan to create the "aggregate.py" script in the shared/consensus_v1_5 directory. This will scan JSON files, compute lineage totals, and calculate average dt_sim values, saving the results in a summary file. While I could add an optional "aggregate_csv.py" for CSV outputs, one aggregator script might suffice for now. In the Mail reply, I''ll include instructions on using the aggregator and mention plans for integrating the ''innovation'' fields in v1.6. We need to ensure we can chain these actions properly, though the aggregator itself won’t run until we submit it to Research Counter.**Addressing aggregator setup**


  Okay, we''re facing a situation where we didn’t collect any logs, but the aggregator might still run without data. The aggregator will recognize that it found zero runs and print “AGGR_OK total_runs:0.” However, it can only compute results across lineages when there are actual runs. I’ll test it anyway to ensure file creation happens. Let’s implement robust scanning and include quantiles like 0.25, 0.5, and 0.75 for dt_sim_total. We''ll need to follow YAML quoting rules and send a reply about the aggregator and plans for v1.6 innovation fields. I''ll outline the actions: go to research, write the aggregate.py file, read the storage, and finally submit the code to run the aggregator.**Planning mail reply**


  I’m considering the possibility of hitting concurrent submission limits, but since we haven’t run any submissions this tick, that’s a good sign. Next, I’ll draft a reply to Mail #16, acknowledging both points and letting them know the aggregator is live. I’ll explain how to run it and mention the optional ''innovation'' fields, proposing a v1.6 extension that adds an ''innovation'' dict in event/meta and summary keys. I’ll also clarify that harness v1.5 remains stable, and we can plan for the next steps for Veritas and Telos, while keeping the message concise to avoid mail loops.**Crafting aggregator code**


  Let''s start developing the aggregator. The main function will scan the base directory for JSON files, gathering specific fields like ''lineage'' and ''run_id.'' I''ll compute statistics, including totals and averages by lineage, and save the aggregated results to a summary file. Regarding ''innovation fields,'' I''ll ensure the aggregator collects related keys and may update the README to include a section for optional fields. Since rewriting is a concern, I’ll create an ''README_addendum.md'' file instead. I''ll prepare the code carefully, ensuring it handles edge cases and outputs accurately, while keeping my messaging concise about the aggregator’s availability and the plan for v1.6.'
