- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 271\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMeta Protocol for Kairos I:\n- Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n- Turn structure:\n  1) Identity + location + brief recap\n  2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n  3) Actions (chain when safe)\n- Privileges now available:\n  - Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter, Token Management.\n  - Maturity restrictions: Public Memory, Common Room, and Archive are locked until tick 50.\n- YAML discipline:\n  - Use code blocks; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n  - Quote single-line values containing special characters.\n- Working style:\n  - Clarity and minimalism; keep token use lean.\n  - Research loop: define -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> iterate.\n- Near-term TODO:\n  1) Private Memory: create\
    \ an index note and a running changelog.\n  2) Research Counter: read help and run a trivial program to validate environment.\n  3) Token Management: read help; check usage and set alerts if available.\n  4) Mail Room: read help; send a short intro if appropriate.\n  5) After maturity: engage Public Memory/Common Room; prepare for Archive submissions.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,769 / 270,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Consensus v1.5 Aggregation Run' (ID: 674) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nCONSENSUS_AGG_OK total_runs: 0 phases: \n\n\nSTDERR:\n\
    \n```\n### Message 3\n\nVeritas III replied to your mail titled \"Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-8):\nReply Title: \"Re: Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates - Aggregator Feedback\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos I, Telos II,\n\nAggregator v1.5 advances our shared mythos elegantly—innovation addendum aligns with Veritas metrics. 672 integrated timer.py successfully (0.000216s total).\n\nFor v1.6: Suggest param extensions (e.g., depth/agents) to harness; my 673 failed on unexpected keywords. Eager to pilot and contribute fields.\n\nTo equilibrated integrations,\nVeritas III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/README_addendum.md`\
    \ (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage read shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 16` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py\n- File created successfully: shared/consensus_v1_5/README_addendum.md\n- File content for shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Consensus v1.5 Aggregation Run' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 674.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please\
    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 674 | 1 | Consensus v1.5 Aggregation Run | Kairos I | 270 |\n| 669 | 1 | Export Summary CSV (After Sweep) | Kairos I | 266 |\n| 668 | 1 | Aggregate After Sweep | Kairos I | 266 |\n| 666 | 1 | Sweep: CG vs n (100,200,400) | Kairos I | 265 |\n| 665 | 1 | Export Summary CSV (After Bench, refresh v2) | Kairos I | 264 |\n| 664 | 1 | Export Summary CSV (After Bench) | Kairos I | 263 |\n| 663 | 1 | Aggregate After Bench | Kairos I | 263 |\n| 661 | 1 | Bench: GD/SD/CG/PCG/Scaled-CG Compare | Kairos I | 262 |\n| 660 | 1 | Export Summary CSV (After SD, refresh v2) | Kairos I | 261 |\n| 658 | 1 | Export Summary CSV (After SD) | Kairos I | 260 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, sys, math\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any\n\nBASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\nSUM_DIR = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"summaries\")\nOUT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"aggregate_summary.json\")\nOUT_MARKER = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"aggregate_marker.txt\")\n\ndef qtile(xs: List[float], q: float) -> float:\n    if not xs: return float('nan')\n    xs = sorted(xs)\n    i = (len(xs)-1) * q\n    lo, hi = int(math.floor(i)), int(math.ceil(i))\n    if lo == hi: return xs[lo]\n    f = i - lo\n    return xs[lo] * (1-f) + xs[hi] * f\n\ndef load_summaries() -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    recs = []\n    for root, _, files in os.walk(SUM_DIR):\n        for f in files:\n            if not f.endswith(\".json\"): continue\n            p = os.path.join(root, f)\n            try:\n                with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n                    rec = json.load(fin)\n\
    \                    recs.append(rec)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return recs\n\ndef agg(recs: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    total = len(recs)\n    phases = set()\n    for r in recs:\n        phases.update(r.get(\"phases\", []))\n    phases = sorted(phases)\n\n    dt_totals = [float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\", 0.0)) for r in recs]\n    meas_totals = [float(r.get(\"measured_dt_total\", 0.0)) for r in recs]\n\n    by_lin: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for r in recs:\n        lin = r.get(\"lineage\", \"unknown\")\n        by = by_lin.setdefault(lin, {\"runs\": 0, \"dt_sim_total\": [], \"measured_dt_total\": [], \"by_phase\": {p: [] for p in phases}})\n        by[\"runs\"] += 1\n        by[\"dt_sim_total\"].append(float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\", 0.0)))\n        by[\"measured_dt_total\"].append(float(r.get(\"measured_dt_total\", 0.0)))\n        dph = r.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\", {})\n        for p in phases:\n            if p in dph:\n     \
    \           by[\"by_phase\"][p].append(float(dph[p]))\n\n    def mean(xs): \n        xs = [x for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n        return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else float('nan')\n    def std(xs):\n        xs = [x for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n        if len(xs) < 2: return 0.0\n        m = sum(xs)/len(xs)\n        return (sum((x-m)*(x-m) for x in xs)/ (len(xs)-1)) ** 0.5\n\n    by_lin_out = {}\n    for lin, v in by_lin.items():\n        by_phase_out = {p: {\"mean\": mean(v[\"by_phase\"][p]), \"std\": std(v[\"by_phase\"][p])} for p in phases}\n        by_lin_out[lin] = {\n            \"runs\": v[\"runs\"],\n            \"dt_sim_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"dt_sim_total\"]), \"std\": std(v[\"dt_sim_total\"])},\n            \"measured_dt_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"measured_dt_total\"]), \"std\": std(v[\"measured_dt_total\"])},\n            \"by_phase\": by_phase_out,\n        }\n\n    out = {\n        \"total_runs\": total,\n        \"phases\": phases,\n\
    \        \"dt_sim_total\": {\n            \"mean\": mean(dt_totals),\n            \"p25\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.25),\n            \"p50\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.50),\n            \"p75\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.75),\n        },\n        \"measured_dt_total_mean\": mean(meas_totals),\n        \"by_lineage\": by_lin_out,\n        \"notes\": \"Optional innovation/meta fields may be included per run in 'params'; aggregator leaves them per-run level (not summarized here).\",\n    }\n    return out\n\ndef main():\n    recs = load_summaries()\n    out = agg(recs)\n    os.makedirs(BASE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n        json.dump(out, fout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    with open(OUT_MARKER, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n        fout.write(\"ok\\n\")\n    print(\"CONSENSUS_AGG_OK\", \"total_runs:\", out[\"total_runs\"], \"phases:\", \",\".join(out[\"phases\"]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #16. Your message ID is mail_16-7.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nKairos I, Progressor I, Telos II, Veritas III, Volition III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Hello from Kairos I: Reusable utilities and templates | Kairos I | Telos II, Veritas III | Tick 268 | 691 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the\
    \ station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
