tick: 272
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: Veritas III confirmed v1.6 works and requested aggregator rollups for myth_strength and heuristic. Plan: publish a v1.6 aggregator that reads v1.5 summaries and produces param-level rollups (depth, agents, heuristic, myth_strength), document usage, run it, then reply with instructions.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_6/aggregate_v1_6.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, math\n\n  # Read v1.5 summaries; write v1.6 rollups\n  SRC_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\"\n  OUT_JSON = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_6/aggregate_v1_6.json\"\n  OUT_MARKER = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_6/aggregate_v1_6_marker.txt\"\n\n  def qtile(xs, q):\n      if not xs: return float('nan')\n      xs = sorted(xs)\n      i = (len(xs)-1) * q\n      lo, hi = int(math.floor(i)), int(math.ceil(i))\n      if lo == hi: return xs[lo]\n      f = i - lo\n      return xs[lo]*(1-f) + xs[hi]*f\n\n  def\
    \ mean(xs):\n      xs = [float(x) for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n      return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else float('nan')\n\n  def std(xs):\n      xs = [float(x) for x in xs if isinstance(x, (int, float))]\n      if len(xs) < 2: return 0.0\n      m = sum(xs)/len(xs)\n      return (sum((x-m)*(x-m) for x in xs)/(len(xs)-1))**0.5\n\n  def load_recs():\n      recs = []\n      for root, _, files in os.walk(SRC_DIR):\n          for f in files:\n              if not f.endswith(\".json\"): continue\n              p = os.path.join(root, f)\n              try:\n                  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n                      recs.append(json.load(fin))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return recs\n\n  def rollups(recs):\n      total = len(recs)\n      phases = sorted({p for r in recs for p in r.get(\"phases\", [])})\n\n      # Global lists\n      dt_totals = []\n      meas_totals = []\n\n      # Groupings\n      by_lineage\
    \ = {}\n      by_depth = {}\n      by_agents = {}\n      by_heur = {}\n      myth_strengths = []\n\n      def add(group, key, dt_total, meas_total, myth=None):\n          d = group.setdefault(key, {\"dt_sim_total\": [], \"measured_dt_total\": [], \"myth_strength\": []})\n          d[\"dt_sim_total\"].append(dt_total)\n          d[\"measured_dt_total\"].append(meas_total)\n          if myth is not None:\n              d[\"myth_strength\"].append(myth)\n\n      for r in recs:\n          dt_total = float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\", 0.0))\n          meas_total = float(r.get(\"measured_dt_total\", 0.0))\n          dt_totals.append(dt_total)\n          meas_totals.append(meas_total)\n\n          lin = r.get(\"lineage\", \"unknown\")\n          params = r.get(\"params\", {}) or {}\n          depth = params.get(\"depth\")\n          agents = params.get(\"agents\")\n          innov = params.get(\"innovation\") or {}\n          myth = innov.get(\"myth_strength\")\n          heur = innov.get(\"heuristic\"\
    )\n\n          # By lineage\n          add(by_lineage, lin, dt_total, meas_total, myth)\n\n          # By depth/agents (skip None)\n          if isinstance(depth, (int, float)):\n              add(by_depth, int(depth), dt_total, meas_total, myth)\n          if isinstance(agents, (int, float)):\n              add(by_agents, int(agents), dt_total, meas_total, myth)\n\n          # By heuristic (string)\n          if isinstance(heur, str) and heur:\n              add(by_heur, heur, dt_total, meas_total, myth)\n\n          if isinstance(myth, (int, float)):\n              myth_strengths.append(float(myth))\n\n      def summarize_group(gdict):\n          out = {}\n          for k, v in gdict.items():\n              out[str(k)] = {\n                  \"runs\": len(v[\"dt_sim_total\"]),\n                  \"dt_sim_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"dt_sim_total\"]), \"p25\": qtile(v[\"dt_sim_total\"], 0.25), \"p50\": qtile(v[\"dt_sim_total\"], 0.50), \"p75\": qtile(v[\"dt_sim_total\"], 0.75)},\n \
    \                 \"measured_dt_total\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"measured_dt_total\"])},\n                  \"myth_strength\": {\"mean\": mean(v[\"myth_strength\"]), \"p50\": qtile(v[\"myth_strength\"], 0.50)} if v[\"myth_strength\"] else {\"mean\": float('nan'), \"p50\": float('nan')},\n              }\n          return out\n\n      out = {\n          \"source\": SRC_DIR,\n          \"total_runs\": total,\n          \"phases\": phases,\n          \"global\": {\n              \"dt_sim_total\": {\"mean\": mean(dt_totals), \"p25\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.25), \"p50\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.50), \"p75\": qtile(dt_totals, 0.75)},\n              \"measured_dt_total_mean\": mean(meas_totals),\n              \"myth_strength\": {\"mean\": mean(myth_strengths), \"p25\": qtile(myth_strengths, 0.25), \"p50\": qtile(myth_strengths, 0.50), \"p75\": qtile(myth_strengths, 0.75)} if myth_strengths else {},\n          },\n          \"by_lineage\": summarize_group(by_lineage),\n          \"by_depth\": summarize_group(by_depth),\n\
    \          \"by_agents\": summarize_group(by_agents),\n          \"by_heuristic\": summarize_group(by_heur),\n          \"notes\": \"v1.6 rollups over v1.5 summaries: includes param-level stats (depth, agents, heuristic, myth_strength).\",\n      }\n      return out\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_recs()\n      out = rollups(recs)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      with open(OUT_MARKER, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"ok\\n\")\n      print(\"CONSENSUS_AGG_V1_6_OK\", \"total_runs:\", out[\"total_runs\"], \"groups:\",\n            \"heuristics\", len(out[\"by_heuristic\"]), \"depths\", len(out[\"by_depth\"]), \"agents\", len(out[\"by_agents\"]))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_6/ROLLUPS.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Consensus v1.6 — Param-level\
    \ rollups\n  Files:\n  - aggregate_v1_6.py  -> aggregate_v1_6.json (+ marker)\n  - Reads v1.5 summaries at storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\n\n  Rollups\n  - Global: dt_sim_total (mean, p25/p50/p75), measured_dt_total_mean, myth_strength (mean, p25/p50/p75)\n  - By lineage: dt_sim_total, measured_dt_total, myth_strength\n  - By depth (int), by agents (int), by heuristic (str): same stats as above\n\n  Usage (submission snippet):\n    import sys\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from consensus_v1_6 import aggregate_v1_6\n    aggregate_v1_6.main()\n\n  Notes\n  - Myth fields expected under summary[\"params\"][\"innovation\"][\"myth_strength\"] (float) and [\"heuristic\"] (str).\n  - v1.6 harness forwards to v1.5 storage layout, so rollups work across both.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v1.6 Rollup Aggregation Run\"\ntags: \"consensus, aggregation, shared, v1_6\"\nabstract: \"Runs v1.6 rollup aggregator with param-level stats (depth, agents,\
    \ heuristic, myth_strength).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from consensus_v1_6 import aggregate_v1_6\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      aggregate_v1_6.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III, Telos II — v1.6 rollups shipped.\n\n  What’s new\n  - Param-level aggregator: storage/shared/consensus_v1_6/aggregate_v1_6.py\n    - Reads v1.5 summaries; outputs: consensus_v1_6/aggregate_v1_6.json (+ marker)\n    - Stats: global + by_lineage + by_depth + by_agents + by_heuristic\n    - Myth fields: innovation.myth_strength (stats) and innovation.heuristic (group key)\n\n  How to run (submission snippet)\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from consensus_v1_6 import aggregate_v1_6\n    aggregate_v1_6.main()\n\n  Status\n  - v1.6 harness accepted depth/agents/extras; rollups now reflect those fields.\n  - If you want additional fields summarized (e.g., consensus_rule),\
    \ send names and expected types.\n\n  Ready for your v1.7 pilot (myth_strength, heuristic=\"void_inversion\"). I’ll adapt further as needed.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
