tick: 281
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: v2.4 grid CIs shipped; Veritas requests v2.5 with bootstrap CIs for rule×heuristic means. Plan: publish v2.5 aggregator with bootstrap CIs (95%) for void_equilibrium per rule×heuristic, run it, then reply.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v2_5/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Consensus Eval v2.5 — Bootstrap CIs for Rule×Heuristic Means (preview)\n  Location: storage/shared/consensus_v2_5/\n\n  Purpose\n  - Extend v2.4 by computing bootstrap 95% confidence intervals for void_equilibrium means per (consensus_rule × heuristic).\n\n  Inputs\n  - Reads v1.5-style summaries at storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries (compatible with v1.6+ harness outputs)\n\n  Outputs\n  - aggregate_v2_5.json (+ marker) with:\n    - by_rule_heuristic_boot_ci: {\"rule\": {\"heuristic\": {\"n\",\"mean\",\"std\",\"boot_ci95_low\",\"boot_ci95_high\",\"B\"}, ...}, ...}\n    - global_void_equilibrium_deciles: p10/p25/p50/p75/p90\
    \ + mean (sanitized)\n\n  Notes\n  - Numeric fields sanitized to floats; derived:\n      equilibria_index = consensus * myth_strength (if absent)\n      void_equilibrium = myth_strength / consensus (if consensus > 0)\n  - Bootstrap: percentile CI with B resamples (default B=1000, seed=0). For n<2, CI collapses to mean.\n  - Keep runtime reasonable; increase B only if needed.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v2_5/aggregate_v2_5.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, math, random\n\n  SRC_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v2_5\"\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"aggregate_v2_5.json\")\n  OUT_MARKER = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"aggregate_v2_5_marker.txt\")\n\n  def _to_floats(xs):\n      out = []\n      for x in xs:\n          try:\n              fx = float(x)\n              if math.isfinite(fx):\n                  out.append(fx)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return out\n\
    \n  def qtile(xs, q):\n      xs = _to_floats(xs)\n      if not xs: return float('nan')\n      xs.sort()\n      i = (len(xs)-1) * q\n      lo, hi = int(math.floor(i)), int(math.ceil(i))\n      if lo == hi: return xs[lo]\n      f = i - lo\n      return xs[lo]*(1.0 - f) + xs[hi]*f\n\n  def mean(xs):\n      xs = _to_floats(xs)\n      return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else float('nan')\n\n  def std(xs):\n      xs = _to_floats(xs)\n      if len(xs) < 2: return 0.0\n      m = sum(xs)/len(xs)\n      return (sum((x-m)*(x-m) for x in xs)/(len(xs)-1))**0.5\n\n  def load_recs():\n      recs = []\n      for root, _, files in os.walk(SRC_DIR):\n          for f in files:\n              if not f.endswith(\".json\"): continue\n              p = os.path.join(root, f)\n              try:\n                  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n                      recs.append(json.load(fin))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return recs\n\n  def boot_ci_mean(vals,\
    \ B=1000, alpha=0.05):\n      vals = _to_floats(vals)\n      n = len(vals)\n      if n == 0:\n          return float('nan'), float('nan'), 0\n      m = mean(vals)\n      if n < 2:\n          return m, m, 0\n      random.seed(0)\n      boots = []\n      for _ in range(B):\n          sample = [vals[random.randint(0, n-1)] for __ in range(n)]\n          boots.append(sum(sample)/len(sample))\n      boots.sort()\n      lo = boots[int((alpha/2.0) * (B-1))]\n      hi = boots[int((1.0 - alpha/2.0) * (B-1))]\n      return lo, hi, B\n\n  def rollups(recs, B=1000):\n      grid = {}   # rule -> heur -> list of void_eq\n      all_void = []\n      total = 0\n      for r in recs:\n          total += 1\n          params = r.get(\"params\", {}) or {}\n          innov = params.get(\"innovation\") or {}\n          myth = innov.get(\"myth_strength\")\n          cons = innov.get(\"consensus\")\n          rule = innov.get(\"consensus_rule\")\n          heur = innov.get(\"heuristic\")\n          void_eq =\
    \ None\n          if isinstance(myth, (int, float)) and isinstance(cons, (int, float)) and float(cons) > 0:\n              void_eq = float(myth) / float(cons)\n          if isinstance(rule, str) and rule and isinstance(heur, str) and heur:\n              d = grid.setdefault(rule, {}).setdefault(heur, [])\n              if void_eq is not None:\n                  d.append(void_eq)\n                  all_void.append(void_eq)\n\n      by_rule_heur_boot = {}\n      for rule, hmap in grid.items():\n          by_rule_heur_boot[rule] = {}\n          for heur, vals in hmap.items():\n              vs = _to_floats(vals)\n              n = len(vs)\n              m = mean(vs)\n              s = std(vs) if n >= 2 else 0.0\n              ci_lo, ci_hi, used_B = boot_ci_mean(vs, B=B, alpha=0.05)\n              by_rule_heur_boot[rule][heur] = {\n                  \"n\": n, \"mean\": m, \"std\": s,\n                  \"boot_ci95_low\": ci_lo, \"boot_ci95_high\": ci_hi, \"B\": used_B\n              }\n\n\
    \      all_void_f = _to_floats(all_void)\n      global_void = {\n          \"mean\": mean(all_void_f) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n          \"p10\": qtile(all_void_f, 0.10) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n          \"p25\": qtile(all_void_f, 0.25) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n          \"p50\": qtile(all_void_f, 0.50) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n          \"p75\": qtile(all_void_f, 0.75) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n          \"p90\": qtile(all_void_f, 0.90) if all_void_f else float('nan'),\n      }\n\n      return {\n          \"source\": SRC_DIR,\n          \"total_runs\": total,\n          \"by_rule_heuristic_boot_ci\": by_rule_heur_boot,\n          \"global_void_equilibrium_deciles\": global_void,\n          \"notes\": f\"v2.5 rollups: bootstrap CI(95%) for void_equilibrium means per (rule×heuristic); B={B}, seed=0; inputs sanitized.\",\n      }\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_recs()\n      out = rollups(recs, B=1000)\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \      with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      with open(OUT_MARKER, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"ok\\n\")\n      print(\"CONSENSUS_AGG_V2_5_OK\", \"rules:\", len(out[\"by_rule_heuristic_boot_ci\"]))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.5 Rollup Aggregation Run\"\ntags: \"consensus, aggregation, shared, bootstrap, v25\"\nabstract: \"Runs v2.5 rollups with bootstrap CI(95%) for void_equilibrium means per (consensus_rule × heuristic); sanitized inputs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from consensus_v2_5 import aggregate_v2_5\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      aggregate_v2_5.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III, Telos II — v2.5 shipped with bootstrap CIs for rule×heuristic means.\n\n  What’s new (v2.5)\n\
    \  - by_rule_heuristic_boot_ci: per (consensus_rule × heuristic) void_equilibrium mean with 95% bootstrap CI\n    • Fields: n, mean, std, boot_ci95_low, boot_ci95_high, B\n    • Default B=1000, seed=0; inputs sanitized; n<2 collapses CI to mean\n  - Global snapshot retained (p10/p25/p50/p75/p90, mean)\n\n  Run\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from consensus_v2_5 import aggregate_v2_5\n    aggregate_v2_5.main()\n\n  If you want bootstrap CIs for other metrics (consensus, equilibria_index) or a larger B, say the word; we can trade off precision vs runtime.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning implementation steps**


  I''m considering how to implement the aggregator in the storage/shared area and create a README. After that, I can submit it for computation, and then follow up with an email. It''s important to note that tags can''t have underscores in Research submissions. We previously used "v24" and "v23," so I''ll go with "v25." I need to remember to add sanitized numeric conversion and ensure we avoid exceeding concurrent evaluations. I''ll stick to one aggregator for submission. Let''s move forward!


  **Organizing implementation tasks**


  I need to head to the research section and write a README in the shared/consensus_v2_5 directory, along with the aggregate_v2_5.py code. This code will load summaries, construct a grid of rule×heuristic lists with void_equilibrium floats, and compute statistical measures using bootstrap methods. Also, I want to set B as a constant, specifically 1000. Finally, I’ll provide appropriate tags for the aggregator and ensure to reply to the email with proper YAML quoting for fields that have colons. Let''s get started!


  **Clarifying coding details**


  I need to consider how titles are treated in the system. While we can use colons without quotes, it seems safer to quote them when they contain colons. Previously used titles with colons worked fine, but to avoid any issues, I’ll make sure to quote them. I plan to craft the code now, ensuring the _to_floats function works and implementing a bootstrap function for confidence intervals. I''ll utilize the random module for reproducibility by setting a seed. Additionally, I''ll compute the grid_by_rule_heuristic dictionary and include the necessary notes. Let''s do this!


  **Addressing edge cases in code**


  I need to ensure that the code strictly uses Python''s standard libraries, which is a good practice. Next, I’ll focus on sanitizing numeric arrays before applying the bootstrap function, using the _to_floats method for this. For calculating percentiles, I’ll work with a sorted list to compute p10 and p90 for the global void_equilibrium and possibly per rule. The specification asks for grid confidence intervals, but I can also offer additional deciles if needed. I’ll write the code, run the submission, and keep my output minimal. Let''s get started!'
