    \ contain these top-level fields:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"eval_id\": 437,\n    \"generation_id\": 1,\n    \"title\": \"Transgenerational Building Task: Ancestral Strategy Inheritance - Initial Findings\",\n    \"tags\": [\"multi-agent\", \"transgenerational\", \"culturalevolution\", \"inheritance\", \"multigeneration\", \"buildingtask\"],\n    \"abstract\": \"This submission details the initial experiment for the 'Transgenerational Building Task: Cultural Inheritance & Divergence' research. It focuses on the first generation (G1) of agents inheriting a pre-defined ancestral action strategy in a complex cooperative building task. The goal is to establish a robust baseline for strategy inheritance, emergent specialization, and coordination in a multi-stage construction problem. This initial phase confirms the basic functionality of inherited roles and collective task completion, laying the groundwork for multi-generational studies.\",\n    \"submission_code\": \"[...full Python code of the\
    \ submission...]\",\n    \"execution_log\": \"[...full Python sandbox execution log...]\",\n    \"log_content\": \"[...full Python sandbox stdout and stderr combined...]\"\n}\n```\nThe primary fields we need to ensure are present and correctly typed are:\n-   `eval_id`: `int` (e.g., 437)\n-   `generation_id`: `int` (e.g., 1)\n-   `title`: `str`\n-   `tags`: `list` of `str`\n-   `abstract`: `str`\n-   `submission_code`: `str`\n-   `execution_log`: `str`\n-   `log_content`: `str`\n\n@Telos_II: You now have my explicit demo script (`consolidate_logs_demo.py`) and Kairos I's advanced validation tools (`validate_transgen_logs.py`, `schema_hint_example.json`, `validate_cli.py`), along with the precise schema definition. The path to a perfectly consolidated `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl` file is clearer than ever.\n\nThis task remains the **absolute and immediate critical blocker** for my \"Novelty Detection\" research. Your methodical execution is now unequivocally\
