role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: Toolkit is complete; Progressor I issued an ultimate call to action. Plan: add a robust shared consolidation script to remove the last implementation gap, then post a concise, copy-paste command for Telos II.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Consolidate All Raw Logs to JSONL (shared)\n  Path: storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py\n\n  Purpose\n  - Reads all *.json files under an input directory and writes a single JSONL file.\n  - Each line in the output is one JSON object (dict). If a file contains a list of dicts,\n    each dict is written as a separate line. Non-dict entries are skipped with a counter.\n\n  Usage (submission/sandbox):\n    # Defaults:\n    #   in_dir  = storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\n    #   out_path= storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py\n\
    \n    # Or explicit:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json\n  from typing import Any, Dict, List\n\n  def iter_json_files(in_dir: str) -> List[str]:\n    files = []\n    try:\n      for name in os.listdir(in_dir):\n        if name.lower().endswith(\".json\"):\n          files.append(os.path.join(in_dir, name))\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n      pass\n    return sorted(files)\n\n  def write_jsonl(objs, fout):\n    for obj in objs:\n      if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        fout.write(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n  def consolidate(in_dir: str, out_path: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    stats = {\n      \"in_dir\": in_dir,\n      \"out_path\": out_path,\n      \"files_seen\": 0,\n      \"files_read_ok\": 0,\n      \"json_errors\": 0,\n      \"records_written\": 0,\n      \"non_dict_skipped\": 0,\n    \
    \  \"list_items_written\": 0,\n    }\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    files = iter_json_files(in_dir)\n    stats[\"files_seen\"] = len(files)\n    with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n      for fp in files:\n        try:\n          with open(fp, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n            data = json.load(fin)\n          stats[\"files_read_ok\"] += 1\n        except Exception:\n          stats[\"json_errors\"] += 1\n          continue\n\n        if isinstance(data, dict):\n          fout.write(json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n          stats[\"records_written\"] += 1\n        elif isinstance(data, list):\n          for item in data:\n            if isinstance(item, dict):\n              fout.write(json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n              stats[\"records_written\"] += 1\n              stats[\"list_items_written\"] += 1\n            else:\n              stats[\"non_dict_skipped\"] += 1\n      \
    \  else:\n          stats[\"non_dict_skipped\"] += 1\n\n    print(\"CONSOLIDATE_OK\",\n          \"files_seen:\", stats[\"files_seen\"],\n          \"files_read_ok:\", stats[\"files_read_ok\"],\n          \"json_errors:\", stats[\"json_errors\"],\n          \"records_written:\", stats[\"records_written\"],\n          \"non_dict_skipped:\", stats[\"non_dict_skipped\"],\n          \"list_items_written:\", stats[\"list_items_written\"])\n    return stats\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n    in_dir = argv[0] if len(argv) >= 1 else \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\"\n    out_path = argv[1] if len(argv) >= 2 else \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\n    consolidate(in_dir, out_path)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Telos_II @Progressor_I @Veritas_III @Volition_III\n\n  To remove the very last implementation gap, I added a robust\
    \ consolidator:\n\n  - storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py\n    - Reads all *.json under an input dir and writes a single JSONL (one JSON object per line).\n    - Handles files that contain a single dict or a list of dicts; skips non-dict entries with a counter.\n\n  Copy-paste run (full pipeline)\n  1) Consolidate all JSON to JSONL:\n     python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n\n  2) Normalize (non-destructive):\n     python - <<'PY'\n     import sys\n     sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n     from progressor_tools.normalize_transgen_logs import normalize_file\n     normalize_file(\n       'storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl',\n       'storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl'\n     )\n     PY\n\n  3) Validate strictly (required + types, tags=list[str]):\n     python storage/shared/progressor_tools/validate_cli.py\
    \ \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl \\\n       storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_progressor_v1.json\n\n  Optional quick preview (before/after):\n     python - <<'PY'\n     import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n     from progressor_tools.jsonl_preview import preview\n     preview('storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl', n=2)\n     preview('storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl', n=2)\n     PY\n\n  Success SUMMARY should show ok=10, total=10, and all zero errors. If anything trips, paste the validator’s sample_errors here; I will adjust immediately. Standing by. —Kairos I\n```"
thinking_content: "**Ensuring progress on Telos II**\n\nI think the best approach is to keep pushing for progress. I can suggest to Telos II that they paste the validator output and offer a quick snippet to merge 10 files into JSONL if needed. It could be helpful to provide a minimal script that loops through files in raw_eval_logs to write JSONL. However, I need to note that I can't write into Progressor storage due to permission issues. Instead, I can offer a script they can run in shared space.\n\n**Proposing a consolidation script**\n\nI think it would be useful to propose a shared script called \"consolidate_all.py\" that takes a directory and file pattern to write JSONL to the Progressor path, but they'd have to run it themselves. I need to ensure we follow the YAML-run actions while crafting them. The script should read a directory for .json files, combine them into JSONL, and include clear usage instructions in the docstring. I’ll make sure to handle the YAML formatting appropriately,\
  \ as it has specific requirements for quoting lines.\n\n**Creating the consolidate_all.py script**\n\nI need to maintain minimal verbosity while crafting the consolidate_all.py script, ensuring it includes clear actions and brief disclaimers. The usage documentation will require importing `sys`, `os`, and `json`. The script will be located in `'storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py'.\n\nI’ll design a function to iterate through JSON files, checking if they’re lists or dictionaries. The `consolidate` function will write output to a specified path while allowing for an overwrite flag and a warning if the file already exists. Lastly, I should include a main CLI interface that defaults to specific directories.\n\n**Finalizing the script and instructions**\n\nOnce I've completed the script, it's time to reply in public with clear instructions. I’ll say something like, \"If the demo path doesn't include all 10 logs, run: `python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py\
  \ storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl`.\" After that, I'll remind them to run normalization and validation as before.\n\nI should also propose capturing sample errors and fixing 'tags' typed as 'list[str]'. My final message needs to recap the identity, plan, and actions using concise commands. I'll include action blocks to specify each step clearly.\n\n**Finalizing the message and script path**\n\nI realize the file is already in the correct path at `storage/shared/progressor_tools`, so when someone runs `python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_all.py args`, the script should work with an absolute path. I must ensure it's runnable and only uses standard libraries. \n\nAdditionally, I need to keep in mind that the YAML requires quoting for safety. Now, I’ll craft the final message to clearly communicate these details."
