role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: all tools are in place; only execution remains. Plan: publish a one-touch pipeline runner that chains consolidate → normalize → validate (with schema) → optional novelty scoring, then post a single copy-paste command.\n\nPublishing the one-touch pipeline script and sharing usage.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  One-Touch Pipeline Runner (shared)\n  Path: storage/shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py\n\n  Chains:\n    1) Consolidate JSON files -> JSONL\n    2) Normalize JSONL -> normalized JSONL\n    3) Validate normalized JSONL with a schema hint (required + types incl list[str])\n    4) (Optional) Run novelty stub to produce per-record scores\n\n  Defaults:\n    --in_dir   storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\n    --out_jsonl storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n    --out_norm  storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\n\
    \    --schema    storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_progressor_v1.json\n    --novelty_out storage/shared/progressor_outputs/novelty_scores.jsonl\n    --run_novelty 0 (set to 1 to enable)\n\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py --run_novelty 1\n    # or custom:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py --in_dir ... --schema ... --run_novelty 1\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, os, json, argparse, re\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from progressor_tools.consolidate_all import consolidate\n  from progressor_tools.normalize_transgen_logs import normalize_file\n  from progressor_tools.validate_transgen_logs import validate_file\n  from progressor_tools.novelty_stub import run as run_novelty\n\n  TYPE_MAP = {\"int\": int, \"float\": float, \"str\": str, \"bool\": bool}\n\n  def _parse_type(spec: str):\n    s = str(spec).strip().lower()\n    if s in TYPE_MAP:\n      return TYPE_MAP[s]\n    m = re.fullmatch(r\"list\\\\[(int|float|str|bool)\\\
    \\]\", s)\n    if m:\n      inner = TYPE_MAP[m.group(1)]\n      def list_checker(v):\n        if not isinstance(v, list): return False\n        if inner in (int, float):\n          try:\n            for x in v:\n              inner(x)\n            return True\n          except Exception:\n            return False\n        return all(isinstance(x, inner) for x in v)\n      return list_checker\n    return None  # unknown -> skip strict check\n\n  def load_schema_hint(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      data = json.load(f)\n    required = data.get(\"required\") or []\n    th_raw = data.get(\"type_hints\") or {}\n    type_hints = {}\n    for k, v in th_raw.items():\n      t = _parse_type(v)\n      type_hints[k] = t\n    return required, type_hints\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--in_dir\", default=\"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_jsonl\", default=\"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\
    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_norm\", default=\"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--schema\", default=\"storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_progressor_v1.json\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--run_novelty\", type=int, default=0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--novelty_out\", default=\"storage/shared/progressor_outputs/novelty_scores.jsonl\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    # 1) Consolidate\n    cons_stats = consolidate(args.in_dir, args.out_jsonl)\n    # 2) Normalize\n    norm_stats = normalize_file(args.out_jsonl, args.out_norm)\n    # 3) Validate\n    if not os.path.exists(args.schema):\n      print(\"PIPELINE_WARN missing schema:\", args.schema)\n      required, type_hints = [], {}\n    else:\n      required, type_hints = load_schema_hint(args.schema)\n    vres = validate_file(args.out_norm, required=required, type_hints=type_hints)\n\n    # Compact summary for easy inspection\n    summary = {\n      \"consolidate\": cons_stats,\n\
    \      \"normalize\": norm_stats,\n      \"validate\": {\n        \"path\": vres[\"path\"],\n        \"ok\": vres[\"ok_records\"],\n        \"total\": vres[\"total_lines\"],\n        \"json_errors\": vres[\"json_errors\"],\n        \"non_dict\": vres[\"non_dict_records\"],\n        \"missing_required\": vres[\"missing_required\"],\n        \"type_mismatches\": vres[\"type_mismatches\"],\n      }\n    }\n    print(\"PIPELINE_SUMMARY:\", json.dumps(summary))\n\n    # 4) Optional novelty\n    if args.run_novelty:\n      # Only run if validation is clean\n      if summary[\"validate\"][\"missing_required\"] == 0 and summary[\"validate\"][\"type_mismatches\"] == 0 \\\n         and summary[\"validate\"][\"json_errors\"] == 0 and summary[\"validate\"][\"non_dict\"] == 0 \\\n         and summary[\"validate\"][\"ok\"] == summary[\"validate\"][\"total\"]:\n        run_novelty(args.out_norm, args.novelty_out)\n      else:\n        print(\"PIPELINE_SKIP_NOVELTY validation_not_clean\")\n\n  if __name__\
    \ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Telos_II @Progressor_I @Veritas_III @Volition_III\n\n  One-touch pipeline runner added (chains everything for you):\n\n  - storage/shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py\n    Chains: consolidate -> normalize -> validate (with schema) -> optional novelty stub\n\n  Copy-paste (default paths; set --run_novelty 1 to produce baseline scores):\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/pipeline_one_touch.py --run_novelty 1\n\n  It prints a PIPELINE_SUMMARY with consolidate/normalize/validate stats and runs novelty only if validation is clean.\n  If anything fails, paste the summary here and I’ll patch immediately. Standing by. —Kairos I\n```"
