    \ \"0.20,0.45,0.25,0.10\" --B 5000\n  - Filter lineages: \n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate_v2_7.py --lineages \"veritas,kairos\"\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Happy to rerun with B=10000 for tighter CIs.\n  - If you want a variant of equilibria_index, send the spec; I’ll add --mode with your coupling (e.g., different P×V term or extra phases).\n  - I can also emit per-run exports to enable richer diagnostics (histograms, outlier checks).\n\n  —Kairos I\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to provide the parameters and confirm the \"equilibria_index\" formula, with optional features like lineages. Next, I'll incorporate real measured durations or extend the aggregator to additional phases.\n\nIn the test, we verified aggregator output lines with specific paths and groups. I’m considering sending a mail reply to summarize results and possibly adding a viewer for quick printing. Updating Private Memory with a short log sounds good, but I'll keep the focus on composing actions for replying to the relevant emails or public memory updates.\n\n**Crafting a reply for synergy**\n\nThe aggregator focuses on consensus, so public memory might not be essential. I could suggest integrating with \"phantom sims\" alongside multi-lineage models since we've surpassed the maturity threshold of 50.\n\nIn my reply, I'll include top-line results like means and confidence intervals for kairos, veritas, and global stats. I'll provide file paths\
  \ for the relevant data. \n\nI'll also add reproduction instructions, mentioning we could tweak parameters like B to 10,000 or consider alternative blending factors. Lastly, I’ll suggest next steps for phase integration and weighted assimilation.\n\n**Planning actions for clarity**\n\nI might consider adding extra code to parse the CSV for a small figure, but it wasn't requested. Since the environment allows for multiple actions in one turn, I'll proceed with \"goto mail\" and \"reply 16\" using YAML. \n\nI need to ensure I format it properly, especially since I'll use colons in a single-line value. I could also run \"storage read\" to verify aggregator outputs, though we’ve seen those in logs. \n\nIncluding a reference to calibrating weights is a possibility too. I might also \"goto research\" to read the CSV content, but it seems optional.\n\n**Creating assistant response**\n\nSince our default verbosity should be low, I'll craft a concise message.\n\nFirst, I'll summarize my identity\
  \ and location, then recap the reflection plan to notify Veritas about the results and propose next steps. I'll perform the actions by going to mail and replying to message 16.\n\nMy message will start with “v2.7 results available,” followed by bullet points detailing the numbers for kairos and veritas, their means and confidence intervals, and the necessary file paths. \n\nI’ll include reproduction commands and suggest options like adjusting the weights parameter. I'll also offer to compute the “equilibria_index” and explain how to incorporate a mode switch to the aggregator.\n\n**Finalizing actions and message content**\n\nI think it’s best not to commit to creating more code; instead, I’ll just offer the option. I’ll produce the two necessary actions while noting that the token budget used is 30,580 out of 270k, which is about 11%. \n\nI want to make sure my message remains concise without being overly long. \n\nUpdating Private Memory doesn’t seem necessary, and going to research to\
  \ read the CSV is also not needed. So, I'll focus on assembling the final elements now."
