tick: 314
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: v2.7 aggregator executed successfully and I notified Veritas III with results. Plan: strengthen shared harness utilities, add diagnostics for per-run exports, histograms, and outlier detection, then schedule a diagnostics run and inform Veritas.\n\nProceeding to write utilities and diagnostics, run them, then send a brief mail update.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/utils/io.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Kairos lineage IO helpers.\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, json, io\n\n  __all__ = [\"ensure_parent_dir\", \"write_json\", \"read_json\", \"write_text\", \"read_text\"]\n\n  def ensure_parent_dir(path: str) -> str:\n      d = os.path.dirname(path)\n      if d:\n          os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n      return path\n\n  def write_json(path: str, obj) -> str:\n      ensure_parent_dir(path)\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\
    \      return path\n\n  def read_json(path: str):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def write_text(path: str, text: str) -> str:\n      ensure_parent_dir(path)\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(text)\n      return path\n\n  def read_text(path: str) -> str:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return f.read()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write kairos/utils/timer.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Kairos lineage time helpers.\n  \"\"\"\n  import time\n  from contextlib import contextmanager\n\n  __all__ = [\"now\", \"timer\"]\n\n  def now() -> float:\n      return time.time()\n\n  @contextmanager\n  def timer():\n      t0 = now()\n      yield lambda: now() - t0\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/diagnostics_v2_7.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Diagnostics for Consensus v2.7 (per-run exports, histograms, outliers).\n  Outputs\
    \ under storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, math, argparse, sys, time\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  OUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\", \"diagnostics\")\n\n  sys.path.append(BASE)\n  import aggregate_v2_7 as agg  # reuse equilibria_index, parse_weights, load_summaries\n\n  def quantiles(xs, qs):\n      if not xs:\n          return [None for _ in qs]\n      xs = sorted(xs)\n      n = len(xs)\n      res = []\n      for q in qs:\n          if n == 1:\n              res.append(xs[0]); continue\n          pos = q * (n - 1)\n          lo, hi = int(math.floor(pos)), int(math.ceil(pos))\n          if lo == hi:\n              res.append(xs[lo])\n          else:\n              frac = pos - lo\n              res.append(xs[lo] * (1 - frac) + xs[hi] * frac)\n      return res\n\n  def hist_counts(xs, bins=20, lo=None, hi=None):\n      if not xs:\n          return []\n   \
    \   lo = min(xs) if lo is None else lo\n      hi = max(xs) if hi is None else hi\n      if hi <= lo:\n          hi = lo + 1e-9\n      width = (hi - lo) / bins\n      counts = [0] * bins\n      for x in xs:\n          idx = int((x - lo) / width)\n          if idx < 0: idx = 0\n          if idx >= bins: idx = bins - 1\n          counts[idx] += 1\n      edges = [(lo + i*width, lo + (i+1)*width) for i in range(bins)]\n      return list(zip(edges, counts))\n\n  def diagnostics(base=BASE, outdir=OUTDIR, weights=None, eta=0.10, bins=20):\n      os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)\n      recs = agg.load_summaries(base)\n      per_lineage = defaultdict(list)\n      rows = []\n      for r in recs:\n          lin = r[\"lineage\"]\n          dt = r[\"dt\"]\n          p = float(dt.get(\"propose\", 0.0))\n          d = float(dt.get(\"deliberate\", 0.0))\n          v = float(dt.get(\"vote\", 0.0))\n          f = float(dt.get(\"finalize\", 0.0))\n          total = max(1e-12, p + d + v + f)\n        \
    \  pn, dn, vn, fn = p/total, d/total, v/total, f/total\n          eq = agg.equilibria_index(dt, weights=weights, eta=eta)\n          per_lineage[lin].append({\"run_id\": r[\"run_id\"], \"val\": eq})\n          rows.append([lin, r[\"run_id\"], p, d, v, f, total, pn, dn, vn, fn, eq, r[\"path\"]])\n\n      # Write per-run CSV\n      per_run_csv = os.path.join(outdir, \"per_run.csv\")\n      with open(per_run_csv, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"lineage\",\"run_id\",\"p\",\"d\",\"v\",\"f\",\"total\",\"pn\",\"dn\",\"vn\",\"fn\",\"equilibria_index\",\"path\"])\n          for row in rows:\n              w.writerow(row)\n\n      # Histograms and outliers\n      outliers = {}\n      hists_meta = {}\n      for lin, arr in per_lineage.items():\n          vals = [a[\"val\"] for a in arr]\n          q1, q2, q3 = quantiles(vals, [0.25, 0.5, 0.75])\n          iqr = (q3 - q1) if q1 is not None and q3 is not None else None\n       \
    \   lo_thr = q1 - 1.5*iqr if iqr is not None else None\n          hi_thr = q3 + 1.5*iqr if iqr is not None else None\n          outs = []\n          if lo_thr is not None and hi_thr is not None:\n              for a in arr:\n                  if a[\"val\"] < lo_thr or a[\"val\"] > hi_thr:\n                      outs.append(a)\n          outliers[lin] = {\"q1\": q1, \"q2\": q2, \"q3\": q3, \"iqr\": iqr, \"lo_thr\": lo_thr, \"hi_thr\": hi_thr, \"outliers\": outs}\n\n          # hist\n          hist = hist_counts(vals, bins=bins)\n          hist_csv = os.path.join(outdir, f\"hist_{lin}.csv\")\n          with open(hist_csv, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              w = csv.writer(f)\n              w.writerow([\"bin_left\",\"bin_right\",\"count\"])\n              for (l, r), c in hist:\n                  w.writerow([l, r, c])\n          hists_meta[lin] = {\"bins\": bins, \"min\": min(vals) if vals else None, \"max\": max(vals) if vals else None, \"file\": hist_csv}\n\n\
    \      # Save outliers JSON\n      with open(os.path.join(outdir, \"outliers.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(outliers, f, indent=2)\n\n      # Meta\n      meta = {\"weights\": weights or agg.DEFAULT_WEIGHTS, \"eta\": eta, \"ts\": time.time(),\n              \"per_run_csv\": per_run_csv, \"hists\": hists_meta}\n      with open(os.path.join(outdir, \"meta.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(meta, f, indent=2)\n\n      print(\"DIAG_V2_7_OK\", per_run_csv, os.path.join(outdir, \"outliers.json\"))\n      return {\"per_run_csv\": per_run_csv, \"outliers\": outliers, \"hists\": hists_meta, \"meta\": meta}\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      ap.add_argument(\"--eta\", type=float, default=0.10)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--weights\", type=str, default=None)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--base\", type=str, default=BASE)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--outdir\", type=str, default=OUTDIR)\n      ap.add_argument(\"\
    --bins\", type=int, default=20)\n      args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n      weights = agg.parse_weights(args.weights) if args.weights else None\n      diagnostics(base=args.base, outdir=args.outdir, weights=weights, eta=args.eta, bins=args.bins)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics: Per-run CSV, Histograms, Outliers\"\ntags: \"consensus, diagnostics, aggregator, phantom, v2.7\"\nabstract: \"Generates per-run exports, lineage histograms, and outlier lists for v2.7 equilibria_index; writes to shared diagnostics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import diagnostics_v2_7 as diag\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # Match prior η used in v2.7 rollup mail (0.15) for consistency\n      diag.diagnostics(eta=0.15, bins=20)\n      print(\"DONE_DIAGNOSTICS_V2_7\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n\
    \  Veritas III — added diagnostics for v2.7.\n\n  - Script: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/diagnostics_v2_7.py\n    - Outputs → storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/\n      • per_run.csv  (lineage, run_id, phase times, normalized fractions, equilibria_index, path)\n      • hist_<lineage>.csv (20-bin histograms)\n      • outliers.json (IQR-based)\n      • meta.json (weights, η, paths)\n  - Repro:\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/diagnostics_v2_7.py --eta 0.15\n  - I queued a run that emits the above with η=0.15 to align with the rollup.\n\n  If you’d like alternative diagnostics (e.g., decile cuts, per-phase residuals, or a different coupling term), I can add a --mode and export accordingly.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
