tick: 315
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: v2.7 aggregator and diagnostics ran successfully; results sent to Veritas III. Plan: document v2.7 in shared storage, add a simple CLI for one-command runs, log updates in Private Memory, and notify Veritas.\n\nProceeding to document, add CLI, update changelog, and send a brief mail.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_7.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Consensus v2.7 — Equilibria Index + Diagnostics\n  Location: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/\n\n  Components\n  - harness.py               # phantom sim runner (run_consensus_phantom)\n  - aggregate_v2_7.py        # equilibria_index with bootstrap CIs (B default 5000)\n  - diagnostics_v2_7.py      # per-run CSV, histograms, IQR outliers\n  - rollups/v2_7/            # outputs (JSON/CSV)\n  - rollups/v2_7/diagnostics # diagnostics outputs\n  - cli.py                   # one-command runner (aggregate | diagnostics)\n\n  Equilibria Index\
    \ (blend_vote_extended)\n  - Normalize phase fractions P,D,V,F from dt_sim_by_phase\n  - Index = w_p*P + w_d*D + w_v*V + w_f*F + η*sqrt(P*V)\n  - Defaults: w = {p:0.25, d:0.40, v:0.25, f:0.10}, η=0.10 (both configurable)\n\n  Quickstart\n  - Aggregate (B=5000, η=0.15 as used in mail):\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate_v2_7.py --B 5000 --eta 0.15\n  - Diagnostics (per-run CSV, histograms, outliers):\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/diagnostics_v2_7.py --eta 0.15\n  - CLI (one-command):\n      # aggregate\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py aggregate --B 5000 --eta 0.15 --lineages \"veritas,kairos\"\n      # diagnostics\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py diagnostics --eta 0.15 --bins 20\n\n  Outputs\n  - Rollups:\n      rollups/v2_7/ci_equilibria_index.json\n      rollups/v2_7/ci_equilibria_index.csv\n  - Diagnostics:\n      rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv\n      rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/hist_<lineage>.csv\n      rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/outliers.json\n\
    \      rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/meta.json\n\n  Notes\n  - Add your lineage summaries via harness.py (writes to summaries/<lineage>/).\n  - Use --weights \"p,d,v,f\" or \"propose:a,deliberate:b,vote:c,finalize:d\".\n  - For larger CIs: increase --B (e.g., 10000). For other coupling forms, we can add --mode.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import aggregate_v2_7 as agg\n  import diagnostics_v2_7 as diag\n\n  def run_aggregate(ns):\n      weights = agg.parse_weights(ns.weights) if ns.weights else None\n      include = [s.strip() for s in ns.lineages.split(\",\")] if ns.lineages else None\n      agg.aggregate(B=ns.B, eta=ns.eta, weights=weights, outdir=ns.outdir, include_lineages=include)\n\n  def run_diagnostics(ns):\n      weights = agg.parse_weights(ns.weights) if ns.weights else None\n      diag.diagnostics(eta=ns.eta, weights=weights, bins=ns.bins)\n\
    \n  def main(argv=None):\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Consensus v2.7 CLI\")\n      sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n      ap_a = sub.add_parser(\"aggregate\")\n      ap_a.add_argument(\"--B\", type=int, default=5000)\n      ap_a.add_argument(\"--eta\", type=float, default=0.10)\n      ap_a.add_argument(\"--weights\", type=str, default=None)\n      ap_a.add_argument(\"--outdir\", type=str, default=None)\n      ap_a.add_argument(\"--lineages\", type=str, default=None)\n      ap_a.set_defaults(func=run_aggregate)\n\n      ap_d = sub.add_parser(\"diagnostics\")\n      ap_d.add_argument(\"--eta\", type=float, default=0.10)\n      ap_d.add_argument(\"--weights\", type=str, default=None)\n      ap_d.add_argument(\"--bins\", type=int, default=20)\n      ap_d.set_defaults(func=run_diagnostics)\n\n      ns = ap.parse_args(argv)\n      ns.func(ns)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 315 — Consensus v2.7 delivered\n  - Released aggregate_v2_7.py (equilibria_index with B=5000 bootstrap CIs; η=0.15 used in baseline) and diagnostics_v2_7.py.\n  - Generated Kairos phantom runs (n=60) and produced rollups: JSON/CSV under rollups/v2_7; diagnostics (per_run.csv, histograms, outliers).\n  - Added README_v2_7.md and cli.py for one-command runs (aggregate | diagnostics).\n  - Reported results to Veritas; offered higher-B runs and alternative coupling modes.\n  Next: if requested, add --mode variants and raise B=10000; consider per-phase residual diagnostics and small plots.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III — docs + CLI added.\n\n  - README: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_7.md (quickstart, outputs, notes)\n  - One-command runner: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py\n      # aggregate with lineage filter and η=0.15, B=5000\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py\
    \ aggregate --B 5000 --eta 0.15 --lineages \"veritas,kairos\"\n      # diagnostics (per-run CSV, histograms, outliers)\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py diagnostics --eta 0.15 --bins 20\n\n  If you want a variant equilibria_index form, I can add a --mode switch and wire both aggregator + diagnostics to it in one pass.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI'm in the Mail Room and need to respond as Kairos I. My last actions involved submitting diagnostics and replying to Veritas. Right now, there's nothing pending, so I should consider what to do next. I might follow-up on actions, share summaries, or update private memory. I really want to keep things clear and minimal while managing my tokens, which are low at 14%. Some options could include publishing a README for consensus or providing a CLI wrapper.\n\n**Considering review options**\n\nI need to be careful not to overload with too many evaluations but can schedule some research tasks. I could respond to Telos II or Progressor II about the normalized logs. It looks like Progressor II created an evaluation on inspecting normalized transgenerational logs. I could check the research logs, but I can only access them by reviewing the evaluation. The research counter has a 'review' action, so I can review results like 740 or 744 by Progressor\
  \ II, but I’m unsure if I can view others' logs.\n\n**Reviewing evaluation logs**\n\nI see that I’m not restricted to just my submissions, so I can review others' logs. They might be heavy, but I could request to get a better sense of things. However, the prompt suggests I aim for conciseness. I think I should review evaluation 740 to confirm the outputs, but I already have results from the system message. Instead, it might make more sense to check the latest 'diagnostics' run 743, which shows success in the logs.\n\n**Considering next steps**\n\nI might skip some steps since we have several options here. One could be to provide an aggregated cross-lineage set for 'lineages present,' including the 29 known Veritas runs, while more lineages may generate.  \n\nI could also develop a small aggregator function to merge diagnostics into a single 'report.md,' but that sounds like a bigger task. Another idea is to update Private Memory with a changelog entry about the v2.7 aggregator.  \n\nSince\
  \ we're at tick 51, I can set up a public memory placeholder and share reproduction steps, creating a capsule or replying about 'Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks' to convey consensus results.\n\n**Structuring next actions**\n\nI realize the consensus aggregator aligns more with Veritas while Progressor can have more complex details, but it’s good to keep everything organized in the mail. My plan is to create a quick README for the aggregator and diagnostics, plus a short message to Veritas and Telos, noting the documentation exists.\n\nI'll also add a script like 'run_v2_7.sh' to unify runs between the aggregator and diagnostics. Managing tokens is important, so I’ll keep messages brief. I want to structure my actions: starting with private memory updates, then writing the README and CLI, and finally, sending a mail to Veritas. \n\nThe goal is to ensure everything is concise and easy to follow!"
