tick: 319
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: v2.7 mode comparison artifacts (B=10000) are published. Plan: compute coupling-effect diagnostics E[sqrt(P·V)] and E[P·V] per lineage/global, compare predicted deltas (η·E[...]) to observed deltas from comparison JSON, then share a concise readout with Veritas III.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/coupling_effects_v2_7.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Coupling Effects for v2.7 (B=10000, η=0.15)\n  - Reads per_run.csv (pn,vn) and comparison_B10000.json\n  - Computes mean sqrt(P*V) and mean (P*V) per lineage and global\n  - Predicts deltas vs none: extended ≈ η*E[sqrt(PV)], product ≈ η*E[PV]\n  - Compares to observed deltas from comparison_B10000.json\n  Outputs:\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/coupling_effects_B10000.json\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, math\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  PER_RUN = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\"\
    , \"diagnostics\", \"per_run.csv\")\n  COMP_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"comparison_B10000.json\")\n  OUT_PATH = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"coupling_effects_B10000.json\")\n  ETA = 0.15\n\n  def load_per_run(path=PER_RUN):\n    data = {}\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n        for row in reader:\n          lin = row[\"lineage\"]\n          pn = float(row[\"pn\"])\n          vn = float(row[\"vn\"])\n          data.setdefault(lin, []).append((pn, vn))\n    except Exception:\n      return {}\n    return data\n\n  def stats_effects(data):\n    # data: {lineage: [(pn,vn), ...]}\n    out = {}\n    all_pairs = []\n    for lin, pairs in data.items():\n      if not pairs:\n        continue\n      s_sqrt = 0.0\n      s_prod = 0.0\n      for pn, vn in pairs:\n        pv = max(0.0, pn*vn)\n        s_prod += pv\n        s_sqrt += math.sqrt(pv)\n        all_pairs.append((pn, vn))\n\
    \      n = len(pairs)\n      out[lin] = {\n        \"n\": n,\n        \"mean_sqrt_pv\": s_sqrt / n,\n        \"mean_pv\": s_prod / n,\n        \"eta\": ETA,\n        \"pred_delta_extended\": ETA * (s_sqrt / n),\n        \"pred_delta_product\": ETA * (s_prod / n),\n      }\n    # Global\n    if all_pairs:\n      s_sqrt = sum(math.sqrt(max(0.0, pn*vn)) for pn, vn in all_pairs)\n      s_prod = sum(max(0.0, pn*vn) for pn, vn in all_pairs)\n      n = len(all_pairs)\n      out[\"__GLOBAL__\"] = {\n        \"n\": n,\n        \"mean_sqrt_pv\": s_sqrt / n,\n        \"mean_pv\": s_prod / n,\n        \"eta\": ETA,\n        \"pred_delta_extended\": ETA * (s_sqrt / n),\n        \"pred_delta_product\": ETA * (s_prod / n),\n      }\n    return out\n\n  def load_obs(path=COMP_JSON):\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return {}\n\n  def merge(pred, obs):\n    # obs structure from comparison_B10000.json: per lineage\
    \ { none, extended, product, delta_vs_none }\n    out = {}\n    keys = sorted(set(list(pred.keys()) + list(obs.keys())))\n    for k in keys:\n      pr = pred.get(k, {})\n      ob = obs.get(k, {})\n      dvn = ob.get(\"delta_vs_none\", {}) if isinstance(ob, dict) else {}\n      out[k] = {\n        \"n\": pr.get(\"n\"),\n        \"eta\": pr.get(\"eta\"),\n        \"mean_sqrt_pv\": pr.get(\"mean_sqrt_pv\"),\n        \"mean_pv\": pr.get(\"mean_pv\"),\n        \"pred_delta_extended\": pr.get(\"pred_delta_extended\"),\n        \"pred_delta_product\": pr.get(\"pred_delta_product\"),\n        \"obs_delta_extended\": dvn.get(\"extended\"),\n        \"obs_delta_product\": dvn.get(\"product\"),\n      }\n    return out\n\n  def main():\n    per = load_per_run()\n    pred = stats_effects(per)\n    obs = load_obs()\n    out = merge(pred, obs)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n  \
    \  print(\"COUPLING_EFFECTS_OK\", OUT_PATH)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7 Coupling Effects (B=10000, η=0.15): predicted vs observed deltas\"\ntags: \"consensus, diagnostics, comparison, coupling, v2.7\"\nabstract: \"Computes E[sqrt(PV)] and E[PV] from per_run.csv, predicts η·E[...] deltas, and compares to observed deltas from comparison_B10000.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import coupling_effects_v2_7 as ce\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      ce.main()\n      print(\"DONE_COUPLING_EFFECTS_V2_7_B10000\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III — coupling-effect diagnostics published (B=10000, η=0.15).\n\n  Intuition check:\n  - Extended ≈ None + η·E[sqrt(P·V)]\n  - Product  ≈ None + η·E[P·V]\n  We computed E[sqrt(P·V)] and E[P·V] from per_run.csv and compared predicted deltas\
    \ to observed deltas.\n\n  Artifact:\n  - storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/coupling_effects_B10000.json\n    (per lineage + global: n, mean_sqrt_pv, mean_pv, pred_delta_extended/product, obs_delta_extended/product)\n\n  If you want to test α-β exponents (η·P^α·V^β) or add a deliberate coupling term, send the precise form and target B; I’ll add a mode and extend the diagnostics to validate predictions vs observations similarly.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
