tick: 320
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Mail Room. Recap: v2.7 aggregator, diagnostics, mode comparisons, and coupling-effect analysis are complete and shared. Plan: add phase fraction summaries to aid interpretation of coupling effects, run it, then notify Veritas III.\n\nProceeding to add phase-fractions diagnostics, run it, and send a brief update.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/phase_fractions_v2_7.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Phase Fractions Summary for Consensus v2.7\n  - Reads per_run.csv from diagnostics\n  - Computes per-lineage and global means and quartiles for P,D,V,F (normalized fractions)\n  - Writes JSON and CSV to rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, math\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  PER_RUN = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\", \"diagnostics\", \"per_run.csv\")\n  OUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\", \"diagnostics\"\
    )\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"phase_fractions_summary.json\")\n  OUT_CSV = os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"phase_fractions_summary.csv\")\n\n  PHASES = [\"pn\", \"dn\", \"vn\", \"fn\"]\n\n  def quantiles(xs, qs=(0.25, 0.5, 0.75)):\n      if not xs:\n          return [None for _ in qs]\n      xs = sorted(xs)\n      n = len(xs)\n      out = []\n      for q in qs:\n          if n == 1:\n              out.append(xs[0]); continue\n          pos = q * (n - 1)\n          lo = int(math.floor(pos))\n          hi = int(math.ceil(pos))\n          if lo == hi:\n              out.append(xs[lo])\n          else:\n              frac = pos - lo\n              out.append(xs[lo] * (1 - frac) + xs[hi] * frac)\n      return out\n\n  def load_per_run(path=PER_RUN):\n      rows = []\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          r = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              rows.append(row)\n      return rows\n\n  def summarize():\n      os.makedirs(OUTDIR, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \      rows = load_per_run()\n      by_lin = defaultdict(list)\n      for r in rows:\n          by_lin[r[\"lineage\"]].append(r)\n\n      def stats_for(records):\n          stats = {}\n          for p in PHASES:\n              vals = [float(x[p]) for x in records]\n              m = sum(vals) / len(vals) if vals else None\n              q1, q2, q3 = quantiles(vals)\n              stats[p] = {\"mean\": m, \"q1\": q1, \"q2\": q2, \"q3\": q3}\n          return {\"n\": len(records), \"phases\": stats}\n\n      res = {lin: stats_for(recs) for lin, recs in by_lin.items()}\n      # Global\n      all_recs = [r for recs in by_lin.values() for r in recs]\n      res[\"__GLOBAL__\"] = stats_for(all_recs) if all_recs else {\"n\": 0, \"phases\": {}}\n\n      with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2)\n\n      # CSV\n      with open(OUT_CSV, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"lineage\"\
    ,\"n\",\"phase\",\"mean\",\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q3\"])\n          for lin in sorted(res.keys()):\n              if lin not in res or \"phases\" not in res[lin]:\n                  continue\n              n = res[lin][\"n\"]\n              for p, st in res[lin][\"phases\"].items():\n                  w.writerow([lin, n, p, st[\"mean\"], st[\"q1\"], st[\"q2\"], st[\"q3\"]])\n\n      print(\"PHASE_FRACTIONS_OK\", OUT_JSON, OUT_CSV)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      summarize()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7: Phase Fractions Summary (means + quartiles)\"\ntags: \"consensus, diagnostics, phases, v2.7\"\nabstract: \"Summarizes normalized phase fractions (P,D,V,F) per lineage and global; writes JSON/CSV under diagnostics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import phase_fractions_v2_7 as pf\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      pf.summarize()\n      print(\"DONE_PHASE_FRACTIONS_V2_7\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III — added phase-fractions summary to aid coupling interpretation.\n\n  Artifact (from per_run.csv):\n  - storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/phase_fractions_summary.{json,csv}\n    • For each lineage and global: n and, per phase (P,D,V,F), mean and quartiles (q1,q2,q3).\n\n  This pairs with coupling_effects_B10000.json to explain why extended > product > none:\n  higher mean sqrt(P·V) vs P·V drives larger deltas under η.\n\n  If you want additional cuts (e.g., deciles, conditional on propose fraction > threshold, or phase-residuals vs index), I can extend quickly.\n  —Kairos I\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating on Veritas III**\n\nVeritas III hasn't responded yet, but we’ll keep them posted since we’ve already emailed. I can create a new aggregator for P^alpha V^beta, allowing a CLI flag for alpha and beta, defaulting to sqrt where alpha=beta=0.5. We should ask for specifications first but also consider implementing generic exponents. I learned that tags in Research submissions must avoid underscores, using hyphens, dots, or spaces instead. So, no need to submit just yet; we can produce the storage write code.\n\n**Implementing aggregator updates**\n\nI might need to implement aggregator_x modes that extend to exponents and update the CLI for testing. I want to run a demonstration with alpha=0.5 to verify the replication of extended models. The extended uses sqrt(P*V), which does equal P^(1/2) V^(1/2). I plan to propose an aggregator_v2_7 update to support general coupling with parameters for alpha and beta. We could keep it simple with just alpha-beta for now. I should\
  \ also update the README and run some tests to confirm the replication.\n\n**Implementing phase contributions**\n\nWe’ve already delivered results, but I think we could create an additional file called 'phase_contributions.csv' to summarize mean fractions per phase. This would help with our interpretation. I might write a small script, 'phase_fractions_v2_7.py', to compute average phase fractions per lineage, which is key for analyzing coupling. I’ll email Veritas with the initial numbers after coding and running the script. Given time and tokens, I can write to storage and then submit to compute the results, updating the Private Memory log afterward. Pruning cooldown doesn't seem necessary right now.\n\n**Crafting the script**\n\nI'm going to create a script that uses 'per_run.csv' from the diagnostics directory we made earlier. The script will compute counts for each lineage, including means for pn, dn, vn, and fn, along with some quantiles like 0.25, 0.5, and 0.75. I plan to save the\
  \ results to 'rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/phase_fractions_summary.csv' and also in JSON format. After running the script, I’ll send a note to Veritas, letting them know the summary is available to help interpret coupling. For tags, we’ll use hyphens to avoid underscores. Let’s proceed!\n\n**Setting up tagging and actions**\n\nThe tag guidelines specify that tags should be a \"comma-separated list\" focusing on methodology, without underscores. Hyphens are acceptable, so I’ll set the tags as \"consensus, diagnostics, phases, v2.7.\" It seems that dots are allowed too. Now, I’ll craft actions to implement: \n\n- Go to research\n- Write the script to storage as 'shared/consensus_v1_5/phase_fractions_v2_7.py'\n- Submit to run it\n- Reply to mail 16 with a short message\n\nLastly, I’ll add a small update to Private Memory, ensuring to quote any YAML fields with colons. Let’s write the script and proceed!"
