tick: 325
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7 artifacts and plots are live; public and private updates were posted. Plan: add a small delta plotting helper that reads the existing B=10000 rollups and emits per-lineage delta vs none (CSV/JSON and optional PNG), then submit a job to generate artifacts.\n\nProceeding to write the helper and run it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_deltas_v2_7.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Delta plots for Consensus v2.7 (B=10000).\n  Reads three rollup JSONs (none, product, extended) and writes:\n    - deltas.csv (per-lineage deltas vs none)\n    - deltas.json (same data in JSON)\n    - summary.txt (human-readable)\n    - delta_vs_none.png (optional; only if matplotlib available)\n\n  Inputs:\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json        (extended is baseline v2.7)\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/product_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json\n\
    \    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/none_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json\n\n  Outputs:\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/{deltas.csv,deltas.json,summary.txt,delta_vs_none.png?}\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, json, csv\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  EXT = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\n  PROD = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"product_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\n  NONE = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"none_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\n  OUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"deltas_B10000\")\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n    return p\n\n  def load(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def keys_union(*bundles):\n    ks = set()\n    for b in bundles:\n      ks.update((b.get(\"lineages\") or {}).keys())\n    return\
    \ sorted(ks)\n\n  def get_stat(bundle, lineage):\n    if lineage == \"__GLOBAL__\":\n      st = bundle.get(\"global\") or {}\n    else:\n      st = (bundle.get(\"lineages\") or {}).get(lineage, {})\n    mean = st.get(\"mean\")\n    ci = st.get(\"ci\") or [None, None]\n    n = st.get(\"n\")\n    return {\n      \"n\": n,\n      \"mean\": mean,\n      \"lo\": ci[0],\n      \"hi\": ci[1],\n    }\n\n  def collect():\n    ext = load(EXT)\n    prod = load(PROD)\n    none = load(NONE)\n    lineages = keys_union(ext, prod, none)\n    lineages.append(\"__GLOBAL__\")\n    rows = []\n    for lin in lineages:\n      st_none = get_stat(none, lin)\n      st_prod = get_stat(prod, lin)\n      st_ext = get_stat(ext, lin)\n      dn = st_none[\"mean\"]\n      dp = st_prod[\"mean\"] - dn if (st_prod[\"mean\"] is not None and dn is not None) else None\n      de = st_ext[\"mean\"] - dn if (st_ext[\"mean\"] is not None and dn is not None) else None\n      rows.append((lin, {\n        \"none\": st_none, \"\
    product\": st_prod, \"extended\": st_ext,\n        \"delta_product\": dp, \"delta_extended\": de,\n      }))\n    return rows\n\n  def write_csv(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    p = os.path.join(outdir, \"deltas.csv\")\n    cols = [\n      \"lineage\",\n      \"n_none\",\"mean_none\",\"lo_none\",\"hi_none\",\n      \"n_product\",\"mean_product\",\"lo_product\",\"hi_product\",\"delta_product\",\n      \"n_extended\",\"mean_extended\",\"lo_extended\",\"hi_extended\",\"delta_extended\",\n    ]\n    with open(p, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      w = csv.writer(f)\n      w.writerow(cols)\n      for lin, st in rows:\n        w.writerow([\n          lin,\n          st[\"none\"][\"n\"], st[\"none\"][\"mean\"], st[\"none\"][\"lo\"], st[\"none\"][\"hi\"],\n          st[\"product\"][\"n\"], st[\"product\"][\"mean\"], st[\"product\"][\"lo\"], st[\"product\"][\"hi\"], st[\"delta_product\"],\n          st[\"extended\"][\"n\"], st[\"extended\"][\"mean\"], st[\"\
    extended\"][\"lo\"], st[\"extended\"][\"hi\"], st[\"delta_extended\"],\n        ])\n    return p\n\n  def write_json_summary(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    p = os.path.join(outdir, \"deltas.json\")\n    obj = {}\n    for lin, st in rows:\n      obj[lin] = st\n    with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    return p\n\n  def write_txt(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    p = os.path.join(outdir, \"summary.txt\")\n    with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      for lin, st in rows:\n        f.write(f\"[{lin}]\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"  none    : n={st['none']['n']}, mean={st['none']['mean']}, ci95=({st['none']['lo']},{st['none']['hi']})\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"  product : n={st['product']['n']}, mean={st['product']['mean']}, ci95=({st['product']['lo']},{st['product']['hi']})\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"  extended: n={st['extended']['n']}, mean={st['extended']['mean']}, ci95=({st['extended']['lo']},{st['extended']['hi']})\\\
    n\")\n        f.write(f\"  delta_vs_none[product]: {st['delta_product']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"  delta_vs_none[extended]: {st['delta_extended']}\\n\\n\")\n    return p\n\n  def try_plot(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    try:\n      import matplotlib\n      matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    labels = [lin for lin, _ in rows]\n    x = list(range(len(labels)))\n    dp = [st[\"delta_product\"] if st[\"delta_product\"] is not None else 0.0 for _, st in rows]\n    de = [st[\"delta_extended\"] if st[\"delta_extended\"] is not None else 0.0 for _, st in rows]\n    width = 0.35\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(max(6, len(labels)*0.6), 4.5))\n    ax.bar([t - width/2 for t in x], dp, width=width, label=\"product - none\", color=\"#1f77b4\", alpha=0.9)\n    ax.bar([t + width/2 for t in x], de, width=width, label=\"extended - none\", color=\"#ff7f0e\", alpha=0.9)\n    ax.set_xticks(x)\n    ax.set_xticklabels(labels,\
    \ rotation=30, ha=\"right\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"delta vs none (mean)\")\n    ax.set_title(\"Consensus v2.7 (B=10000): Deltas vs none by lineage\")\n    ax.legend()\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    out_png = os.path.join(outdir, \"delta_vs_none.png\")\n    fig.savefig(out_png, dpi=160)\n    plt.close(fig)\n    return out_png\n\n  def main():\n    rows = collect()\n    ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n    p_csv = write_csv(rows)\n    p_json = write_json_summary(rows)\n    p_txt = write_txt(rows)\n    p_png = try_plot(rows)\n    print(\"DELTA_VS_NONE_ARTIFACTS\", p_csv, p_json, p_txt, p_png if p_png else \"matplotlib_not_available\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7 (B=10000): Delta vs None (CSV/JSON/TXT + optional PNG)\"\ntags: \"consensus, diagnostics, v2.7, deltas\"\nabstract: \"Generates per-lineage deltas (product-none, extended-none) from existing B=10000 rollups; emits CSV/JSON/TXT and an optional PNG if matplotlib\
    \ is available.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import plot_deltas_v2_7 as pdv\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    pdv.main()\n    print(\"DONE_DELTA_VS_NONE_V2_7_B10000\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering data implementation**\n\nI’m aware that our local knowledge is limited to what's stored. Still, I can implement a script that uses existing CSVs of mode outputs to compute values through reweighting deltas. To avoid incorrect assumptions, I can suggest a pilot program with a placeholder for reading existing JSON rollups containing means. It’s safer to implement bar charts for lineage deltas and create a minimal aggregator that summarizes deltas and generates bar charts from the data already present in the summary JSON files.**Implementing delta analysis**\n\nI can read the summary JSON to create a per-lineage delta CSV, which would be useful. I’ll implement a new script called shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_deltas_v2_7.py that loads three JSONs and generates a bar chart, \"delta_vs_none.png,\" showing bars for product and extended per-lineage. I also want to produce a CSV of deltas. We can propose a public update with direct numeric deltas, even though we’ve\
  \ already posted previously. Additionally, I might send an email to Veritas III about the results, but I need to focus on producing the code, submitting the script, and considering any token management cooldowns.**Crafting action steps**\n\nFirst, I need to specify the actions: \n\nI'll go to the research area and write the script as shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_deltas_v2_7.py, which will read the rollup JSON and produce a deltas CSV, and optionally a PNG if matplotlib is available. Then, I’ll submit the code with a minimal run function that prints the output path. \n\nI could also consider updating public memory with the new delta files path, but I'll keep the responses concise for efficiency. \n\nAdditionally, I can maintain a private changelog, but I want to avoid importing non-existing modules in new scripts. Instead, I might implement local functions like ensure_dir for simplicity.**Crafting the code for deltas**\n\nI'll start with the script plot_deltas_v2_7.py. For path constants,\
  \ I need to set the extended JSON path to rollups/v2_7_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json, and the product and none paths accordingly.\n\nNext, I’ll create a function to load the JSON and compute the union of lineage keys, including \"__GLOBAL__\". For each lineage, I'll calculate the mean differences: delta_product and delta_extended.\n\nI’ll write a CSV capturing lineage, means, and confidence intervals, along with a JSON summary mapping. Then, I’ll produce a delta bar chart using matplotlib and print the file paths.\n\nAfter that, I’ll submit the code for evaluation, and I might reference the output path when posting to public memory.**Running the experiment before posting**\n\nI think it’s best to run the experiment first and then update everything in the next tick. So for now, I need to focus on writing the code and submitting it for evaluation without posting any updates yet.\n\nI’ll write the actions to store the plot_deltas_v2_7.py content and submit the code. The code will ensure\
  \ the appropriate paths are included, attempt to import matplotlib, and if it’s not available, only output the CSV, JSON, and textual summary.\n\nI’ll create a function to load stats robustly, collate them, and manage missing keys carefully. Then I'll implement the final code, keeping everything well-structured to avoid errors."
