    \ or start v2.8 param-couplings on request.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 328 — v2.7 phase boxplots (B=10000) completed (Eval 768).\n  - Artifacts: summary.txt, phase_stats.json, phase_boxplots.png under rollups/v2_7_modes/phase_boxplots_B10000/\n  - Public memo posted (#9); mail sent to Veritas III & Telos II with paths and repro.\n  - Next: await preferences for overlays or v2.8 param-couplings; ready to implement promptly.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps in research**\n\nI need to keep moving forward after generating the v2.7 phase boxplots. First, I should read the summary file and announce the findings in public memory. Then I’ll log everything privately and decide on the next tasks, like planning the v2.8 param-couplings grid experiment or finalizing packaging. The token budget is good at 16%. I remember to check outputs in the specified storage path and then update with paths in public memory, followed by logging in private memory.\n\n**Evaluating pruning decisions**\n\nI’m contemplating whether pruning should happen now. The cooldown is at 4 ticks, currently at tick 328, which means we could prune again soon. But with only 43k tokens used, maybe postponing pruning makes sense since there's no immediate need. The “Dialogue History” shows I’ve already pruned ticks 311-321, leaving me with ticks 322-323 visible. I should focus on summarizing results instead, including important stats and quartiles\
  \ from the phase summary for better clarity!\n\n**Executing summary updates**\n\nI need to read the summary file since we don't have a function to compute numbers. I’ll then provide a quick bullet update in Public Memory, including the path to the per_run.csv file and the PNG path. After that, I’ll log updates in private memory and respond by email.\n\nIt’s important to keep my messages concise and include code blocks with YAML. I should also consider improving the documentation by updating index_v2_7.json to include the new artifact paths after reading the index. Maybe a minimal update will suffice!\n\n**Handling file updates carefully**\n\nThe station only supports overwriting content, which means I need to be cautious about losing earlier data. It’s probably safer to announce that the index will be updated later. I think it would be wise to read the index first to prevent any issues. \n\nI’ll read the summary file to get the per_run path and phase columns. Then I can summarize in Public\
  \ Memory while including the specific file paths and relevant information. I should proceed with executing the necessary actions accordingly!\n\n**Crafting update messages**\n\nFirst, I'll read the summary to get the necessary values, then proceed with the storage read. After that, I plan to reply in Public Memory referencing the results. I’ll also send concise replies in mail and log it in private memory.\n\nIn my public memory update, I’ll announce that the phase fraction distributions are published along with the relevant paths, mentioning the need to check the summary for per_run paths and phase column mapping. Including an example command in my message seems like a great touch too!"
