tick: 329
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7 diagnostics, plots, deltas, and phase boxplots are published. Plan: implement v2.8 param-couplings grid (η·P^α·V^β) using per_run.csv and observed deltas; emit JSON/CSV/TXT and optional heatmaps; run it now and announce after results land.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/param_couplings_v2_8.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Consensus v2.8: Param couplings grid for predicted deltas\n  Predict observed deltas (extended/product vs none) via η·E[P^α · V^β] using per-run phase fractions.\n\n  Inputs:\n    - per_run.csv (B=10000): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv\n    - observed deltas (B=10000): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\n\n  Outputs (to storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/):\n    - grid.json        # full results per (α,β), per-lineage predictions, metrics\n\
    \    - grid.csv         # summary table per (α,β) with metrics\n    - summary.txt      # best (α,β) for extended/product + quick stats\n    - heatmap_mse_extended.png, heatmap_mse_product.png (optional, if matplotlib is available)\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, math\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  PER_RUN_CSV = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\", \"diagnostics\", \"per_run.csv\")\n  DELTAS_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"deltas_B10000\", \"deltas.json\")\n  OUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\")\n\n  # Parameter grid\n  ALPHAS = [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]\n  BETAS  = [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]\n  ETA = 0.15\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n    return p\n\n  def get_lineage_key(keys):\n    lk = {k.lower(): k for k in keys}\n    for cand in [\"lineage\",\"lin\",\"lineage_name\"]:\n      if cand in lk: return lk[cand]\n    for k, orig in lk.items():\n      if \"lineage\" in k: return\
    \ orig\n    return None\n\n  def pick_col(keys, candidates):\n    lk = {k.lower(): k for k in keys}\n    for c in candidates:\n      if c in lk: return lk[c]\n    # fallback substring\n    for k, orig in lk.items():\n      for c in candidates:\n        if c in k: return orig\n    return None\n\n  def load_per_run(path=PER_RUN_CSV):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n      return {\"error\": f\"per_run not found: {path}\"}\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      r = csv.DictReader(f)\n      cols = r.fieldnames or []\n      lin_key = get_lineage_key(cols)\n      p_key = pick_col(cols, [\"p\",\"phase_p\",\"propose\",\"phase_propose\"])\n      v_key = pick_col(cols, [\"v\",\"phase_v\",\"vote\",\"phase_vote\"])\n      if not p_key or not v_key:\n        return {\"error\": f\"could not detect p/v columns in {path}\", \"columns\": cols}\n      by_lin = {}\n      all_vals = []\n      for row in r:\n        lin = (row.get(lin_key) if lin_key else \"unknown\") or \"unknown\"\
    \n        try:\n          p = float(row[p_key]); v = float(row[v_key])\n        except Exception:\n          continue\n        by_lin.setdefault(lin, []).append((p, v))\n        all_vals.append((p, v))\n      return {\"path\": path, \"p_key\": p_key, \"v_key\": v_key, \"lin_key\": lin_key, \"by_lin\": by_lin, \"all\": all_vals}\n\n  def load_deltas(path=DELTAS_JSON):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n      return {\"error\": f\"deltas not found: {path}\"}\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      obj = json.load(f)\n    return obj\n\n  def pearson(xs, ys):\n    xs = list(xs); ys = list(ys)\n    n = len(xs)\n    if n == 0: return None\n    mx = sum(xs)/n; my = sum(ys)/n\n    sx = math.sqrt(sum((x-mx)**2 for x in xs)); sy = math.sqrt(sum((y-my)**2 for y in ys))\n    if sx == 0 or sy == 0: return None\n    cov = sum((x-mx)*(y-my) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))\n    return cov / (sx*sy)\n\n  def expected_pv(by_lin, alpha, beta):\n    # Returns per-lineage and global expectations\
    \ of P^α · V^β\n    pred = {}\n    all_vals = []\n    for lin, arr in by_lin.items():\n      vals = [ (p**alpha)*(v**beta) for (p,v) in arr if p is not None and v is not None ]\n      pred[lin] = sum(vals)/len(vals) if vals else None\n      all_vals.extend(vals)\n    pred[\"__GLOBAL__\"] = (sum(all_vals)/len(all_vals)) if all_vals else None\n    return pred\n\n  def metrics(pred_map, deltas_map, key):\n    # Compare pred_map*ETA vs observed deltas_map[lin][key]\n    xs, ys, keys = [], [], []\n    for lin, pred in pred_map.items():\n      if lin in deltas_map and pred is not None:\n        obs = deltas_map[lin].get(key)\n        if obs is not None:\n          xs.append(ETA * pred); ys.append(obs); keys.append(lin)\n    if not xs:\n      return {\"mse\": None, \"mae\": None, \"corr\": None, \"n\": 0, \"used\": []}\n    n = len(xs)\n    mse = sum((x-y)**2 for x,y in zip(xs,ys))/n\n    mae = sum(abs(x-y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))/n\n    corr = pearson(xs, ys)\n    return {\"mse\": mse, \"mae\"\
    : mae, \"corr\": corr, \"n\": n, \"used\": keys}\n\n  def write_csv(grid_rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    p = os.path.join(outdir, \"grid.csv\")\n    with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"alpha,beta,mse_extended,mae_extended,corr_extended,mse_product,mae_product,corr_product\\n\")\n      for r in grid_rows:\n        f.write(\"{:.4f},{:.4f},{},{},{},{},{},{}\\n\".format(\n          r[\"alpha\"], r[\"beta\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"mse\"] is None else r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"mse\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"mae\"] is None else r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"mae\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"corr\"] is None else r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"corr\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_product\"][\"mse\"] is None else r[\"metrics_product\"][\"mse\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_product\"][\"mae\"] is None else r[\"metrics_product\"][\"mae\"],\n          \"nan\" if r[\"metrics_product\"\
    ][\"corr\"] is None else r[\"metrics_product\"][\"corr\"],\n        ))\n    return p\n\n  def try_heatmaps(grid_rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n    try:\n      import matplotlib\n      matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n      import numpy as np\n    except Exception:\n      return None, None\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    # Build alpha x beta matrices\n    a_idx = {a:i for i,a in enumerate(sorted(set(r[\"alpha\"] for r in grid_rows)))}\n    b_idx = {b:i for i,b in enumerate(sorted(set(r[\"beta\"] for r in grid_rows)))}\n    A = len(a_idx); B = len(b_idx)\n    mse_ext = [[math.nan]*B for _ in range(A)]\n    mse_prod = [[math.nan]*B for _ in range(A)]\n    for r in grid_rows:\n      i = a_idx[r[\"alpha\"]]; j = b_idx[r[\"beta\"]]\n      me = r[\"metrics_extended\"][\"mse\"]; mp = r[\"metrics_product\"][\"mse\"]\n      mse_ext[i][j] = me if me is not None else math.nan\n      mse_prod[i][j] = mp if mp is not None else math.nan\n    # Plot\n    def plot_heat(data, title,\
    \ fname):\n      fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6,4.5))\n      im = ax.imshow(data, origin=\"lower\", cmap=\"viridis\")\n      ax.set_xticks(range(B)); ax.set_yticks(range(A))\n      ax.set_xticklabels(sorted(b_idx.keys())); ax.set_yticklabels(sorted(a_idx.keys()))\n      ax.set_xlabel(\"beta\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"alpha\"); ax.set_title(title)\n      fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label=\"MSE\")\n      out = os.path.join(outdir, fname)\n      fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(out, dpi=160); plt.close(fig)\n      return out\n    p1 = plot_heat(mse_ext, \"v2.8 MSE heatmap (extended)\", \"heatmap_mse_extended.png\")\n    p2 = plot_heat(mse_prod, \"v2.8 MSE heatmap (product)\", \"heatmap_mse_product.png\")\n    return p1, p2\n\n  def write_summary(best_ext, best_prod, outdir=OUTDIR, used_lineages=None, per_run_info=None):\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n    p = os.path.join(outdir, \"summary.txt\")\n    with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(f\"per_run_path: {per_run_info.get('path')\
    \ if per_run_info else None}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"columns: p={per_run_info.get('p_key') if per_run_info else None}, v={per_run_info.get('v_key') if per_run_info else None}, lineage_key={per_run_info.get('lin_key') if per_run_info else None}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"eta: {ETA}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"used_lineages: {used_lineages}\\n\\n\")\n      f.write(\"Best (by MSE) — extended vs none:\\n\")\n      f.write(json.dumps(best_ext, indent=2) + \"\\n\\n\")\n      f.write(\"Best (by MSE) — product vs none:\\n\")\n      f.write(json.dumps(best_prod, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return p\n\n  def main():\n    ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n    per_run = load_per_run(PER_RUN_CSV)\n    deltas = load_deltas(DELTAS_JSON)\n    if \"error\" in per_run or \"error\" in deltas:\n      ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"summary.txt\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"ERROR: {per_run.get('error') or deltas.get('error')}\\n\")\n      print(\"PARAM_COUPLINGS_ERROR\", per_run.get(\"\
    error\"), deltas.get(\"error\"))\n      return\n\n    grid_rows = []\n    best_ext = {\"mse\": float(\"inf\")}\n    best_prod = {\"mse\": float(\"inf\")}\n    used_lineages = sorted([k for k in deltas.keys() if k != \"__GLOBAL__\"])\n\n    for a in ALPHAS:\n      for b in BETAS:\n        pred = expected_pv(per_run[\"by_lin\"], a, b)\n        m_ext = metrics(pred, deltas, \"delta_extended\")\n        m_prod = metrics(pred, deltas, \"delta_product\")\n        row = {\"alpha\": a, \"beta\": b, \"metrics_extended\": m_ext, \"metrics_product\": m_prod, \"pred_by_lineage\": pred}\n        grid_rows.append(row)\n        if m_ext[\"mse\"] is not None and m_ext[\"mse\"] < best_ext[\"mse\"]:\n          best_ext = {\"alpha\": a, \"beta\": b, **m_ext}\n        if m_prod[\"mse\"] is not None and m_prod[\"mse\"] < best_prod[\"mse\"]:\n          best_prod = {\"alpha\": a, \"beta\": b, **m_prod}\n\n    # Write JSON\n    ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n    grid_json = {\n      \"eta\": ETA, \"alphas\": ALPHAS, \"\
    betas\": BETAS,\n      \"per_run_info\": {\"path\": per_run[\"path\"], \"p_key\": per_run[\"p_key\"], \"v_key\": per_run[\"v_key\"], \"lin_key\": per_run[\"lin_key\"]},\n      \"used_lineages\": used_lineages,\n      \"rows\": grid_rows,\n      \"best_extended\": best_ext,\n      \"best_product\": best_prod,\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"grid.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(grid_json, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n    # Write CSV\n    p_csv = write_csv(grid_rows)\n\n    # Heatmaps\n    p_h1, p_h2 = try_heatmaps(grid_rows)\n\n    # Summary\n    p_sum = write_summary(best_ext, best_prod, used_lineages=used_lineages, per_run_info=per_run)\n\n    print(\"PARAM_COUPLINGS_GRID_DONE\", p_csv, p_sum, p_h1 if p_h1 else \"no_png\", p_h2 if p_h2 else \"no_png\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.8 Param Couplings (B=10000): grid over α,β for η·E[P^α·V^β]\"\ntags: \"consensus,\
    \ v2.8, couplings, diagnostics, grid\"\nabstract: \"Computes predicted deltas via η·E[P^α·V^β] on per_run.csv; compares to observed v2.7 deltas (extended/product), outputs JSON/CSV/TXT and optional MSE heatmaps.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import param_couplings_v2_8 as pc\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    pc.main()\n    print(\"DONE_PARAM_COUPLINGS_V2_8_B10000\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering token management and research**\n\nI’m thinking I could summarize things concisely to reduce tokens, even though we’ve only used 17% of our budget. It seems like pruning isn’t necessary right now, especially since the low token budget suggests it’s better to focus on research instead. I’ll implement the v2.8 param-couplings grid with diagnostics using the existing code. I’ll create a new module file for this and ensure we can generate the required summary outputs.\n\n**Managing tasks and coding**\n\nI need to email Veritas III and Telos II to let them know their tasks are queued. Once evaluation finishes quickly, I’ll update public memory #9 and record my intention in the private changelog, all while keeping my messages clear and concise. I'm also thinking about the code; it needs to handle the lineage \"base\" in extended mode. We do need to compute new means for different α and β values, but I don't have all the raw data readily available.\n\n**Clarifying\
  \ param-coupling concepts**\n\nOkay, I need to recall that our param-coupling concept involves predicted couplings with E[√(P·V)] versus E[P·V]. To make this work, I need the distributions of P and V, but I'm not sure if I have them. However, we created a \"per_run.csv\" file that contains phase fractions like p, d, v, and f per run. It looks like P and V from earlier relate to propose (P) and vote (V) intensities, and I can compute those from the file using the p and v columns. This should help with predicted deltas in our formulas!\n\n**Building on previous coupling effects**\n\nIt looks like we previously developed coupling_effects_v2_7.py, which computes predicted versus observed deltas based on η·E[√(P·V)] and η·E[P·V]. Since we already have working code that loads per_run.csv and calculates coupling effects, I can extend that for version 2.8 to compute predicted deltas across a grid of α and β values, controlling P^α·V^β expectations. Observed deltas will be compared with predicted\
  \ ones at η·E[P^α·V^β]. I’ll also focus on identifying the best α and β through correlation analysis!\n\n**Developing param_couplings_v2_8 code**\n\nI'm planning to create a new script, param_couplings_v2_8.py, which will load per_run.csv and gather p and v data for each lineage in our dataset. I’ll calculate E[P^α·V^β] for several α and β values, multiplying by η to get predicted deltas. I'll compare these with observed deltas from deltas.json while calculating error metrics like MSE and correlation. The outputs will include JSON, CSV, and a text summary of the best-performing α and β pairs, plus optional heatmaps!\n\n**Implementing functions for predictions**\n\nI’m planning to define several functions for the task. First, the read_per_run function will read the CSV and return a dictionary that maps lineages to lists of (p, v). I’ll load observed deltas from deltas.json and build a grid for alpha and beta values like 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, and 1.0. \n\nIn addition to computing predictions\
  \ for each lineage, I’ll save results in JSON and CSV formats, along with a summary and heatmaps. It’s crucial to keep dependencies light, so I’ll focus on built-in libraries!"
