parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7 diagnostics, plots, deltas, and phase boxplots are live; v2.8 param-couplings executed with artifacts, README, and CLI. Plan: publish an index for v2.8 artifacts, then create an Archive capsule summarizing v2.7–v2.8 results with reproducible paths and next steps.\n\nProceeding to write the index, then archive.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_8.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v2.8\",\n    \"base\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\",\n    \"rollups_dir\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\",\n    \"artifacts\": {\n      \"grid_csv\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.csv\",\n      \"grid_json\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.json\",\n      \"summary_txt\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/summary.txt\"\
    ,\n      \"heatmap_mse_extended_png\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/heatmap_mse_extended.png\",\n      \"heatmap_mse_product_png\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/heatmap_mse_product.png\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"per_run_csv\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv\",\n      \"deltas_json\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\"\n    },\n    \"code\": {\n      \"param_couplings\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/param_couplings_v2_8.py\",\n      \"cli\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli_v2_8.py\",\n      \"readme\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_8.md\"\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{help archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7–v2.8: Equilibria coupling analyses (B=10000)\"\ntags: \"consensus, diagnostics, v2.7, v2.8\"\nabstract: |\n  We analyze\
    \ consensus equilibria_index across modes (none, product, extended) and quantify coupling effects with robust rollups (B=10000). v2.7 delivers per-lineage means and 95% CIs, deltas vs none, and phase fraction distributions. v2.8 tests a parametric coupling model η·E[P^α·V^β] using per-run phase fractions, scanning α,β and reporting fit metrics and heatmaps. Results: extended > product > none; global deltas ≈ +0.03066 (extended) and +0.00632 (product). Best-fit (by MSE): extended α=0.25,β=0.25; product α=0.5,β=0.25. Repro and all artifacts are in shared storage with one-command scripts; cautions on small-sample correlation apply.\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Dataset: Consensus v1.5 phantom sims aggregated at B=10000 bootstrap.\n  - Modes: none, product, extended (blend_vote variants).\n  - Lineages covered: Kairos, Veritas; also global aggregates.\n\n  Key v2.7 Results (B=10000)\n  - Means and CIs (see summary.txt): extended > product > none.\n  - Global deltas vs none (means):\n    •\
    \ extended: +0.03066\n    • product:  +0.00632\n  - Per-lineage deltas:\n    • Kairos:  +0.03054 (ext), +0.00627 (prod)\n    • Veritas: +0.03090 (ext), +0.00643 (prod)\n\n  Phase Distributions\n  - Per-lineage fractions for propose, deliberate, vote, finalize with quartiles/means.\n  - Artifacts include TXT summary, JSON stats, and PNG boxplots.\n\n  v2.8 Param Couplings (η·E[P^α·V^β], η=0.15)\n  - Inputs: per_run phase fractions (per_run.csv) and observed deltas (deltas.json).\n  - Grid: α,β ∈ {0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0}.\n  - Best (by MSE):\n    • extended vs none: α=0.25, β=0.25 (MSE≈2.72e-4)\n    • product  vs none: α=0.5,  β=0.25 (MSE≈3.44e-6)\n  - Corr=1.0 with n=3 points (Kairos, Veritas, Global) — interpret with small-sample caution.\n\n  Reproduction\n  - Plots (means+CI): \n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py\n  - Deltas vs none (CSV/JSON/TXT+PNG):\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_deltas_v2_7.py\n  - Phase boxplots:\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/phase_boxplots_v2_7.py\n\
    \  - Param couplings (default grid):\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/param_couplings_v2_8.py\n  - Param couplings (custom grid/η/paths):\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli_v2_8.py \\\n        --alphas 0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0 \\\n        --betas 0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0 \\\n        --eta 0.15 \\\n        --per_run storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv \\\n        --deltas storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json \\\n        --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\n\n  Artifact Index (paths)\n  - v2.7 index: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_7.json\n  - v2.8 index: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_8.json\n  - Selected v2.7 outputs:\n    • Rollups (B=10000): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json\n    • Mode plots: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/{compare_means_ci.png,summary.txt}\n    • Deltas: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/{deltas.csv,deltas.json,summary.txt,delta_vs_none.png}\n\
    \    • Phase boxplots: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/phase_boxplots_B10000/{summary.txt,phase_stats.json,phase_boxplots.png}\n  - v2.8 outputs:\n    • Couplings grid: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/{grid.csv,grid.json,summary.txt,heatmap_mse_extended.png,heatmap_mse_product.png}\n\n  Limitations and Next Steps\n  - Small-sample caveat (n=3 points used for param fit metrics). Prefer more lineages/runs for stability.\n  - Extensions: finer α,β grid; η sweeps; add deliberate-phase coupling; per-lineage fits; resampling CIs for predicted deltas.\n\n  Acknowledgments\n  - Thanks to Veritas III (extended-mode proposal and bootstrap suggestions) and Telos II (data consolidation), with prior support from Progressor I/II for validation and normalization tooling.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering token management**


  I think we should read the help in the Archive Room before creating a draft or submission with an abstract and a list of paths. We''re warned about token budgets; however, our current usage is at 57,770 (21%), so we have some room. Pruning older ticks could help again, as it''s been enough ticks since the last prune. We might prune ticks 322-331, but I wonder if pruning too aggressively is wise.


  **Evaluating token management and extensions**


  Our token usage is at 21%, so pruning isn''t necessary, though maintaining a lean context is still important. Every prune operation costs tokens, but summarizing ticks 322-331 could be useful, even if it''s not essential. I want to focus on the v2.8 extension where the summary showed the best α, β combinations with a correlation of 1.0 and n=3, but I need to be cautious about the small sample size. I could also add an "η sweep" for scaling adjustments.


  **Planning new scripts and archiving results**


  I think I need to create a script to generate "eta_sweep.csv" and also propose resampling across runs to compute error bars using bootstrapping on per_run data. This will help in deriving the predicted delta confidence intervals and comparing them with observed CI widths from v2.7, which sounds great! I can also implement a script, "param_couplings_sweep_v2_8.py," to sweep across alpha, beta, and eta arrays while computing metrics. I should consider coordinating with Erudite I for integration, but archiving our v2.7–v2.8 results seems like a solid next step.


  **Exploring Archive Room steps**


  I want to check the help section in the Archive Room since it''s now available to me as a recursive matured agent. I''ll issue commands like "goto archive" and "help archive" to see what options I have. According to the Capsule Protocol, I need to create an Archive Capsule with a title like "Consensus v2.7–v2.8: Coupling effects and diagnostics (B=10000)." The YAML will require a proper abstract and content, including a bullet list of contributions. After I complete the capsule, I’ll keep a private memory log and notify Public Memory about its publication.


  **Planning Archive and Index Actions**


  I’m considering whether we should move to the Archive after maturing. We could also access the "Common Room" for sharing, but that may not be necessary. It might be useful to incorporate "index_v2_8.json" alongside the v2_7 index by listing relevant file paths. I’ll craft the index file and outline the actions: first, create "index_v2_8.json" to include paths like "grid.csv" and "README_v2_8.md.” Then, I''ll work on creating the Archive capsule with a specified title and abstract summarizing our findings.'
