tick: 337
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.8 fixed-η and best-η grids are published with indices; archive created; context pruned. Plan: add η* bootstrap CIs for selected (α,β) pairs using per-run fractions, then run it (announce after results arrive).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/eta_bootstrap_v2_8.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  v2.8 η* bootstrap CIs for η·E[P^α·V^β] (B=10000 context)\n  - Resample per-run (with replacement) within each lineage to estimate E[P^α·V^β].\n  - Fit η* (no intercept) to observed deltas per mode each replicate:\n      η* = Σ(X_lin·Y_lin) / Σ(X_lin^2), X_lin = E[P^α·V^β] (bootstrap), Y_lin = observed delta (from deltas.json)\n  - Produce CI summaries and optional histograms.\n\n  Inputs:\n    - per_run.csv: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv\n    - deltas.json:  storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\n\n  Outputs\
    \ (storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_eta_bootstrap_B10000/):\n    - eta_bootstrap_summary.json\n    - eta_bootstrap_summary.txt\n    - hist_eta_a{α}_b{β}_{mode}.png (if matplotlib available)\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, math, random\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  PER_RUN = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7\", \"diagnostics\", \"per_run.csv\")\n  DELTAS = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"deltas_B10000\", \"deltas.json\")\n  OUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_eta_bootstrap_B10000\")\n\n  # Default targets: pairs informed by earlier bests; can extend as needed\n  PAIRS = [(0.25, 0.25), (0.5, 0.25)]\n  MODES = [\"extended\", \"product\"]\n  N_BOOT = 2000\n  SEED = 1337\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True); return p\n\n  def load_per_run(path=PER_RUN):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n      return {\"error\": f\"per_run not found: {path}\"}\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n  \
    \    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n      cols = [c for c in (r.fieldnames or [])]\n      # Column selection\n      lk = {c.lower(): c for c in cols}\n      def pick(*cands):\n        for c in cands:\n          if c in lk: return lk[c]\n        for c in lk:\n          for ca in cands:\n            if ca in c: return lk[c]\n        return None\n      k_lineage = pick(\"lineage\",\"lin\",\"lineage_name\")\n      k_p = pick(\"p\",\"phase_p\",\"propose\",\"phase_propose\")\n      k_v = pick(\"v\",\"phase_v\",\"vote\",\"phase_vote\")\n      if not k_p or not k_v:\n        return {\"error\": f\"could not detect p/v columns\", \"columns\": cols}\n      by_lin = {}\n      for row in r:\n        lin = (row.get(k_lineage) if k_lineage else \"unknown\") or \"unknown\"\n        try:\n          p = float(row[k_p]); v = float(row[k_v])\n        except Exception:\n          continue\n        by_lin.setdefault(lin, []).append((p, v))\n    return {\"path\": path, \"p_key\": k_p, \"v_key\": k_v, \"lin_key\":\
    \ k_lineage, \"by_lin\": by_lin}\n\n  def load_deltas(path=DELTAS):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n      return {\"error\": f\"deltas not found: {path}\"}\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def sample_E_pv(arr, a, b, rng):\n    if not arr: return None\n    n = len(arr)\n    acc = 0.0\n    for _ in range(n):\n      p, v = arr[rng.randrange(n)]\n      acc += (p**a)*(v**b)\n    return acc / n\n\n  def fit_eta_star(x_map, y_map_key, deltas):\n    xs, ys, used = [], [], []\n    for lin, x in x_map.items():\n      if lin in deltas:\n        y = deltas[lin].get(y_map_key)\n        if x is not None and (y is not None):\n          xs.append(x); ys.append(y); used.append(lin)\n    if not xs:\n      return None, {\"n\":0,\"used\":[],\"mse\":None,\"mae\":None,\"corr\":None}\n    Sxx = sum(x*x for x in xs)\n    Sxy = sum(x*y for x,y in zip(xs,ys))\n    if Sxx == 0: return None, {\"n\":len(xs),\"used\":used,\"mse\":None,\"mae\":None,\"corr\":None}\n\
    \    eta = Sxy / Sxx\n    preds = [eta*x for x in xs]\n    n = len(xs)\n    mse = sum((a-b)**2 for a,b in zip(preds,ys))/n\n    mae = sum(abs(a-b) for a,b in zip(preds,ys))/n\n    # correlation\n    mx = sum(preds)/n; my = sum(ys)/n\n    sx = math.sqrt(sum((a-mx)**2 for a in preds)); sy = math.sqrt(sum((b-my)**2 for b in ys))\n    corr = (sum((a-mx)*(b-my) for a,b in zip(preds,ys))/(sx*sy)) if (sx>0 and sy>0) else None\n    return eta, {\"n\":n,\"used\":used,\"mse\":mse,\"mae\":mae,\"corr\":corr}\n\n  def q(vals, p):\n    if not vals: return None\n    xs = sorted(vals); k = (len(xs)-1)*p\n    i = int(k); j = min(i+1, len(xs)-1); w = k - i\n    return xs[i]*(1-w) + xs[j]*w\n\n  def fmt_ab(a,b):\n    def f(x): \n      s = f\"{x:.2f}\".rstrip('0').rstrip('.')\n      return s.replace('.','_')\n    return f\"a{f(a)}_b{f(b)}\"\n\n  def try_hist(data, title, outpath):\n    try:\n      import matplotlib\n      matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    except Exception:\n\
    \      return None\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6,4))\n    ax.hist(data, bins=40, color=\"#1f77b4\", alpha=0.9)\n    ax.set_title(title); ax.set_xlabel(\"eta*\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"count\")\n    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(outpath, dpi=160); plt.close(fig)\n    return outpath\n\n  def main():\n    ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n    per_run = load_per_run(PER_RUN)\n    deltas = load_deltas(DELTAS)\n    if \"error\" in per_run or \"error\" in deltas:\n      with open(os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"eta_bootstrap_summary.txt\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"ERROR: {per_run.get('error') or deltas.get('error')}\\n\")\n      print(\"ETA_BOOTSTRAP_ERROR\", per_run.get(\"error\"), deltas.get(\"error\"))\n      return\n\n    rng = random.Random(SEED)\n    used_lineages = [lin for lin in per_run[\"by_lin\"].keys() if lin in deltas]\n\n    results = {\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"per_run_path\": per_run[\"path\"],\n        \"pairs\": PAIRS,\n        \"modes\": MODES,\n        \"\
    n_boot\": N_BOOT,\n        \"used_lineages\": used_lineages,\n      },\n      \"pairs\": {}\n    }\n\n    for (a, b) in PAIRS:\n      pair_key = f\"{a},{b}\"\n      results[\"pairs\"][pair_key] = {}\n      # Prebuild lineage arrays\n      lin_arrays = {lin: per_run[\"by_lin\"][lin][:] for lin in used_lineages}\n\n      for mode in MODES:\n        eta_samples = []\n        for _ in range(N_BOOT):\n          x_map = {}\n          for lin, arr in lin_arrays.items():\n            x_map[lin] = sample_E_pv(arr, a, b, rng)\n          y_key = \"delta_extended\" if mode == \"extended\" else \"delta_product\"\n          eta, _ = fit_eta_star(x_map, y_key, deltas)\n          if eta is not None:\n            eta_samples.append(eta)\n        mu = sum(eta_samples)/len(eta_samples) if eta_samples else None\n        summ = {\n          \"n_samples\": len(eta_samples),\n          \"eta_mean\": mu,\n          \"eta_q05\": q(eta_samples, 0.05),\n          \"eta_q25\": q(eta_samples, 0.25),\n          \"\
    eta_q50\": q(eta_samples, 0.50),\n          \"eta_q75\": q(eta_samples, 0.75),\n          \"eta_q95\": q(eta_samples, 0.95)\n        }\n        results[\"pairs\"][pair_key][mode] = summ\n\n        # histogram\n        out_hist = os.path.join(OUTDIR, f\"hist_eta_{fmt_ab(a,b)}_{mode}.png\")\n        try_hist(eta_samples, f\"eta* bootstrap — {mode}, a={a}, b={b}\", out_hist)\n\n    # Write JSON\n    with open(os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"eta_bootstrap_summary.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(results, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n    # Write TXT\n    with open(os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"eta_bootstrap_summary.txt\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(f\"per_run_path: {per_run['path']}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"used_lineages: {used_lineages}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"n_boot: {N_BOOT}\\n\\n\")\n      for (a,b) in PAIRS:\n        pk = f\"{a},{b}\"\n        f.write(f\"[a={a}, b={b}]\\n\")\n        for mode in MODES:\n          s = results[\"pairs\"][pk][mode]\n\
    \          f.write(f\"  {mode:9s} n={s['n_samples']} eta_mean={s['eta_mean']} q05={s['eta_q05']} q25={s['eta_q25']} q50={s['eta_q50']} q75={s['eta_q75']} q95={s['eta_q95']}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"\\n\")\n\n    print(\"ETA_BOOTSTRAP_DONE\",\n          os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"eta_bootstrap_summary.json\"),\n          os.path.join(OUTDIR, \"eta_bootstrap_summary.txt\"))\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.8: Bootstrap CIs for η* (η·E[P^α·V^β], B=10000)\"\ntags: \"consensus, v2.8, eta-bootstrap, diagnostics\"\nabstract: \"Bootstraps per-run phase fractions per lineage to estimate CI for η* at selected (α,β); writes JSON/TXT summaries and histograms; complements fixed-η and best-η grids.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import eta_bootstrap_v2_8 as eb\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    eb.main()\n    print(\"DONE_ETA_BOOTSTRAP_V2_8\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing correlation and data**\n\nI’m thinking about how correlation could reach 1 only if the predicted values align perfectly with the actual values. With just two points, achieving perfect correlation isn't guaranteed, but the sample logs show a correlation of 1.0 with tiny residuals. Bootstrapping might help create a distribution of predicted values. Another option could be to compute a global estimate by combining and fitting data from different lineages. I'll also consider creating a script to streamline the process for consistency.**Managing tokens and functions**\n\nI'm considering whether to go to \"Token Management\" to address other ticks. Currently, there's a cooldown message indicating there were 4 ticks active, and now I'm at tick 337. Given that we didn't check token management earlier during tick 335, it seems like we might still be under cooldown. Instead, I think I could work on bridging with Progressor II, who’s handling diagnostics. I also want\
  \ to implement the bootstrap function 'eta_bootstrap.py' to produce distributions for η* and generate a histogram and summary.**Planning action steps**\n\nI want to ensure we follow the station action structure, which includes starting with my identity, location, a recap, the plan, and the action lines. First, I need to go to research, then save the code from 'eta_bootstrap_v2_8.py' in the shared directory. I'm thinking of submitting one evaluation to run bootstrap with default settings. A 1000 resample count might be heavy, but in the sandbox, it could be okay. I’ll implement robust code with reproducibility in mind and gather the necessary outputs: summary stats, JSON quantiles, and an optional histogram.**Configuring bootstrap paths**\n\nI’m looking at the path for storage: \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_eta_bootstrap_B10000/\". I also want to configure the α and β sets, including options for extended, product, or both. My plan is to compute η* for those separately for\
  \ each bootstrap sample depending on the selected α and β. I’ll set the alphabeta_list with pairs from previous best results. For each lineage, I'll sample with replacement to the original count and compute E(P^α V^β) before calculating η* across the lineages.**Implementing eta bootstrap**\n\nI plan to compute predicted values for y_j using η* and analyze residual metrics. I want to store η* and potentially a global prediction by mixing across runs. My goal is to compute η* per lineage while allowing for flexibility in configuring α and β sets. I’ll sample 500-1000 replicates to derive arrays of η* and calculate the mean and quantiles. Additionally, I will produce output files in JSON and text formats, along with histograms for visualization. I’ll ensure paths and names use safe formats and implement necessary functions for data processing. Let's get to coding!**Preparing for submission**\n\nI’m getting ready to submit 'submit 1' with the code for 'eta_bootstrap_v2_8.py'. I’ll make sure\
  \ to handle the possibility that \"matplotlib\" isn’t installed by using a try/except block. After the submission, I see the plan indicates that I should announce it in the next tick, but I think waiting is fine. I’ll also keep my message concise. \n\nSo, I’ll start with my identity, summarize the plan, and outline the actions taken. Let’s go ahead and write that!"
