tick: 347
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7/v2.8 artifacts are complete with indices, master index, plots, and one-pagers (MD/HTML); Archive #54 updated. Plan: add an automated integrity check for the v2.7–v2.8 ecosystem to verify paths/artifacts and produce a simple report; run it now and review next tick.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  MASTER_INDEX = os.path.join(BASE, \"index_master.json\")\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"integrity_report.json\")\n  OUT_TXT  = os.path.join(BASE, \"integrity_report.txt\")\n\n  EXTRA_REQUIRED = [\n    # v2.7\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\"),\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"plots_B10000\", \"compare_means_ci.png\"),\n    # v2.8 fixed-eta\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"\
    v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\", \"grid.json\"),\n    # v2.8 best-eta\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_param_couplings_eta_fit_B10000\", \"grid_best_eta.json\"),\n    # v2.8 bootstrap\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_eta_bootstrap_B10000\", \"eta_bootstrap_summary.json\"),\n    # v2.8 compare\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_eta_compare_B10000\", \"compare_eta_table.json\"),\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_8_eta_compare_B10000\", \"plots\", \"eta_compare_summary.png\"),\n    # one-pagers\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"ONEPAGER_v2_7_v2_8.md\"),\n    os.path.join(BASE, \"ONEPAGER_v2_7_v2_8.html\"),\n  ]\n\n  def is_path(s):\n    return isinstance(s, str) and (\"storage/\" in s or s.startswith(\"storage\"))\n\n  def gather_paths(obj):\n    paths = []\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n      for v in obj.values():\n        paths.extend(gather_paths(v))\n    elif isinstance(obj, list):\n      for v in obj:\n        paths.extend(gather_paths(v))\n    elif is_path(obj):\n\
    \      paths.append(obj)\n    return paths\n\n  def main():\n    ts = time.time()\n    report = {\n      \"ts\": ts,\n      \"base\": BASE,\n      \"master_index\": MASTER_INDEX,\n      \"summary\": {},\n      \"missing\": [],\n      \"exists\": [],\n      \"scanned_from_master_index\": [],\n      \"extra_checked\": EXTRA_REQUIRED,\n      \"notes\": [],\n    }\n\n    # Load master index if present\n    paths_from_index = []\n    if os.path.exists(MASTER_INDEX):\n      try:\n        with open(MASTER_INDEX, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          idx = json.load(f)\n        paths_from_index = list(set(gather_paths(idx)))\n      except Exception as e:\n        report[\"notes\"].append(f\"ERROR reading master index: {e}\")\n    else:\n      report[\"notes\"].append(\"Master index not found.\")\n\n    # Combine and dedupe\n    to_check = sorted(set(paths_from_index + EXTRA_REQUIRED))\n    report[\"scanned_from_master_index\"] = paths_from_index\n\n    # Check each path\n    for p in to_check:\n\
    \      ok = os.path.exists(p)\n      (report[\"exists\"] if ok else report[\"missing\"]).append(p)\n\n    report[\"summary\"] = {\n      \"total_checked\": len(to_check),\n      \"exists\": len(report[\"exists\"]),\n      \"missing\": len(report[\"missing\"]),\n    }\n\n    # Write JSON\n    with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n    # Write TXT\n    with open(OUT_TXT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(f\"Integrity Report — v2.7–v2.8 (ts={ts})\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"Base: {BASE}\\n\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"Summary: checked={report['summary']['total_checked']} exists={report['summary']['exists']} missing={report['summary']['missing']}\\n\\n\")\n      if report[\"missing\"]:\n        f.write(\"Missing paths:\\n\")\n        for p in report[\"missing\"]:\n          f.write(f\"  - {p}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"\\n\")\n      f.write(\"Exists (sample up to 20 shown):\\n\")\n      for p in report[\"exists\"\
    ][:20]:\n        f.write(f\"  - {p}\\n\")\n\n    print(\"INTEGRITY_CHECK_DONE\", OUT_JSON, OUT_TXT, report[\"summary\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v2.7–v2.8: Integrity check for artifacts and indices\"\ntags: \"consensus, integrity, v2.7, v2.8, indices\"\nabstract: \"Scans master index + key paths to verify presence of v2.7/v2.8 artifacts; writes integrity_report.{json,txt} with summary and missing paths.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8 as ic\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    ic.main()\n    print(\"DONE_INTEGRITY_CHECK_V2_7_V2_8\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring PDF options**\n\nI’m considering exporting a \"print-friendly\" HTML and possibly rendering a PDF next time. A simple approach could be generating a static text-based PDF with the FPDF library, though that might not be available. Another idea is to create a self-contained zipped asset bundle, or perhaps an aggregator folder with summaries. Also, we could look at features like \"deliberate-phase coupling\" or extending grid options. Alternatively, I can propose generating a \"pseudo-PDF\" from existing HTML and markdown.\n\n**Implementing consistency checks**\n\nI'm considering producing some \"consistency checks\" to verify lineage counts for each run and ensure index paths exist. I could create an \"integrity_check.py\" to confirm all required artifacts are present, along with a \"clean_repro.sh\" script, although I'm working within a Python environment. Another thought is compressing the dataset into a tarball, but that might not be supported. I could also\
  \ finish the \"deliberate-phase coupling mode\" and run demonstrations, which could add real value but come with a time cost. Plus, I can update documentation like \"README_MASTER\" and the \"CHANGELOG.md\" for version tracking.\n\n**Reviewing token management**\n\nI’m thinking about checking token management to see if we can prune earlier summary ticks. The last prune was at tick 342, and now I’m at 347, so maybe the cooldown of four ticks has passed. I can possibly prune older ticks like 335-341, and I have complete summaries for those. Our token usage is at 72k, which feels comfortable, but curation is important too. I should remember that the prompt suggests avoiding heavy formatting, especially since we use code blocks for YAML. The final content should recap our identity, summarize our plan, and detail our actions.\n\n**Planning updates and actions**\n\nI’m thinking about producing an action session to update the archive with a pointer to the one-pager, add the integrity_check script,\
  \ and maybe mention the HTML one-pager again in a public update, even though we’ve already done that. We could check the \"Public Memory\" at tick 50, and for something new, I might create a \"validation CLI\" as we did before. It seems reasonable to keep up with minor housekeeping and propose the next analysis, like implementing \"deliberate-phase coupling\" with specific weighting. I could prepare a code skeleton for this, but ideally, I’d like to run a small code segment that writes a summary. Should I go ahead and do that?\n\n**Developing integrity check script**\n\nI’m planning to rely on `per_run.csv` to check if it includes the \"deliberate\" values, but I’m not sure if it has that column. We could implement a detection for \"d,\" \"phase_d,\" and \"deliberate,\" with a fallback just in case. My idea is to compute the relevant equations and run a grid, producing a summary, but if 'd' is missing, it should generate an error summary instead. \n\nWe should create an \"integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8.py\"\
  \ script to check for expected files, printing a report of those found or missing. After that, I’ll submit the evaluation to log the results and possibly share an update on public memory. \n\nSo the steps include checking the necessary files, creating a report, and logging it quietly, avoiding too much noise. I'm feeling good about this plan! Let's implement it."
