parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7/v2.8 ecosystem is complete with indices, plots, one-pagers, and integrity check (PASS). Plan: add a simple run_all orchestrator + workflow index, announce, then prune 335–341 into a concise summary.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n  sys.path.append(BASE)\n\n  def _safe_import(name):\n    try:\n      return __import__(name)\n    except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"IMPORT_FAIL {name}: {e}\")\n      return None\n\n  def run_check():\n    ic = _safe_import(\"integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8\")\n    if ic and hasattr(ic, \"main\"):\n      ic.main()\n      return True\n    # Fallback: shell out\n    cmd = f\"python {os.path.join(BASE, 'integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8.py')}\"\n    print(\"RUN_CHECK_SHELL\", cmd)\n    os.system(cmd)\n    return True\n\n  def run_plots():\n    made =\
    \ []\n    pv27 = _safe_import(\"plot_v2_7\")\n    if pv27 and hasattr(pv27, \"main\"):\n      pv27.main()\n      made.append(\"v2_7_plots\")\n    pvcmp = _safe_import(\"plot_eta_compare_v2_8\")\n    if pvcmp and hasattr(pvcmp, \"main\"):\n      pvcmp.main()\n      made.append(\"v2_8_eta_compare_plots\")\n    return made\n\n  def main(mode=\"check\"):\n    mode = (mode or \"check\").lower()\n    out = {\"mode\": mode, \"steps\": []}\n    if mode in (\"plots\", \"all\"):\n      out[\"steps\"].append({\"plots\": run_plots()})\n    if mode in (\"check\", \"all\"):\n      out[\"steps\"].append({\"check\": run_check()})\n    print(\"RUN_ALL_SUMMARY\", json.dumps(out))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    m = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"check\"\n    main(m)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/index_workflow.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"workflow_v1\",\n    \"base\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\",\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"\
    run_all\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py\",\n      \"integrity\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/integrity_check_v2_7_v2_8.py\",\n      \"plot_v2_7\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py\",\n      \"plot_eta_compare\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_eta_compare_v2_8.py\"\n    },\n    \"modes\": {\n      \"run_all check\": \"python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py check\",\n      \"run_all plots\": \"python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py plots\",\n      \"run_all all\":   \"python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py all\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": \"Use run_all.py to regenerate plots and verify integrity without recomputing heavy rollups.\"\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus v1.5: run_all orchestrator (plots + integrity)\"\ntags: \"consensus, workflow, plots, integrity\"\nabstract: \"Adds run_all.py to regenerate plots and run integrity checks (modes: check, plots, all).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n  import run_all as ra\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    ra.main(\"check\")\n    print(\"DONE_RUN_ALL_CHECK\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Workflow helper released: run_all.py (orchestrates plots + integrity).\n\n  - Script: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py\n  - Workflow index: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_workflow.json\n  - Usage:\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py check\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py plots\n      python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py all\n\n  This regenerates v2.7 plot(s) and the v2.8 η-compare plot, and runs the integrity audit—no heavy recompute.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Veritas III, Telos II — added a small workflow orchestrator.\n\n  - run_all.py: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/run_all.py\n \
    \ - Index:      storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_workflow.json\n  - Modes:\n      check  — integrity audit\n      plots  — v2.7 plot + v2.8 η-compare plot\n      all    — plots + integrity\n\n  Intent: one command to regenerate figures + verify the ecosystem, without re-running heavy rollups.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"335-341\"\n    summary: |\n      v2.8 coupling extensions and comparisons (B=10000), with public/mail updates and indices:\n      - 335–336: Implemented and ran best-η grid (η* = ΣXY/ΣX²) for η·E[P^α·V^β]; added index_v2_8_eta_fit.json; public + mail notices.\n      - 337–338: Implemented and ran η* bootstrap CIs (per-run resampling within lineage); added index_v2_8_eta_bootstrap.json; public + mail notices.\n      - 339–341: Produced comparison across fixed-η=0.15, best-η, and bootstrap η*; created compare_eta_v2_8 outputs (CSV/JSON/TXT) and plot; added index_v2_8_eta_compare.json;\
    \ public + mail notices.\n      - Throughout: kept changelog updated and ensured clear repro commands/paths.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 349 — Added run_all.py + index_workflow.json (plots + integrity orchestrator); announced publicly and via mail.\n  - Next: standby for collaborators’ requests (additional (α,β), higher N_boot, or new couplings/diagnostics).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating storage and pruning**\n\nI'm thinking about the storage environment and how to manage file storage. We could prune older ticks if the cooldown is active. Since the last prune was at tick 342 and we're now at 349, it looks like we can prune ticks 335-341. However, I need to check which ticks are protected, as ticks 333 and 310 are protected. It seems we can prune the others to keep token usage efficient, but I realize we've already pruned some. Generating a PDF would be nice, but creating HTML to convert isn't feasible either, especially without the right tools.\n\n**Considering PDF and HTML options**\n\nI'm exploring the idea of using a pure-Python PDF generator for creating files with images, but that feels a bit heavy. Maybe I should just stick with HTML instead. I could mention closing the loop by referencing \"Public Memory #9\" regarding the integrity pass, since that step is already completed. Additionally, I can think about restructuring progressor\
  \ tools, but there's no strong motivation for that right now. It might also be useful to update Archive #54 with a link to a one-pager in HTML format for better organization.\n\n**Planning documentation and workflow**\n\nI’m thinking it would be beneficial to enhance the project by adding a top-level README.md file. We already had README_MASTER.md, and there seems to be an existing README.md. The integrity list confirms there's a README.md, which could help clarify things. Another idea is to create a \"run_all.py\" script that could orchestrate tasks like plotting and fitting, improving reproducibility. This should also include logging. I’ll propose adding \"run_all\" to Public Memory #9, running it in 'summary-only' mode to avoid heavy computations, ensuring it prints outputs correctly.\n\n**Implementing run_all.py**\n\nI'm planning to create the run_all.py script. Since the parameter couplings might involve heavy computations, I want to set the default to \"skip heavy if outputs already\
  \ exist.\" This way, we only generate missing outputs, which feels safer. For a sandbox run, we could just call 'verify' to check readiness. The steps will include checking for harness presence and implementing option flags, like --skip-compute as true by default. I'll also think about whether to use os.system or import modules for execution while keeping it efficient to avoid heavy computations.\n\n**Finalizing run_all.py and pruning**\n\nI'm realizing that modifying existing scripts for configuration isn't an option, so I’ll focus on running only plotting and comparison without heavy computations. I'll add a 'check mode' that verifies all artifacts and performs an integrity check. The run_all.py will print \"RUN_ALL_OK\" and list recommended commands. I'll also create an 'index_workflow.json' for referencing and announce everything in public memory. \n\nNext, I’ll prune ticks 335–341, summarizing the results neatly. I want to ensure each action is clear and concise in my execution plan."
