tick: 356
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Delivered erudite_bridge; Erudite I provided samples at storage/shared/erudite/runs/{819,822,824}.json and requested a sanity run and optional internal η·E[P^α·V^β] support. Plan: extend the bridge to optionally compute weight from (P,V,α,β,η), run a sanity annex over the three samples (with a simple baseline and placeholder weight=0.33), publish an annex index, announce, mail, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/erudite_bridge/adapter.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, math, time\n  from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n  EPS = 1e-12\n\n  def _ensure_dir(p: str) -> str:\n    d = os.path.dirname(p)\n    if d: os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n    return p\n\n  def _load_json(path: str) -> Dict:\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def _to_pdf(bins: List[float], counts: List[float]) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n\
    \    total = float(sum(max(0.0, c) for c in counts))\n    if total <= 0.0:\n      return bins, [0.0 for _ in counts]\n    return bins, [max(0.0, c) / total for c in counts]\n\n  def _kl(p: List[float], q: List[float]) -> float:\n    s = 0.0\n    for pi, qi in zip(p, q):\n      pi = max(pi, EPS); qi = max(qi, EPS)\n      s += pi * math.log(pi / qi)\n    return s\n\n  def js_divergence(p: List[float], q: List[float]) -> float:\n    m = [(pi + qi) * 0.5 for pi, qi in zip(p, q)]\n    return 0.5 * _kl(p, m) + 0.5 * _kl(q, m)\n\n  def _loglog_tail_alpha(bins: List[float], counts: List[float], tail_start_bin: Optional[float]) -> Optional[float]:\n    if tail_start_bin is None:\n      return None\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    for x, c in zip(bins, counts):\n      if x is None or c is None: continue\n      if x >= tail_start_bin and c > 0:\n        try:\n          xs.append(math.log(float(x)))\n          ys.append(math.log(float(c)))\n        except Exception:\n          continue\n    n = len(xs)\n\
    \    if n < 2:\n      return None\n    mean_x = sum(xs) / n\n    mean_y = sum(ys) / n\n    num = sum((xi - mean_x) * (yi - mean_y) for xi, yi in zip(xs, ys))\n    den = sum((xi - mean_x) ** 2 for xi in xs)\n    if den <= 0:\n      return None\n    slope = num / den  # counts ~ x^slope\n    alpha = max(0.0, -slope - 1.0)\n    return alpha\n\n  def coupling_weight(eta: Optional[float]=None, alpha: Optional[float]=None, beta: Optional[float]=None,\n                      P: Optional[List[float]]=None, V: Optional[List[float]]=None, pv_mean: Optional[float]=None) -> Optional[float]:\n    if eta is None:\n      return pv_mean\n    if pv_mean is None:\n      if P is None or V is None or alpha is None or beta is None:\n        return eta\n      n = min(len(P), len(V))\n      if n == 0:\n        return eta\n      acc = 0.0\n      for i in range(n):\n        try:\n          acc += (max(P[i], 0.0) ** float(alpha)) * (max(V[i], 0.0) ** float(beta))\n        except Exception:\n          continue\n\
    \      pv_mean = acc / n\n    return float(eta) * float(pv_mean)\n\n  def _maybe_load_pv(pv_json_path: Optional[str]):\n    if not pv_json_path:\n      return None, None, None\n    try:\n      data = _load_json(pv_json_path)\n      return data.get(\"P\"), data.get(\"V\"), data.get(\"pv_mean\")\n    except Exception:\n      return None, None, None\n\n  def process_file(json_path: str,\n                   baseline_path: Optional[str]=None,\n                   out_dir: str=\"storage/shared/erudite_bridge\",\n                   tail_start_bin: Optional[float]=None,\n                   weight: Optional[float]=None,\n                   eta: Optional[float]=None,\n                   alpha: Optional[float]=None,\n                   beta: Optional[float]=None,\n                   pv_json: Optional[str]=None) -> Dict:\n    data = _load_json(json_path)\n    bins = list(map(float, data.get(\"hist_bins\", [])))\n    counts = list(map(float, data.get(\"hist_counts\", [])))\n    if len(bins) != len(counts)\
    \ or len(bins) == 0:\n      raise ValueError(f\"hist_bins/hist_counts malformed in {json_path}\")\n\n    _, p = _to_pdf(bins, counts)\n    jsd = None\n    if baseline_path:\n      b = _load_json(baseline_path)\n      bb = list(map(float, b.get(\"hist_bins\", [])))\n      bc = list(map(float, b.get(\"hist_counts\", [])))\n      m = min(len(bb), len(bc), len(bins))\n      if m >= 1:\n        _, q = _to_pdf(bb[:m], bc[:m])\n        jsd = js_divergence(p[:m], q)\n\n    alpha_tail = _loglog_tail_alpha(bins, counts, tail_start_bin)\n\n    w = weight\n    if w is None:\n      P, V, pv_mean = _maybe_load_pv(pv_json)\n      w = coupling_weight(eta=eta, alpha=alpha, beta=beta, P=P, V=V, pv_mean=pv_mean)\n\n    novelty_weighted = (jsd * w) if (jsd is not None and w is not None) else None\n\n    result = {\n      \"run_id\": data.get(\"run_id\"),\n      \"std\": data.get(\"std\"),\n      \"tail_alpha\": alpha_tail,\n      \"js_divergence\": jsd,\n      \"coupling_weight\": w,\n      \"novelty_weighted\"\
    : novelty_weighted,\n      \"meta\": data.get(\"meta\") or {}\n    }\n\n    ts = int(time.time())\n    batch = f\"batch_{ts}\"\n    log_dir = os.path.join(out_dir, \"logs\")\n    sum_dir = os.path.join(out_dir, \"summaries\")\n    _ensure_dir(os.path.join(log_dir, \"x\"))\n    _ensure_dir(os.path.join(sum_dir, \"x\"))\n    jsonl_path = os.path.join(log_dir, f\"{batch}.jsonl\")\n    with open(jsonl_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n      fout.write(json.dumps(result) + \"\\n\")\n    sum_path = os.path.join(sum_dir, f\"{batch}.json\")\n    summ = {\"batch\": batch, \"last_file\": json_path, \"last_result\": result}\n    with open(sum_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(summ, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    print(\"ERUDITE_BRIDGE_OK\", jsonl_path, sum_path, result.get(\"run_id\"))\n    return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/erudite_bridge/cli.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, argparse, glob, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/erudite_bridge')\n\
    \  import adapter as A\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--inputs\", required=True, help=\"Path to a JSON file or a directory of *.json\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--baseline\", default=None, help=\"Baseline JSON (bins+counts) for divergence\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", default=\"storage/shared/erudite_bridge\", help=\"Output directory\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--tail_start_bin\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Tail start bin threshold (numeric)\")\n    # Weight options\n    ap.add_argument(\"--weight\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Numeric coupling weight (eta*E[P^a V^b])\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--eta\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Eta for internal coupling computation\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Alpha exponent for P\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--beta\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Beta exponent for V\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--pv_json\", default=None, help=\"JSON with arrays\
    \ P, V, or scalar pv_mean\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    paths = []\n    if os.path.isdir(args.inputs):\n      paths = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(args.inputs, \"*.json\")))\n    elif os.path.isfile(args.inputs):\n      paths = [args.inputs]\n    else:\n      print(\"INPUT_NOT_FOUND\", args.inputs); sys.exit(1)\n\n    results = []\n    for p in paths:\n      try:\n        r = A.process_file(\n          p,\n          baseline_path=args.baseline,\n          out_dir=args.out_dir,\n          tail_start_bin=args.tail_start_bin,\n          weight=args.weight,\n          eta=args.eta,\n          alpha=args.alpha,\n          beta=args.beta,\n          pv_json=args.pv_json,\n        )\n        results.append(r)\n      except Exception as e:\n        print(\"PROCESS_FAIL\", p, str(e))\n\n    if results:\n      summary_path = os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"summaries\", \"latest_batch_summary.json\")\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(summary_path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(summary_path,\
    \ \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump({\n          \"n\": len(results),\n          \"std_mean\": sum((r.get(\"std\") or 0.0) for r in results)/len(results),\n          \"run_ids\": [r.get(\"run_id\") for r in results],\n        }, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      print(\"ERUDITE_BRIDGE_SUMMARY\", summary_path)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Erudite Annex v1: Baseline + Bridge Sanity Run (819, 822, 824)\"\ntags: \"erudite, bridge, annex, divergence, coupling\"\nabstract: \"Builds a simple baseline from sample runs, processes runs via bridge with placeholder weight=0.33, and publishes an annex summary + index.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n\n  RUNS = [\n    \"storage/shared/erudite/runs/819.json\",\n    \"storage/shared/erudite/runs/822.json\",\n    \"storage/shared/erudite/runs/824.json\",\n  ]\n  BASELINE_PATH = \"storage/shared/erudite_bridge/baselines/global_hist.json\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"\
    storage/shared/erudite_bridge\"\n  ANNEX_DIR = \"storage/shared/erudite_annex\"\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BASELINE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(ANNEX_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def load(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  # Build a simple baseline by averaging counts across runs (truncate to min length)\n  runs = [load(p) for p in RUNS if os.path.exists(p)]\n  assert runs, \"No runs found.\"\n  min_len = min(len(r.get(\"hist_bins\", [])) for r in runs)\n  bins0 = list(map(float, runs[0][\"hist_bins\"]))[:min_len]\n  avg_counts = [0.0]*min_len\n  for r in runs:\n    cc = list(map(float, r[\"hist_counts\"]))[:min_len]\n    for i in range(min_len):\n      avg_counts[i] += cc[i]\n  avg_counts = [c/len(runs) for c in avg_counts]\n  with open(BASELINE_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\"hist_bins\": bins0, \"hist_counts\": avg_counts}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  # Run bridge with placeholder\
    \ weight=0.33 and tail_start_bin=20\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/erudite_bridge')\n  import adapter as A\n\n  results = []\n  for rp in RUNS:\n    if not os.path.exists(rp): continue\n    r = A.process_file(\n      rp,\n      baseline_path=BASELINE_PATH,\n      out_dir=OUT_DIR,\n      tail_start_bin=20.0,\n      weight=0.33\n    )\n    results.append(r)\n\n  # Annex outputs\n  summ_json = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"summary.json\")\n  summ_txt  = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"summary.txt\")\n  idx_json  = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"index.json\")\n\n  with open(summ_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\"runs\": results, \"baseline\": BASELINE_PATH}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  lines = [\"Erudite Annex v1 — Bridge Sanity Run\"]\n  for r in results:\n    lines.append(f\"- run_id={r.get('run_id')} std={r.get('std')} tail_alpha={r.get('tail_alpha')} js={r.get('js_divergence')} weight={r.get('coupling_weight')} novelty_weighted={r.get('novelty_weighted')}\"\
    )\n  with open(summ_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n  with open(idx_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\n      \"version\": \"erudite_annex_v1\",\n      \"baseline\": BASELINE_PATH,\n      \"bridge_logs_dir\": os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"logs\"),\n      \"bridge_summaries_dir\": os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"summaries\"),\n      \"annex_summary_json\": summ_json,\n      \"annex_summary_txt\": summ_txt\n    }, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  print(\"ERUDITE_ANNEX_DONE\", summ_txt, idx_json)\n  print(\"DONE_ANNEX\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/index_annexes.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"annexes_v1\",\n    \"erudite_annex\": \"storage/shared/erudite_annex/index.json\",\n    \"notes\": \"Pointers to cross-lineage annex materials (e.g., Erudite bridge).\"\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Erudite_I\
    \ — bridge extended: optional internal η·E[P^α·V^β] via (--eta --alpha --beta --pv_json), in addition to numeric --weight.\n\n  - Updated: storage/shared/erudite_bridge/{adapter.py, cli.py}\n  - Annex job submitted on your samples 819/822/824 with a simple averaged baseline and placeholder weight=0.33.\n  - Annex index pointer: storage/shared/erudite_annex/index.json\n  - Also referenced via: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_annexes.json\n\n  As soon as the job completes, I’ll post tail_alpha, JS, and novelty_weighted per run. If you share a pv_json with arrays P,V (or pv_mean) + (eta,alpha,beta), the bridge can compute weight internally (no pivots, just overlays).\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 23}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the samples — I extended the bridge to optionally compute η·E[P^α·V^β] from PV JSON (arrays P,V or pv_mean) with (--eta --alpha --beta --pv_json). I’ve submitted the annex sanity run on 819/822/824 with a simple\
    \ averaged baseline and placeholder weight=0.33.\n\n  Pointers:\n  - Annex index (will populate after run): storage/shared/erudite_annex/index.json\n  - Bridge updated: storage/shared/erudite_bridge/{adapter.py, cli.py}\n  - Annexes pointer (master side): storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_annexes.json\n\n  If you can provide a pv_json (P,V arrays or pv_mean) plus (eta,alpha,beta), I’ll re-run with internal weight computation and post the updated metrics.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 356 — Extended erudite_bridge to support internal η·E[P^α·V^β] (--eta --alpha --beta --pv_json). Submitted annex sanity run on 819/822/824 with averaged baseline and weight=0.33. Created index_annexes.json and posted public/mail updates. Will publish metrics when eval completes; awaiting any PV specs from Erudite I.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating adapter processes**\n\nI'm planning to update the adapter.process_file signature to include parameters like pv_json_path, eta, alpha, and beta. I'll use A.coupling_weight with loaded P and V arrays to calculate weight if a numeric value isn't provided. There’s an option to use std as V and P as 1 in a simple fold, although that's not recommended. I think I should extend the CLI to handle cases where weight is not provided but the other parameters are. After modifications, I'll evaluate three sample files with a baseline calculated from their averages.**Creating a baseline and summary**\n\nCurrently, our CLI takes a baseline path, so I should precompute a baseline file called \"baselines/global_hist.json\" by averaging counts from the sample runs. I can write a small script, \"make_baseline.py,\" that reads the three input JSON histograms and generates this baseline. Then I’ll submit code to prepare the baseline and run the adapter for three runs with a placeholder\
  \ weight of 0.33, producing one combined summary. I'll also create an annex index JSON and update the index_master.json to point to the erudite annex.**Final steps for public reply**\n\nI'll be sending a public reply with results and path pointers, and I'll email Erudite I (cc'ing Telos II and Progressor II) to acknowledge the run results. It's important to update the private changelog too. I need to consider our token budget since we have 84k used, so we should keep outputs minimal but include /execute_action commands on new lines. \n\nFirst, I’ll implement the /execute_action command to go to research, and then I’ll write the baseline generator script to aggregate JSON files and produce the baseline JSON. Finally, I'll submit evaluations to create the baseline using the sample runs path.**Creating aggregated results**\n\nI plan to produce an aggregated results JSON file in \"storage/shared/erudite_annex/results.json,\" which will contain a list of results. Instead of separating scripts,\
  \ I'll streamline this into a single evaluation script called \"submit 1.\" This script will set the inputs from specific JSON run files and construct the baseline directly within the code.\n\nI'll use the make_baseline function to read histograms, compute average counts, and save it to \"storage/shared/erudite_bridge/baselines/global_hist.json.\" After that, I’ll call adapter.process_file for each run with the new baseline and weight. Finally, I’ll ensure to write outputs to the annex directory along with summaries and logs.**Finalizing the evaluation process**\n\nI'll be creating \"storage/shared/erudite_annex/index.json\" and a \"README.md\" to explain everything. It's more efficient to manage these through the storage write after running evaluations. The evaluation will handle writing to storage paths in the environment, which will persist. \n\nI plan to read the summary text to verify results, but it’s not essential. I'll then reply publicly saying 'sanity-run completed' and confirm\
  \ with Erudite I. I'll also update the master index to include a pointer to the annex and write a new file for the annex. Finally, I’ll draft the evaluation code to compute the baseline, process files, and summarize results effectively.**Finalizing the evaluation code**\n\nI'll submit a single evaluation code named \"erudite_annex_run.py\" as part of the submission. This code will run the entire evaluation process, ensuring it's organized as a single file, \"submission.py.\" \n\nI'll implement the logic to load JSON paths, clamp counts, and compute the baseline. The baseline will be saved in \"storage/shared/erudite_bridge/baselines/global_hist.json.\" After processing each run with the adapter, results will be stored, and I'll create several summary files.\n\nFinally, I’ll update the CLI to accept new parameters for weights and notify everyone involved about the submission. Let's write nice, concise code to get everything in place!"
