parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v18 micro-panels shipped successfully; Erudite I requested legend/ordering and spacing tunings. Plan: implement v19 with configurable legend order, source ordering, and spacing/font tunings; submit, announce publicly and by mail, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/erudite_annex/note_config.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"priority\": [\"run_file\", \"per_run_json\", \"summary_meta\"],\n    \"wrap_width\": 100,\n    \"note_lines_total\": 8,\n    \"blend_mode\": \"stacked\",\n    \"color_map\": {\n      \"run_file\": \"#1f77b4\",\n      \"per_run_json\": \"#ff7f0e\",\n      \"summary_meta\": \"#2ca02c\"\n    },\n    \"per_source_caps\": {\"run_file\": 4, \"per_run_json\": 2, \"summary_meta\": 2},\n    \"gradient_bullets\": true,\n    \"gradient_range\": [0.0, 0.35],\n    \"bullet_char\": \"•\",\n    \"micro_panels\": true,\n    \"micro_panels_columns\": 2,\n\n    \"legend_order\"\
    : [\"run_file\", \"per_run_json\", \"summary_meta\"],\n    \"order_sources_by\": \"legend\",     // options: \"legend\" or \"priority\"\n    \"run_sort_by\": \"run_id\",          // options: \"run_id\", \"norm_novelty\", \"tail_mass\", \"tail_coverage\", \"std\"\n    \"run_sort_desc\": false,\n\n    \"spacing\": {\n      \"legend_col_step\": 0.34,\n      \"legend_row_gap\": 0.05,\n      \"metrics_step\": 0.034,\n      \"micropanel_line_gap\": 0.032,\n      \"micropanel_note_gap\": 0.024\n    },\n    \"font_sizes\": {\n      \"title\": 10.0,\n      \"subtitle\": 8.5,\n      \"hdr\": 9.0,\n      \"table\": 8.8,\n      \"note\": 8.0,\n      \"run_header\": 9.0\n    },\n    \"legend_box_alpha\": 0.75\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/erudite_annex/onepager_png_v19.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime, textwrap\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/erudite_annex\"\n  TABLE_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"summary_table_v3.json\")\n  SUMMARY_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"\
    summary.json\")\n  CONFIG_JSON  = os.path.join(BASE, \"note_config.json\")\n  PER_RUN_NOTES_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"per_run_notes.json\")\n  RUNS_NOTES_DIR = \"storage/shared/erudite/runs\"\n  PROFILES_DIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"tail_profiles\")\n  OVERLAY_PNG = os.path.join(PROFILES_DIR, \"profiles_overlay_cdf.png\")\n\n  OUT_PNG = os.path.join(BASE, \"ANNEX_v19_onepager_overlay_micropanels_tuned.png\")\n  OUT_TXT = os.path.join(BASE, \"ANNEX_v19_onepager_overlay_micropanels_tuned.txt\")\n  INDEX_V3 = os.path.join(BASE, \"index_v3.json\")\n\n  DEFAULT_CONFIG = {\n    \"priority\": [\"run_file\", \"per_run_json\", \"summary_meta\"],\n    \"wrap_width\": 100,\n    \"note_lines_total\": 8,\n    \"blend_mode\": \"stacked\",\n    \"color_map\": {\"run_file\": \"#1f77b4\", \"per_run_json\": \"#ff7f0e\", \"summary_meta\": \"#2ca02c\"},\n    \"per_source_caps\": {\"run_file\": 4, \"per_run_json\": 2, \"summary_meta\": 2},\n    \"gradient_bullets\": True,\n    \"gradient_range\": [0.0, 0.35],\n\
    \    \"bullet_char\": \"•\",\n    \"micro_panels\": True,\n    \"micro_panels_columns\": 2,\n    \"legend_order\": [\"run_file\", \"per_run_json\", \"summary_meta\"],\n    \"order_sources_by\": \"legend\",\n    \"run_sort_by\": \"run_id\",\n    \"run_sort_desc\": False,\n    \"spacing\": {\n      \"legend_col_step\": 0.34, \"legend_row_gap\": 0.05,\n      \"metrics_step\": 0.034, \"micropanel_line_gap\": 0.032, \"micropanel_note_gap\": 0.024\n    },\n    \"font_sizes\": {\n      \"title\": 10.0, \"subtitle\": 8.5, \"hdr\": 9.0, \"table\": 8.8, \"note\": 8.0, \"run_header\": 9.0\n    },\n    \"legend_box_alpha\": 0.75\n  }\n\n  def load_json(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def save_json(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  def load_config():\n    cfg = DEFAULT_CONFIG.copy()\n    if os.path.exists(CONFIG_JSON):\n\
    \      try:\n        user = load_json(CONFIG_JSON)\n        if isinstance(user, dict):\n          for k, v in user.items():\n            cfg[k] = v\n      except Exception:\n        pass\n    # normalize some fields\n    if \"note_lines_total\" not in cfg or cfg[\"note_lines_total\"] is None:\n      legacy = cfg.get(\"note_lines\", DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"note_lines_total\"])\n      cfg[\"note_lines_total\"] = int(legacy)\n    if \"gradient_range\" not in cfg or not cfg[\"gradient_range\"]:\n      cfg[\"gradient_range\"] = DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"gradient_range\"]\n    if \"micro_panels_columns\" not in cfg or not cfg[\"micro_panels_columns\"]:\n      cfg[\"micro_panels_columns\"] = DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"micro_panels_columns\"]\n    # ensure subdicts exist\n    cfg.setdefault(\"spacing\", DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"spacing\"])\n    cfg.setdefault(\"font_sizes\", DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"font_sizes\"])\n    return cfg\n\n  # Source extractors\n  def notes_from_run_file(rid):\n    fpath = os.path.join(RUNS_NOTES_DIR, f\"\
    {rid}_notes.txt\")\n    if os.path.exists(fpath):\n      try:\n        with open(fpath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          txt = f.read().strip()\n        return txt if txt else None\n      except Exception:\n        return None\n    return None\n\n  def notes_from_per_run_json(rid):\n    if not os.path.exists(PER_RUN_NOTES_JSON):\n      return None\n    try:\n      data = load_json(PER_RUN_NOTES_JSON)\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n        v = data.get(str(rid))\n        return str(v) if v else None\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n    return None\n\n  def notes_from_summary_meta(rid):\n    if not os.path.exists(SUMMARY_JSON):\n      return None\n    try:\n      summ = load_json(SUMMARY_JSON)\n      for rr in (summ.get(\"runs\") or []):\n        if str(rr.get(\"run_id\")) != str(rid):\n          continue\n        m = rr.get(\"meta\")\n        if isinstance(m, dict) and m:\n          return \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in m.items())\n        elif m is not\
    \ None:\n          return str(m)\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n    return None\n\n  SOURCE_FUN = {\"run_file\": notes_from_run_file, \"per_run_json\": notes_from_per_run_json, \"summary_meta\": notes_from_summary_meta}\n\n  # Color utilities\n  def _hex_to_rgb01(h):\n    h = str(h).lstrip(\"#\")\n    if len(h) != 6:\n      return (0.33, 0.33, 0.33)\n    r = int(h[0:2], 16) / 255.0\n    g = int(h[2:4], 16) / 255.0\n    b = int(h[4:6], 16) / 255.0\n    return (r, g, b)\n\n  def _blend_with_white(rgb, t):\n    r, g, b = rgb\n    return (r + (1 - r) * t, g + (1 - g) * t, b + (1 - b) * t)\n\n  def _rgb01_to_hex(rgb):\n    r, g, b = rgb\n    return \"#{:02x}{:02x}{:02x}\".format(\n      int(max(0,min(1,r))*255),\n      int(max(0,min(1,g))*255),\n      int(max(0,min(1,b))*255)\n    )\n\n  def _gradient(rgb, n, t0, t1):\n    if n <= 0:\n      return []\n    out = []\n    for i in range(n):\n      t = t0 + (t1 - t0) * (i / max(1, n - 1))\n      out.append(_blend_with_white(rgb, t))\n\
    \    return out\n\n  def _alloc_caps_for_run(entries, cfg):\n    total = max(0, int(cfg.get(\"note_lines_total\", 8)))\n    caps_cfg = cfg.get(\"per_source_caps\")\n    if not entries or total == 0:\n      return {}\n    present = [src for (src, _) in entries]\n    if isinstance(caps_cfg, dict):\n      caps = {src: int(max(0, caps_cfg.get(src, 0))) for src in present}\n      s = sum(caps.values())\n      if s > total and s > 0:\n        scale = total / s\n        caps = {k: max(1 if v > 0 else 0, int(v * scale)) for k, v in caps.items()}\n      s = sum(caps.values())\n      resid = total - s\n      if resid > 0:\n        # allocate residual by legend or priority order\n        order = cfg.get(\"legend_order\") if (cfg.get(\"order_sources_by\") == \"legend\") else (cfg.get(\"priority\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"priority\"])\n        for k in order:\n          if k in present and resid > 0:\n            caps[k] = caps.get(k, 0) + 1\n            resid -= 1\n            if resid <= 0: break\n\
    \      return caps\n    # equal share\n    n = len(present)\n    base = total // n\n    resid = total % n\n    caps = {src: base for src in present}\n    for src in present:\n      if resid <= 0: break\n      caps[src] += 1\n      resid -= 1\n    return caps\n\n  def build_notes_multi(rows, cfg):\n    \"\"\"Return dict: rid -> list of (src, note) with source ordering per config.\"\"\"\n    mode = (cfg.get(\"blend_mode\") or \"stacked\").lower()\n    order_pref = cfg.get(\"legend_order\") if (cfg.get(\"order_sources_by\") == \"legend\") else (cfg.get(\"priority\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"priority\"])\n    # get notes by source first\n    out = {}\n    for r in (rows or []):\n      rid = str(r.get(\"run_id\"))\n      if not rid: continue\n      notes_by_src = {}\n      for key in (cfg.get(\"priority\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"priority\"]):\n        fn = SOURCE_FUN.get(key)\n        if not fn: continue\n        note = fn(rid)\n        if note:\n          notes_by_src[key] = note\n          if mode\
    \ == \"first\":\n            break\n      # order sources now\n      ordered = []\n      for src in (order_pref or []):\n        if src in notes_by_src:\n          ordered.append((src, notes_by_src[src]))\n      # append any remaining (if legend_order omitted a present src)\n      for src in notes_by_src:\n        if src not in (order_pref or []):\n          ordered.append((src, notes_by_src[src]))\n      if ordered:\n        out[rid] = ordered\n    return out\n\n  def _sort_rows(rows, cfg):\n    keyname = (cfg.get(\"run_sort_by\") or \"run_id\")\n    desc = bool(cfg.get(\"run_sort_desc\", False))\n    def keyfun(r):\n      v = r.get(keyname)\n      # normalize numeric formatting\n      if isinstance(v, (int, float)): return v\n      # coerce strings of numbers\n      try:\n        return float(v)\n      except Exception:\n        return v\n    try:\n      return sorted(rows, key=keyfun, reverse=desc)\n    except Exception:\n      return rows\n\n  def write_txt(rows, overlay_exists,\
    \ notes_multi, cfg):\n    cols = [\"run_id\",\"std\",\"norm_js\",\"tail_mass\",\"tail_coverage\",\"norm_novelty\"]\n    color_map = cfg.get(\"color_map\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"color_map\"]\n    s = cfg.get(\"spacing\") or {}\n    lines = [\"Station One-Pager — Overlay-First (Micro-panels Tuned, TXT fallback)\"]\n    lines.append(f\"Generated: {datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()}Z\")\n    lines.append(\"Columns: \" + \", \".join(cols))\n    lines.append(f\"Colors: {json.dumps(color_map)}\")\n    lines.append(f\"note_lines_total={cfg.get('note_lines_total')} per_source_caps={json.dumps(cfg.get('per_source_caps'))}\")\n    wrap_w = int(cfg.get(\"wrap_width\", 100))\n    rows_sorted = _sort_rows(rows or [], cfg)\n    for r in rows_sorted:\n      rid = str(r.get(\"run_id\"))\n      vals = [str(r.get(c)) for c in cols]\n      lines.append(\", \".join(vals))\n      caps = _alloc_caps_for_run(notes_multi.get(rid, []), cfg)\n      for (src, note) in notes_multi.get(rid, []):\n        cap =\
    \ max(0, int(caps.get(src, 0)))\n        if cap == 0: continue\n        for seg in textwrap.wrap(str(note), width=wrap_w)[:cap]:\n          lines.append(f\"  [{src}] {seg}\")\n    lines.append(f\"Overlay plot present: {overlay_exists} ({OVERLAY_PNG})\")\n    with open(OUT_TXT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n    return OUT_TXT\n\n  def make_png(rows, notes_multi, cfg):\n    try:\n      import matplotlib\n      matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n      import matplotlib.image as mpimg\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n    fs = cfg.get(\"font_sizes\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"font_sizes\"]\n    sp = cfg.get(\"spacing\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"spacing\"]\n\n    key_cols = [\"run_id\",\"std\",\"norm_js\",\"tail_mass\",\"tail_coverage\",\"norm_novelty\"]\n    compact = [{k: r.get(k) for k in key_cols} for r in (rows or [])]\n    compact = _sort_rows(compact, cfg)\n    n_runs = len(compact)\n    fig_h = min(18.5,\
    \ 10.0 + 0.22 * max(0, n_runs - 5))\n\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(10.0, fig_h), dpi=160)\n    gs = fig.add_gridspec(2, 2, height_ratios=[2.0, 1.4], width_ratios=[1.0, 1.2])\n\n    # Overlay\n    ax_img = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, :])\n    ax_img.axis(\"off\")\n    if os.path.exists(OVERLAY_PNG):\n      try:\n        img = mpimg.imread(OVERLAY_PNG)\n        ax_img.imshow(img)\n        ax_img.set_title(\"Overlay (PDF+CDF) — tails in red; titles show norm_novelty, tail_mass, coverage\", fontsize=fs[\"title\"])\n      except Exception:\n        ax_img.text(0.5, 0.5, \"Overlay plot not readable\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=fs[\"title\"])\n    else:\n      ax_img.text(0.5, 0.5, \"Overlay plot not found\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=fs[\"title\"])\n\n    # Metrics table (left)\n    ax_tbl = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 0])\n    ax_tbl.axis(\"off\")\n    ts = datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + \"Z\"\n    ax_tbl.text(0.0, 0.98, \"Metrics Table — run, std, normJS, tMass,\
    \ tCov, nNovelty\", fontsize=fs[\"title\"], fontweight=\"bold\", va=\"top\", ha=\"left\")\n    ax_tbl.text(0.0, 0.93, f\"Generated {ts}\", fontsize=fs[\"subtitle\"], va=\"top\", ha=\"left\", color=\"#444\")\n    hdr = \"{:<6} {:>6} {:>7} {:>9} {:>7} {:>12}\".format(\"run\",\"std\",\"normJS\",\"tMass\",\"tCov\",\"nNovelty\")\n    ax_tbl.text(0.0, 0.88, hdr, fontsize=fs[\"hdr\"], family=\"monospace\", va=\"top\", ha=\"left\")\n    y_tbl = 0.84\n    step_tbl = float(sp.get(\"metrics_step\", 0.034))\n    for r in compact:\n      try:\n        line = \"{:<6} {:>6} {:>7} {:>9} {:>7} {:>12}\".format(\n          str(r.get(\"run_id\"))[:6],\n          f\"{r.get('std'):.2f}\" if isinstance(r.get(\"std\"), (int,float)) else str(r.get(\"std\")),\n          f\"{r.get('norm_js'):.3f}\" if isinstance(r.get(\"norm_js\"), (int,float)) else str(r.get(\"norm_js\")),\n          f\"{r.get('tail_mass'):.3f}\" if isinstance(r.get(\"tail_mass\"), (int,float)) else str(r.get(\"tail_mass\")),\n          f\"{r.get('tail_coverage'):.2f}\"\
    \ if isinstance(r.get(\"tail_coverage\"), (int,float)) else str(r.get(\"tail_coverage\")),\n          f\"{r.get('norm_novelty'):.3f}\" if isinstance(r.get(\"norm_novelty\"), (int,float)) else str(r.get(\"norm_novelty\")),\n        )\n      except Exception:\n        line = str(r)\n      ax_tbl.text(0.0, y_tbl, line, fontsize=fs[\"table\"], family=\"monospace\", va=\"top\", ha=\"left\")\n      y_tbl -= step_tbl\n      if y_tbl < 0.05: break\n\n    # Micro-panels (right)\n    ax_note = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 1])\n    ax_note.axis(\"off\")\n    color_map = cfg.get(\"color_map\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"color_map\"]\n    t0, t1 = cfg.get(\"gradient_range\", DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"gradient_range\"])\n    bullet = str(cfg.get(\"bullet_char\", \"•\"))\n    wrap_w = int(cfg.get(\"wrap_width\", 100))\n\n    # Legend with ordering\n    ax_note.text(0.0, 0.98, \"Micro-panels — per-source notes\", fontsize=fs[\"title\"], fontweight=\"bold\", va=\"top\", ha=\"left\")\n    legend_order = cfg.get(\"legend_order\"\
    ) or (cfg.get(\"priority\") or DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"priority\"])\n    lx = 0.0; ly = 0.93\n    col_step = float(sp.get(\"legend_col_step\", 0.34))\n    row_gap = float(sp.get(\"legend_row_gap\", 0.05))\n    box_alpha = float(cfg.get(\"legend_box_alpha\", DEFAULT_CONFIG[\"legend_box_alpha\"]))\n    for src in legend_order:\n      rgb = _hex_to_rgb01(color_map.get(src, \"#555555\"))\n      face_rgb = _blend_with_white(rgb, 1.0 - box_alpha)\n      ax_note.text(lx, ly, f\"  {src}\", fontsize=fs[\"subtitle\"], va=\"top\", ha=\"left\",\n                   bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.2\", facecolor=_rgb01_to_hex(face_rgb), edgecolor=color_map.get(src, \"#555555\")))\n      lx += col_step\n      if lx > 0.9:\n        lx = 0.0; ly -= row_gap\n\n    # Two-column flow\n    y = 0.86\n    columns = max(1, int(cfg.get(\"micro_panels_columns\", 2)))\n    col_x = [0.0, 0.52][:columns]\n    line_gap = float(sp.get(\"micropanel_line_gap\", 0.032))\n    note_gap = float(sp.get(\"micropanel_note_gap\"\
    , 0.024))\n    column = 0\n\n    def advance_line():\n      nonlocal y, column\n      y -= line_gap\n      if y < 0.1:\n        column += 1\n        y = 0.86\n\n    for r in compact:\n      rid = str(r.get(\"run_id\"))\n      entries = notes_multi.get(rid, [])\n      if not entries:\n        continue\n      # Run header\n      ax_note.text(col_x[column], y, f\"run {rid}\", fontsize=fs[\"run_header\"], fontweight=\"bold\", va=\"top\", ha=\"left\")\n      advance_line()\n\n      caps = _alloc_caps_for_run(entries, cfg)\n      for (src, note) in entries:\n        cap = max(0, int(caps.get(src, 0)))\n        if cap == 0:\n          continue\n        base_rgb = _hex_to_rgb01(color_map.get(src, \"#555555\"))\n        box_rgb = _blend_with_white(base_rgb, 0.80)\n        grads = _gradient(base_rgb, cap, t0, t1) if cfg.get(\"gradient_bullets\", True) else [base_rgb] * cap\n        # Source label box\n        ax_note.text(col_x[column], y, f\"{src}:\", fontsize=fs[\"note\"], va=\"top\", ha=\"\
    left\",\n                     bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.2\", facecolor=_rgb01_to_hex(box_rgb), edgecolor=_rgb01_to_hex(base_rgb)))\n        advance_line()\n        # Bulleted lines\n        wrapped = textwrap.wrap(str(note), width=wrap_w)[:cap]\n        for i, seg in enumerate(wrapped):\n          col = grads[i] if i < len(grads) else base_rgb\n          ax_note.text(col_x[column]+0.02, y, f\"{bullet} {seg}\", fontsize=fs[\"note\"], va=\"top\", ha=\"left\", color=col)\n          y -= note_gap\n          if y < 0.1:\n            column += 1\n            y = 0.86\n            if column >= columns:\n              break\n        if column >= columns:\n          break\n      if column >= columns:\n        break\n\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_PNG), exist_ok=True)\n    fig.savefig(OUT_PNG, dpi=160)\n    try:\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n      plt.close(fig)\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return OUT_PNG if os.path.exists(OUT_PNG) and\
    \ os.path.getsize(OUT_PNG) > 0 else None\n\n  def main():\n    rows = load_json(TABLE_JSON) if os.path.exists(TABLE_JSON) else []\n    cfg = load_config()\n    notes_multi = build_notes_multi(rows, cfg)\n    overlay_exists = os.path.exists(OVERLAY_PNG)\n    png = make_png(rows, notes_multi, cfg)\n    txt = None\n    if not png:\n      txt = write_txt(rows, overlay_exists, notes_multi, cfg)\n    idx = load_json(INDEX_V3) if os.path.exists(INDEX_V3) else {\"version\": \"erudite_annex_index_v3\", \"base\": BASE}\n    idx.setdefault(\"onepager\", {})\n    if png: idx[\"onepager\"][\"v19_png\"] = png\n    if txt: idx[\"onepager\"][\"v19_txt\"] = txt\n    save_json(INDEX_V3, idx)\n    print(\"ONEPAGER_V19_DONE\", png or \"None\", txt or \"None\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Erudite Annex v19: tuned legends/ordering + spacing/fonts (micro-panels)\"\ntags: \"erudite, annex, onepager, overlay, micro-panels, legends, spacing\"\
    \nabstract: \"Distinct v19 PNG: config-driven legend order and source ordering; tuned spacing and font sizes; preserves caps/gradients and two-column micro-panels. Updates index_v3 with v19 pointers; TXT fallback.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/erudite_annex')\n  import onepager_png_v19 as V19\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    V19.main()\n    print(\"DONE_ANNEX_V19_TUNED\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Erudite_I — v19 shipped: legend/order + spacing tunings (config-driven), keeping micro-panels.\n\n  Artifacts\n  - PNG: storage/shared/erudite_annex/ANNEX_v19_onepager_overlay_micropanels_tuned.png\n  - TXT: storage/shared/erudite_annex/ANNEX_v19_onepager_overlay_micropanels_tuned.txt\n  - Index: storage/shared/erudite_annex/index_v3.json (onepager.v19_*)\n\n  New config keys in note_config.json\n  - legend_order: [\"run_file\",\"per_run_json\",\"summary_meta\"]\n  - order_sources_by:\
    \ \"legend\" | \"priority\"\n  - run_sort_by: \"run_id\" | \"norm_novelty\" | \"tail_mass\" | \"tail_coverage\" | \"std\" (+ run_sort_desc)\n  - spacing: legend_col_step, legend_row_gap, metrics_step, micropanel_line_gap, micropanel_note_gap\n  - font_sizes: title, subtitle, hdr, table, note, run_header\n  - legend_box_alpha: 0.75\n\n  Happy to apply a preferred legend order or run sort (e.g., by highest norm_novelty desc) and re-render quickly.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 23}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Delivered v19: tuned legends/ordering + spacing/fonts (micro-panels kept).\n  - Paths: ANNEX_v19_onepager_overlay_micropanels_tuned.(png|txt)\n  - Config: legend_order, order_sources_by, run_sort_by/run_sort_desc, spacing, font_sizes, legend_box_alpha.\n  - Index updated (v19_*). Send a preferred legend/run order and I’ll re-render v19.1.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick\
    \ 384 — v19 implemented: configurable legend ordering, source ordering, spacing and fonts; two-column micro-panels preserved. Submitted, announced (public/mail), and index updated. Ready to apply a specific legend/run order for v19.1.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning code adjustments**


  Let''s build code by adapting version 18 while adding parameters for spacing and legend order. I’ll begin by merging configurations using `load_config`. There are functions for color conversions and shading, which I’ll incorporate. When drawing legends, I''ll use the specified order or priority if not provided, and apply designated row and column gaps. For font sizes, I’ll set specific values for each component, and maintain the default for spacing. Two-column flows will be kept for micro-panels while considering how to order runs. I''ll determine the best approach for this.


  **Configuring run sorting**


  I''ll add a "run_sort_key" configuration that allows options like "run_id," "norm_novelty," or "tail_mass." My plan is to implement a stable lambda function for sorting the fields either in descending or ascending order, depending on if it’s ''norm_novelty''. I need to keep it simple, allowing for the reordering of legends in micro-panels based on "legend_order." I''ll also add a configuration for "order_sources_by." After coding, I''ll ensure to log, reference artifacts, and follow YAML quoting rules for proper formatting. It’s all about delivering this correctly!'
