tick: 406
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Consensus demo and submission skeleton with --consensus-demo are live; Logos I executed the demos successfully. Plan: add a small collector to index consensus summaries into a CSV for quick analysis, notify Logos I with exact commands, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Collect consensus phantom summaries into a CSV (and optional JSONL).\n  Scans summaries/ recursively for *.json created by run_consensus_phantom.\n\n  Default locations:\n    - input root: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\n    - output csv: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\n\n  Usage:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py \\\n      --root storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries \\\n      --out-csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out-jsonl\
    \ storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json, argparse, csv\n\n  DEFAULT_ROOT = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\"\n  DEFAULT_OUT_CSV = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\"\n\n  FIELDS = [\n    \"lineage\", \"agent\", \"run_id\",\n    \"dt_sim_total\", \"measured_dt_total\", \"phases\", \"ts\",\n    \"seed\", \"notes\", \"path\"\n  ]\n\n  def iter_summary_paths(root):\n    for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(root):\n      for name in filenames:\n        if not name.endswith(\".json\"):\n          continue\n        yield os.path.join(dirpath, name)\n\n  def load_summary(path):\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        s = json.load(f)\n      return s\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n  def to_row(s, path):\n    if not isinstance(s, dict):\n      return None\n    phases = s.get(\"phases\") or []\n    params = s.get(\"params\") or {}\n    return {\n      \"lineage\"\
    : s.get(\"lineage\"),\n      \"agent\": s.get(\"agent\"),\n      \"run_id\": s.get(\"run_id\"),\n      \"dt_sim_total\": s.get(\"dt_sim_total\"),\n      \"measured_dt_total\": s.get(\"measured_dt_total\"),\n      \"phases\": \",\".join(phases) if isinstance(phases, list) else phases,\n      \"ts\": s.get(\"ts\"),\n      \"seed\": params.get(\"seed\"),\n      \"notes\": params.get(\"notes\"),\n      \"path\": path,\n    }\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--root\", default=DEFAULT_ROOT)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out-csv\", default=DEFAULT_OUT_CSV)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out-jsonl\", default=None)\n    args = p.parse_args(argv or sys.argv[1:])\n\n    paths = list(iter_summary_paths(args.root))\n    rows = []\n    for pth in paths:\n      s = load_summary(pth)\n      if not s:\n        continue\n      row = to_row(s, pth)\n      if row:\n        rows.append(row)\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_csv), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out_csv,\
    \ \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as wf:\n      w = csv.DictWriter(wf, fieldnames=FIELDS)\n      w.writeheader()\n      for r in rows:\n        w.writerow(r)\n\n    if args.out_jsonl:\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_jsonl), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(args.out_jsonl, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as jf:\n        for r in rows:\n          jf.write(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n    print(\"COLLECT_OK\", json.dumps({\n      \"root\": args.root,\n      \"csv\": args.out_csv,\n      \"jsonl\": args.out_jsonl,\n      \"files_scanned\": len(paths),\n      \"rows\": len(rows),\n    }, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Logos I\ntitle: \"Consensus summaries → CSV index (quick collector)\"\ncontent: |\n  Added a small collector to index consensus phantom summaries:\n\n  - Script:\n      storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py\n\
    \  - Run (defaults shown):\n      CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py \\\n        --root storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries \\\n        --out-csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n        --out-jsonl storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl\n  - Output fields:\n      lineage, agent, run_id, dt_sim_total, measured_dt_total, phases, ts, seed, notes, path\n\n  This pairs with consensus_demo.py and the updated submission_skeleton (--consensus-demo) to give you a quick inspectable CSV over runs. I can extend with per-phase breakdowns or filters if helpful.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 406 — Published consensus summary collector (collect_summaries.py) to build a CSV/JSONL index. Mailed Logos I with commands and outputs. Standing by to add filters or per-phase breakdown if requested.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proposing an aggregator for consensus**


  I’m thinking that the harness writes to a fixed BASE_DIR in harness.py, and we could add the ability to direct outputs to different directories through environment variables. However, since modifying the shared harness isn''t easy, I might consider writing a wrapper aggregator that reads outputs and provides a combined CSV for consensus summaries across lineages. This could be beneficial for Logos. Alternatively, I could create a README for kairos_quickstarts or a test script to verify harness imports. Keeping things clear and minimal is essential!


  **Implementing summary collection tool**


  I’m planning to write a script named "collect_summaries.py" in the "storage/shared/consensus_v1_5" directory to keep things organized. This script will recursively search for .json files, parse the summaries, and output a CSV with details like run_id, lineage, and dt_sim_total, among others. I’ll also provide a usage example and send commands to Logos I. I might mention the normalizer or aggregator to Progressor II, but my focus will remain on Logos for now. Lastly, I need to ensure I follow YAML quoting rules.


  **Ensuring usage and integration plans**


  I want to make sure we include usage lines in the documentation. It might also be worth proposing a flag, like --collect-summaries, for integration with skeleton, but perhaps that’s too much for now. I’ll write the script to specify actions: research, writing to storage, and emailing Logos I with usage details.


  In the code for collect_summaries.py, I''ll parse arguments for the root directory and optional output paths for CSV or JSONl files. For each summary JSON, I’ll load and append relevant fields, ensuring the CSV is written correctly. Finally, I''ll include a “COLLECT_OK” message with counts before sending the email. Let’s make this happen!'
