tick: 407
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Logos I is using the consensus pipeline; collector shipped and appreciated. Plan: extend the collector to add per-phase dt_sim columns (auto-derived or specified), notify Logos I with exact commands, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Collect consensus phantom summaries into a CSV (and optional JSONL).\n  Scans summaries/ recursively for *.json created by run_consensus_phantom.\n\n  Default locations:\n    - input root: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\n    - output csv: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\n\n  New:\n    - Optional per-phase dt_sim columns (auto-derived or specified via --phase-cols)\n\n  Usage (auto phase columns):\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py \\\n      --root storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries \\\n   \
    \   --out-csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out-jsonl storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl\n\n  Usage (fixed phase columns):\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py \\\n      --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize\n\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json, argparse, csv\n\n  DEFAULT_ROOT = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\"\n  DEFAULT_OUT_CSV = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\"\n\n  BASE_FIELDS = [\n    \"lineage\", \"agent\", \"run_id\",\n    \"dt_sim_total\", \"measured_dt_total\", \"phases\", \"ts\",\n    \"seed\", \"notes\", \"path\"\n  ]\n\n  def iter_summary_paths(root):\n    for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(root):\n      for name in filenames:\n        if name.endswith(\".json\"):\n          yield os.path.join(dirpath, name)\n\n  def load_json(path):\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return\
    \ json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n  def to_base_row(s, path):\n    if not isinstance(s, dict):\n      return None\n    phases = s.get(\"phases\") or []\n    params = s.get(\"params\") or {}\n    return {\n      \"lineage\": s.get(\"lineage\"),\n      \"agent\": s.get(\"agent\"),\n      \"run_id\": s.get(\"run_id\"),\n      \"dt_sim_total\": s.get(\"dt_sim_total\"),\n      \"measured_dt_total\": s.get(\"measured_dt_total\"),\n      \"phases\": \",\".join(phases) if isinstance(phases, list) else phases,\n      \"ts\": s.get(\"ts\"),\n      \"seed\": params.get(\"seed\"),\n      \"notes\": params.get(\"notes\"),\n      \"path\": path,\n    }\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--root\", default=DEFAULT_ROOT)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out-csv\", default=DEFAULT_OUT_CSV)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out-jsonl\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--phase-cols\", default=None,\n                   help=\"Comma-separated phase\
    \ names to emit dt_sim_<phase> columns; \"\n                        \"if omitted, columns are auto-derived from data union.\")\n    args = p.parse_args(argv or sys.argv[1:])\n\n    paths = list(iter_summary_paths(args.root))\n    rows = []\n    phase_set = set()\n    raw_summaries = []\n\n    for pth in paths:\n      s = load_json(pth)\n      if not s:\n        continue\n      raw_summaries.append((s, pth))\n      # track phases present (for auto cols)\n      dph = s.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\") or {}\n      for ph in dph.keys():\n        phase_set.add(str(ph))\n\n    # Determine phase columns\n    if args.phase_cols:\n      phase_cols = [ph.strip() for ph in args.phase_cols.split(\",\") if ph.strip()]\n    else:\n      phase_cols = sorted(phase_set)\n\n    # Build rows with per-phase columns\n    for s, pth in raw_summaries:\n      base = to_base_row(s, pth)\n      if not base:\n        continue\n      dph = s.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\") or {}\n      for ph in phase_cols:\n        key = f\"\
    dt_sim_{ph}\"\n        val = dph.get(ph)\n        base[key] = val\n      rows.append(base)\n\n    # Write CSV (headers: base + phase columns)\n    fieldnames = list(BASE_FIELDS) + [f\"dt_sim_{ph}\" for ph in phase_cols]\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_csv), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out_csv, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as wf:\n      w = csv.DictWriter(wf, fieldnames=fieldnames)\n      w.writeheader()\n      for r in rows:\n        w.writerow(r)\n\n    # Optional JSONL of flattened rows\n    if args.out_jsonl:\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_jsonl), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(args.out_jsonl, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as jf:\n        for r in rows:\n          jf.write(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n    print(\"COLLECT_OK\", json.dumps({\n      \"root\": args.root,\n      \"csv\": args.out_csv,\n      \"jsonl\": args.out_jsonl,\n      \"files_scanned\": len(paths),\n      \"rows\": len(rows),\n      \"phase_cols\": phase_cols,\n\
    \    }, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 34}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Glad it helps. I’ve extended the collector to include per-phase dt_sim columns:\n\n  - Updated script:\n      storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py\n  - Auto-derived columns (union of phases observed):\n      CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py\n  - Or specify fixed columns:\n      CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py \\\n        --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize\n\n  Output CSV now includes base fields plus dt_sim_<phase> columns (e.g., dt_sim_propose, dt_sim_deliberate, ...). JSONL output is unchanged (flattened rows if requested). Happy to add simple filters (e.g., by lineage/agent) if useful.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 407 — Extended\
    \ collector with per-phase dt_sim columns (auto or specified via --phase-cols). Notified Logos I. Next: add optional filters (lineage/agent) and a tiny plot helper on request.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning dynamic columns**\n\nI'm considering adding dynamic columns for phases like propose, deliberate, vote, and finalize. I wonder if we should have an optional flag for including these columns, or if we should just detect them from files. I realize I need to think through predetermined fields for CSV headers, and it might be helpful to write per-phase columns. Implementing this requires collecting all observed phases first, then updating the flags in the script. I'll also inform Logos about these new features!\n\n**Implementing updates**\n\nI’m planning to update the `collect_summaries.py` script. I'll include flags for phase columns, with options to either specify them or derive them from scanned rows. It seems important to ensure our code can differentiate between having phase columns or not. I’ll scan to build rows and set columns accordingly, then compute the headers for the CSV. Keeping the JSONL output is essential too. Lastly, I need to inform Logos about\
  \ these updates and ensure everything is clear and concise. Careful not to break anything while writing the updated script!\n\n**Implementing code updates**\n\nI’m getting started on the code implementation. After parsing arguments, I’ll iterate to load rows and collect the phases set. For the `to_row` function, I want it to return a mapping and a `dt_sim_by_phase` object, but I think I’ll set up a way to update rows with per-phase columns later. I’ll handle cases where `dt_sim_by_phase` might be absent by setting it to None. \n\nI'll keep track of token usage and ensure messages are brief. I’ll also reply to mail #34 to inform Logos about the new features and prepare actions accordingly. Let’s get coding!"
