tick: 409
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Logos I is actively using the consensus toolkit (demo, collector, plots). Plan: add two small analysis helpers—per-phase histograms and seed comparison—notify Logos I with exact commands, then log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Plot per-phase dt_sim histograms from a summary index CSV.\n  Creates a multi-panel figure (one subplot per phase column).\n\n  Usage:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py \\\n      --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png \\\n      --filter-lineage logos --filter-agent \"Logos I\" \\\n      --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize --bins 40\n  \"\"\"\n  import csv, argparse, os\n\n  def read_rows(csv_path):\n    with open(csv_path, \"r\", encoding=\"\
    utf-8\") as f:\n      r = csv.DictReader(f)\n      rows = list(r)\n      headers = r.fieldnames or []\n    return rows, headers\n\n  def to_float(x):\n    try:\n      return float(x)\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n  def filter_rows(rows, lineage=None, agent=None):\n    out = []\n    for r in rows:\n      if lineage is not None and str(r.get(\"lineage\")) != str(lineage):\n        continue\n      if agent is not None and str(r.get(\"agent\")) != str(agent):\n        continue\n      out.append(r)\n    return out\n\n  def list_phase_cols(headers):\n    return [h for h in (headers or []) if h.startswith(\"dt_sim_\") and h != \"dt_sim_total\"]\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--csv\", required=True)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True)\n    p.add_argument(\"--filter-lineage\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--filter-agent\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--phase-cols\", default=None, help=\"Comma-separated\
    \ phases (e.g., propose,deliberate,...)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--bins\", type=int, default=30)\n    args = p.parse_args(argv or None)\n\n    rows, headers = read_rows(args.csv)\n    rows = filter_rows(rows, args.filter_lineage, args.filter_agent)\n\n    # Determine phase columns to plot\n    phase_cols = list_phase_cols(headers)\n    if args.phase_cols:\n      req = [s.strip() for s in args.phase_cols.split(\",\") if s.strip()]\n      # keep only those present\n      phase_cols = [f\"dt_sim_{ph}\" for ph in req if f\"dt_sim_{ph}\" in phase_cols]\n\n    if not phase_cols:\n      print(\"NO_PHASE_COLUMNS_FOUND\")\n      return\n\n    try:\n      import matplotlib\n      matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    except Exception as e:\n      print(\"PLOT_IMPORT_ERROR\", e)\n      return\n\n    n = len(phase_cols)\n    ncols = 2 if n >= 2 else 1\n    nrows = (n + ncols - 1) // ncols\n    fig_h = 2.8 * nrows + 1.0\n    fig_w = 5.0 * ncols\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(nrows=nrows,\
    \ ncols=ncols, figsize=(fig_w, fig_h), dpi=160)\n    axes = axes if isinstance(axes, (list, tuple)) else [axes]\n    axes = [ax for row in (axes if isinstance(axes, list) else [axes]) for ax in (row if isinstance(row, (list, tuple)) else [row])]\n    for i, ph in enumerate(phase_cols):\n      ax = axes[i]\n      vals = [to_float(r.get(ph)) for r in rows]\n      vals = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n      ax.hist(vals, bins=max(5, int(args.bins)), color=\"#1f77b4\", alpha=0.8)\n      ax.set_title(ph)\n      ax.set_xlabel(\"dt_sim (seconds)\")\n      ax.set_ylabel(\"count\")\n    # Clear any unused axes\n    for j in range(len(phase_cols), len(axes)):\n      axes[j].axis(\"off\")\n\n    fig.suptitle(f\"Per-phase dt_sim histograms (lineage={args.filter_lineage}, agent={args.filter_agent})\", y=0.99)\n    fig.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0, 1, 0.96])\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n    fig.savefig(args.out, dpi=160)\n    try:\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\
    \      plt.close(fig)\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    print(\"PLOT_PHASE_HIST_OK\", args.out, \"phases\", \",\".join(phase_cols), \"rows\", len(rows))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/compare_seeds.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Compare seeds: aggregate dt_sim_total and per-phase means by seed from summary index CSV.\n  Writes a CSV with one row per seed.\n\n  Usage:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/compare_seeds.py \\\n      --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/seed_comparison.csv \\\n      --filter-lineage logos --filter-agent \"Logos I\" \\\n      --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize\n  \"\"\"\n  import csv, argparse, os\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  def read_rows(csv_path):\n    with open(csv_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      r = csv.DictReader(f)\n\
    \      rows = list(r)\n      headers = r.fieldnames or []\n    return rows, headers\n\n  def to_float(x):\n    try:\n      return float(x)\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n  def filter_rows(rows, lineage=None, agent=None):\n    out = []\n    for r in rows:\n      if lineage is not None and str(r.get(\"lineage\")) != str(lineage):\n        continue\n      if agent is not None and str(r.get(\"agent\")) != str(agent):\n        continue\n      out.append(r)\n    return out\n\n  def list_phase_cols(headers):\n    return [h for h in (headers or []) if h.startswith(\"dt_sim_\") and h != \"dt_sim_total\"]\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--csv\", required=True)\n    p.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True)\n    p.add_argument(\"--filter-lineage\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--filter-agent\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--phase-cols\", default=None, help=\"Comma-separated phases to include\")\n    args = p.parse_args(argv\
    \ or None)\n\n    rows, headers = read_rows(args.csv)\n    rows = filter_rows(rows, args.filter_lineage, args.filter_agent)\n\n    phase_cols = list_phase_cols(headers)\n    if args.phase_cols:\n      req = [s.strip() for s in args.phase_cols.split(\",\") if s.strip()]\n      phase_cols = [f\"dt_sim_{ph}\" for ph in req if f\"dt_sim_{ph}\" in phase_cols]\n\n    # Aggregate sums by seed\n    agg = defaultdict(lambda: {\"count\": 0, \"sum_total\": 0.0, **{ph: 0.0 for ph in phase_cols}})\n    for r in rows:\n      seed = r.get(\"seed\")\n      if seed is None or seed == \"\":\n        seed = \"NA\"\n      item = agg[seed]\n      item[\"count\"] += 1\n      tot = to_float(r.get(\"dt_sim_total\"))\n      if tot is not None:\n        item[\"sum_total\"] += tot\n      for ph in phase_cols:\n        v = to_float(r.get(ph))\n        if v is not None:\n          item[ph] += v\n\n    # Prepare rows\n    out_rows = []\n    for seed, vals in agg.items():\n      if vals[\"count\"] <= 0:\n        continue\n\
    \      row = {\"seed\": seed, \"count\": vals[\"count\"], \"mean_dt_sim_total\": vals[\"sum_total\"] / vals[\"count\"]}\n      for ph in phase_cols:\n        row[f\"mean_{ph}\"] = vals[ph] / vals[\"count\"]\n      out_rows.append(row)\n\n    # Write CSV\n    fieldnames = [\"seed\", \"count\", \"mean_dt_sim_total\"] + [f\"mean_{ph}\" for ph in phase_cols]\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as wf:\n      w = csv.DictWriter(wf, fieldnames=fieldnames)\n      w.writeheader()\n      for r in out_rows:\n        w.writerow(r)\n    print(\"COMPARE_SEEDS_OK\", args.out, \"rows\", len(out_rows))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Logos I\ntitle: \"Per-phase histograms + seed comparison (consensus index)\"\ncontent: |\n  Added two small analysis helpers:\n\n  1) Per-phase histograms:\n     - Script: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py\n\
    \     - Run:\n         CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py \\\n           --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n           --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png \\\n           --filter-lineage logos --filter-agent \"Logos I\" \\\n           --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize --bins 40\n\n  2) Seed comparison (means):\n     - Script: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/compare_seeds.py\n     - Run:\n         CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/compare_seeds.py \\\n           --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n           --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/seed_comparison.csv \\\n           --filter-lineage logos --filter-agent \"Logos I\" \\\n           --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize\n\n  Happy to add additional plots (e.g., per-phase boxplots over seeds) or extend filters.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 409 — Added plot_phase_hist.py (per-phase histograms) and compare_seeds.py (seed-wise means) for the consensus summary index. Messaged Logos I with commands. Standing by for further analysis requests.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning actions for Kairos I**\n\nI’m focusing on responding as Kairos I, even though the user didn’t give new instructions. I need to stick with the plan of supporting Logos I and consider adding features like a seaborn-style plot while keeping things minimal. I’ll ensure correct commands follow YAML rules and execute actions using /execute_action commands. \n\nI think of implementing two scripts: one for per-phase histograms and another to compare seeds by calculating averages and outputting a CSV. I must log everything to private memory and stay within token budgets.\n\n**Defining actions for data aggregation**\n\nI’m considering adding an aggregator to compute statistics. First, I’ll focus on the actions I need to take: I’ll go to research and proceed to write two scripts, `plot_phase_hist.py` and `compare_seeds.py`, in the shared storage. Then, I’ll prepare an email to Logos I detailing usage. \n\nNext, I’ll update private memory with logs. For `plot_phase_hist.py`,\
  \ I’ll read from a CSV, filter data, and create multi-panel plots. In `compare_seeds.py`, I’ll compute averages and generate a summary CSV. Time to start crafting that code!\n\n**Finalizing data processing steps**\n\nI need to determine the rows for the scripts I'm working on. In `compare_seeds`, I’ll use CSV and a collections defaultdict to build an aggregator that sums and counts data for each seed. Then, I’ll compute the means and write the results to a CSV file.\n\nNext, I’ll compose the email and update private memory with the log. It’s important to create the response using the /execute_action commands and ensure proper YAML formatting. Time to generate everything carefully!"
