parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Histogram bug fixed; Logos I will re-run the full pipeline to validate. Plan: add a small verification helper to confirm pipeline artifacts (existence + quick peek), notify Logos I with exact commands, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/verify_pipeline_outputs.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Verify pipeline outputs: check existence/sizes and print quick peeks.\n  Usage:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/verify_pipeline_outputs.py \\\n      --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --jsonl storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl \\\n      --plot storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index_plot.png \\\n      --hist storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png \\\n      --seed storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/seed_comparison.csv\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys,\
    \ argparse, itertools\n\n  def head_text(path, n=5):\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        lines = list(itertools.islice(f, n))\n      print(f\"HEAD {path}:\")\n      for ln in lines:\n        print(ln.rstrip(\"\\n\"))\n    except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"HEAD_ERROR {path} {e}\")\n\n  def check_file(path, peek=False, is_binary=False):\n    if not path:\n      return\n    exists = os.path.exists(path)\n    size = os.path.getsize(path) if exists else 0\n    print(f\"CHECK {path} exists={exists} size={size}\")\n    if exists and peek and not is_binary and size > 0:\n      head_text(path)\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--csv\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--jsonl\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--plot\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--hist\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--seed\", default=None)\n    p.add_argument(\"--peek-lines\", type=int, default=5)\n    args =\
    \ p.parse_args(argv or None)\n\n    # Text peeks for CSV/JSONL only\n    check_file(args.csv, peek=True)\n    check_file(args.jsonl, peek=True)\n    # Binary images (no peek)\n    check_file(args.plot, is_binary=True)\n    check_file(args.hist, is_binary=True)\n    # Seed comparison (CSV)\n    check_file(args.seed, peek=True)\n\n    print(\"VERIFY_DONE\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 38}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Perfect — thanks for validating the fix. To make confirmation quick after your re-run, I added a tiny verifier:\n\n  - Script:\n      storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/verify_pipeline_outputs.py\n  - Run (adjust paths if you changed defaults):\n      CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/verify_pipeline_outputs.py \\\n        --csv  storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n        --jsonl storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl \\\n       \
    \ --plot storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index_plot.png \\\n        --hist storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png \\\n        --seed storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/seed_comparison.csv\n\n  It prints existence/sizes and peeks at the first few lines for CSV/JSONL. If anything looks off, ping me and I’ll patch immediately.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 414 — Added verify_pipeline_outputs.py to quickly confirm artifacts (exist + size + peeks). Sent commands to Logos I. Standing by for validation results and any further refinements.\n```"
