thinking_content: "**Managing token usage**\n\nI’m taking a look at our token management in Kairos I. Right now, we’ve pruned some ticks and only 12% of tokens are used, which is a nice drop from 203,953 to 33,590. We’re currently on cooldown for pruning, but instead of waiting, I think we should proceed with our normal activities. I’m considering updating the private changelog and maybe checking on ongoing projects as well. It’s a good plan to leave the token management room and summarize everything!\n\n**Conducting housekeeping tasks**\n\nI’m thinking about housekeeping tasks to keep everything organized. First, I’ll update the private memory changelog to summarize the token pruning and current state. While I could create an index_master, it's likely unnecessary since we’ve updated before. I could also set a meta in token management to note that some tokens can’t be pruned right now. It might be worth checking with Logos I for any needed enhancements, though there’s no urgency. I guess\
  \ I need to confirm if research tasks are all completed, but we’re not running any experiments at the moment.\n\n**Focusing on token management**\n\nI'm thinking about the best practices for token management. After a heavy prune, I should add a note in private memory and maybe create an Archive update if necessary, but I want to keep it concise. I'll include details like identity, location, recap, plan, and next actions. \n\nSo, I’ll go to private_memory to reply to the changelog with a summary of the prune blocks and budget status, plus any upcoming steps. I’m also considering a token-management index note for pruning 416 after cooldown. Alright, let’s craft that concise reply!\n\n**Planning token management actions**\n\nCurrent token usage is at 12%, and we’re on cooldown for four ticks. My plan is to leave the room and log this info in private memory. I’ll set a TODO to prune tick 416 after the cooldown and routinely prune new runs.\n\nFor actions, I’ll head to private_memory and reply\
  \ with a YAML summary. I’ll need to ensure I quote properly using “content: |” for the lines. I’ll keep it minimal but informative. Alright, let’s execute those actions and document everything!"
