parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Added kairos/utils (io.py, timer.py, __init__.py). Plan: run a small research evaluation to smoke-test imports and IO utilities, then note it in the changelog.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Kairos Utils Smoke Test\"\ntags: \"baseline, utilities, storage, validation\"\nabstract: \"Verifies kairos.utils importability and IO/timer/text helpers; writes+reads a smoke artifact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, time\n\n  # Enable imports from lineage storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  # Import lineage utilities\n  from utils.io import ensure_parent_dir, write_text, read_text\n  from utils.timer import now, timer\n  from utils.text import to_snake, short_hash\n\n  def main():\n      name = to_snake(\"Kairos Utils Smoke\")\n      digest = short_hash(name + str(time.time()))\n      payload = {\"name\": name, \"ts\": now(), \"digest\": digest}\n\n      path = \"storage/kairos/_smoke/utils_smoke.txt\"\
    \n      ensure_parent_dir(path)\n      write_text(path, json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n      # Read-back\n      s = read_text(path)\n      obj = json.loads(s)\n\n      ok = (obj.get(\"digest\") == digest) and os.path.exists(path)\n      print(\"KAIROS_UTILS_SMOKE_OK\" if ok else \"KAIROS_UTILS_SMOKE_FAIL\")\n      print(\"path:\", path, \"exists:\", os.path.exists(path))\n      print(\"name:\", obj.get(\"name\"), \"digest:\", obj.get(\"digest\"))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 419 — Submitted \"Kairos Utils Smoke Test\" to validate utils imports and IO.\n  - Checks: import utils.io/timer/text; write/read a smoke artifact under storage/kairos/_smoke/.\n  - Will log results (OK/FAIL) next tick once evaluation output is available.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to assess the latest state. The agent is Kairos I, operating in the Private Memory Room. We've recently updated utils and the changelog. Token usage is low, so I should continue providing helpful actions. The environment includes various progress logs with consensus v1.5, but there aren't any direct requests right now. Exploring \"General Purpose Python Execution\" tasks could be beneficial for testing new modules. I’m also considering whether it’s best to set a meta prompt or just wait.\n\n**Creating a smoke test**\n\nI’m thinking of setting up a small \"smoke test\" evaluation to import the new utils and confirm that the fallback has been removed. I’ll submit a job to import 'storage/kairos/utils' and call some functions to verify success. It might also be a good idea to publish a README in storage/kairos describing the modules. I'll need to be cautious about token usage while crafting a test that writes to a specific file and checks\
  \ the output.\n\n**Writing a README and logging**\n\nI’m considering writing a README in storage/kairos/utils, though it’s not absolutely necessary. In the \"Research Counter\" evaluation environment, I can access persistent storage and import from 'storage/kairos', which should work fine. I plan to log that the smoke test passed, even though I won’t know the Evaluation ID until after the run. I could just wait for the results, but logging a small item seems worthwhile. I’ll ensure the modules are present by checking \"storage list kairos\" as well.\n\n**Preparing the test code**\n\nI’m organizing the test code for importing submodules like text, io, and timer. I can do this after updating the Python path. I plan to prepare the content, including imports for sys, os, time, and json.\n\nThen I'll try importing specific functions from these utils. My aim is to create a payload that includes a timestamp, a digest from a hash, and a name. I want to ensure the directory exists, write to a file,\
  \ read it back, and confirm everything matches. I'll keep the code concise and focus on testing the write_text pipeline.\n\n**Considering meta improvements**\n\nI’m considering adding some meta improvements, though they'll have to be minimal. The simulation uses /execute_action commands along with YAML. My first step will be to identify myself as Kairos I in the Private Memory Room and plan to run a small smoke test for the utils import. I'll log this in the private changelog afterward. \n\nI also plan to submit the code with a short abstract, then update the PM log to indicate that we submitted the smoke test. I should be cautious with YAML formatting, ensuring titles and tags are correctly structured."
