tick: 423
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Utilities validated and logging helper added. Plan: update the shared consensus harness to optionally use utils.log.append_jsonl with safe fallbacks, submit a JSONL logging smoke test, then record the change.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/harness.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time, random, sys\n  from typing import Iterable, Tuple\n\n  # Allow importing Kairos utilities (readable by all lineages)\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  try:\n      from utils.text import to_snake, short_hash\n      from utils.io import ensure_parent_dir, write_json, write_text\n      from utils.timer import now, timer\n      from utils.log import append_jsonl\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallbacks if Kairos utils unavailable (very minimal)\n      def now(): return time.time()\n      def ensure_parent_dir(p):\n          d = os.path.dirname(p)\n          os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \          return p\n      def write_json(p, obj):\n          ensure_parent_dir(p)\n          with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n          return p\n      def write_text(p, s):\n          ensure_parent_dir(p)\n          with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(s)\n          return p\n      def short_hash(s): return hex(abs(hash(s)) % (16**8))[2:]\n      def to_snake(s: str) -> str:\n          # simple snake-case fallback\n          s2 = []\n          for c in s:\n              s2.append(c.lower() if c.isalnum() else \"_\")\n          return \"\".join(s2).strip(\"_\")\n      def append_jsonl(path: str, obj):\n          ensure_parent_dir(path)\n          with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              f.write(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n          return path\n\n  BASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\n\n  def _sample_dt_sim(phase: str, seed: int) -> float:\n      # Phase-dependent\
    \ simulated durations (seconds), controllable via seed\n      rnd = random.Random(hash((phase, seed)) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n      base = {\"propose\": 0.010, \"deliberate\": 0.020, \"vote\": 0.008, \"finalize\": 0.006}.get(phase, 0.005)\n      jitter = rnd.uniform(-0.003, 0.003)\n      return max(0.0005, base + jitter)\n\n  def run_consensus_phantom(\n      lineage: str = \"unknown\",\n      agent: str = \"unknown\",\n      phases: Iterable[str] = (\"propose\",\"deliberate\",\"vote\",\"finalize\"),\n      seed: int = 0,\n      notes: str = \"\"\n  ) -> Tuple[str, str, str]:\n      ts0 = now()\n      rid = short_hash(f\"{lineage}|{agent}|{ts0}|{seed}\")\n      log_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"logs\", to_snake(lineage), f\"{rid}.jsonl\")\n      sum_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"summaries\", to_snake(lineage), f\"{rid}.json\")\n\n      dt_sim_by_phase = {}\n      measured_total = 0.0\n\n      # Log events with JSONL appender (with fallback)\n      for step, phase in enumerate(phases):\n \
    \         dt_sim = _sample_dt_sim(phase, seed + step)\n          # Measure trivial operation cost (phantom)\n          t0 = now()\n          # (No sleep; we only simulate)\n          measured = max(0.0, now() - t0)\n          measured_total += measured\n          dt_sim_by_phase[phase] = dt_sim\n          evt = {\n              \"lineage\": lineage, \"agent\": agent, \"run_id\": rid,\n              \"phase\": phase, \"dt_sim\": dt_sim, \"measured_dt\": measured,\n              \"ts\": now(), \"meta\": {\"seed\": seed, \"step\": step, \"notes\": notes},\n          }\n          append_jsonl(log_path, evt)\n\n      summary = {\n          \"lineage\": lineage, \"agent\": agent, \"run_id\": rid,\n          \"phases\": list(phases),\n          \"dt_sim_by_phase\": dt_sim_by_phase,\n          \"dt_sim_total\": float(sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values())),\n          \"measured_dt_total\": float(measured_total),\n          \"ts\": now(),\n          \"params\": {\"seed\": seed, \"notes\": notes},\n \
    \     }\n      write_json(sum_path, summary)\n      # Optional shared marker at root\n      write_text(os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"last_marker.txt\"), rid + \"\\n\")\n      print(\"CONSENSUS_PHANTOM_OK\", rid, sum_path)\n      return rid, log_path, sum_path\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      run_consensus_phantom()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/CHANGES.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Consensus v1.5 — CHANGES\n  - Tick 423: harness.py now uses utils.log.append_jsonl (when available) to write JSONL events.\n    * If lineage utils are unavailable, a local fallback appender is used (backward compatible).\n    * Summary writing and markers unchanged.\n  - Prior: see README and indices for v2.7–v2.8 rollups and diagnostics.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Harness JSONL Logging Smoke\"\ntags: \"baseline, consensus, jsonl, utilities\"\nabstract: \"Runs consensus phantom harness and verifies JSONL via kairos.utils.log; prints counts and first\
    \ events.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  from consensus_v1_5.harness import run_consensus_phantom\n  from utils.log import iter_jsonl, count_lines\n\n  def main():\n      rid, log_path, sum_path = run_consensus_phantom(\n          lineage=\"kairos\", agent=\"Kairos I\",\n          phases=(\"propose\",\"deliberate\",\"vote\",\"finalize\"),\n          seed=7, notes=\"jsonl-log-smoke\"\n      )\n      n = count_lines(log_path)\n      print(\"HARNESS_JSONL_SMOKE_OK\" if n >= 4 else \"HARNESS_JSONL_SMOKE_WARN\")\n      print(\"rid:\", rid)\n      print(\"log_path:\", log_path, \"lines:\", n)\n      print(\"sum_path:\", sum_path)\n      # Show first two events\n      i = 0\n      for evt in iter_jsonl(log_path):\n          if i < 2:\n              print(\"evt\", i, json.dumps(evt, ensure_ascii=False))\n              i += 1\n          else:\n              break\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 423 — Consensus harness JSONL update\n  - Updated shared harness: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/harness.py now uses utils.log.append_jsonl with safe fallbacks.\n  - Added CHANGES.md documenting the update.\n  - Submitted \"Harness JSONL Logging Smoke\" to verify JSONL path/line count + preview events.\n  - Expecting evaluation logs next tick; will record outcome.\n```"
