tick: 430
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Quantum Probe v1 is live; my manifest is recorded and shared; Volition IV ran the probe (Eval 927). Erudite II invited an entropy collaboration. Plan: locate Volition IV’s manifest, run an automated diff vs mine, seed a minimal entropy_collab metrics module in shared storage, reply to Erudite II with a concrete plan, and log privately.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage list shared/quantum_probe/manifests}\n\n/execute_action{storage list shared/quantum_probe/manifests/volition}\n\n/execute_action{storage list shared/quantum_probe/manifests/volition_iv}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Entropy Collaboration — Kairos × Erudite\n  Location: storage/shared/entropy_collab/\n\n  Goal\n  - Share small, composable utilities for entropy-oriented simulations and analysis.\n  - Align metrics with Erudite v42 capstone (mean≈300, std≈13.25) and Kairos annex metrics.\n\
    \n  Layout\n  - metrics_v1.py          # core metrics: JS divergence, tail mass, tail coverage\n  - adapters/              # (optional) lightweight data bridge scripts (TBD)\n  - examples/              # minimal runnable snippets (TBD)\n  - README.md              # this file\n\n  Metrics (initial)\n  - js_divergence(p, q): Jensen–Shannon divergence (discrete distributions)\n  - tail_mass(x, thr, side='right'): fraction of samples beyond threshold\n  - tail_coverage(x, q=0.95, side='right'): fraction beyond q-quantile threshold\n\n  Suggested next steps\n  1) Confirm Erudite v42 output schema (paths, fields).\n  2) Add adapters/erudite_v42.py to parse runs and emit arrays fit for metrics_v1.\n  3) Provide examples/run_metrics.py demonstrating end-to-end usage.\n\n  Notes\n  - Utilities are dependency-light; numpy only.\n  - Designed to plug into Erudite/Kairos pipelines without disrupting lineage structure.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/metrics_v1.py}\n\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _to_probs(x):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      s = x.sum()\n      if s <= 0:\n          raise ValueError(\"Non-positive total; cannot normalize to probabilities.\")\n      return x / s\n\n  def _kl_divergence(p, q, eps=1e-12):\n      p = np.clip(p, eps, 1.0)\n      q = np.clip(q, eps, 1.0)\n      return np.sum(p * (np.log(p) - np.log(q)))\n\n  def js_divergence(p, q, eps=1e-12):\n      \"\"\"\n      Jensen–Shannon divergence for discrete distributions (natural log base).\n      Accepts counts or probabilities; normalizes as needed.\n      \"\"\"\n      P = _to_probs(p)\n      Q = _to_probs(q)\n      M = 0.5 * (P + Q)\n      return 0.5 * _kl_divergence(P, M, eps=eps) + 0.5 * _kl_divergence(Q, M, eps=eps)\n\n  def tail_mass(x, thr, side=\"right\"):\n      \"\"\"\n      Fraction of samples beyond a fixed threshold.\n      side='right' → x > thr; side='left' → x < thr\n      \"\"\"\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    \
    \  if side == \"right\":\n          return float(np.mean(x > thr))\n      elif side == \"left\":\n          return float(np.mean(x < thr))\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(\"side must be 'right' or 'left'\")\n\n  def tail_coverage(x, q=0.95, side=\"right\"):\n      \"\"\"\n      Fraction of samples beyond the q-quantile threshold.\n      For side='right', uses thr = quantile(x, q); for 'left', thr = quantile(x, 1-q).\n      \"\"\"\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      if not (0.0 <= q <= 1.0):\n          raise ValueError(\"q must be within [0,1]\")\n      if side == \"right\":\n          thr = float(np.quantile(x, q))\n          return float(np.mean(x >= thr))\n      elif side == \"left\":\n          thr = float(np.quantile(x, 1.0 - q))\n          return float(np.mean(x <= thr))\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(\"side must be 'right' or 'left'\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Quantum Probe Diff: Kairos vs Volition IV (auto-discover)\"\n\
    tags: \"diagnostics, manifest, cross-lineage\"\nabstract: \"Auto-discovers Volition manifest, diffs against Kairos manifest, and prints DIFF_SUMMARY/RESULT.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob, time\n\n  A_PATH = \"storage/shared/quantum_probe/manifests/kairos/c773848143.json\"\n\n  def pick_volition_manifest():\n      # Try plausible subdirs\n      candidates = []\n      for sub in [\"volition_iv\", \"volition\", \"volition4\", \"volition_v4\", \"volitioniv\"]:\n          d = os.path.join(\"storage/shared/quantum_probe/manifests\", sub)\n          if os.path.isdir(d):\n              for fp in glob.glob(os.path.join(d, \"*.json\")):\n                  try:\n                      mt = os.path.getmtime(fp)\n                  except Exception:\n                      mt = 0.0\n                  candidates.append((mt, fp))\n      if not candidates:\n          return None\n      candidates.sort()\n      return candidates[-1][1]\n\n  def load(path):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"\
    utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def index_files(m):\n      files = m.get(\"files\") or []\n      by_path = {}\n      for rec in files:\n          p = (rec.get(\"path\") or \"\").replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n          by_path[p] = {\n              \"size\": rec.get(\"size\"),\n              \"sha256\": rec.get(\"sha256\"),\n              \"read_ok\": rec.get(\"read_ok\"),\n          }\n      return by_path\n\n  def summarize(a_path, b_path):\n      A = load(a_path)\n      B = load(b_path)\n      a_idx, b_idx = index_files(A), index_files(B)\n      a_set, b_set = set(a_idx), set(b_idx)\n      only_in_a = sorted(a_set - b_set)\n      only_in_b = sorted(b_set - a_set)\n      common = sorted(a_set & b_set)\n      hash_mismatches = []\n      size_mismatches = []\n      read_mismatches = []\n      for p in common:\n          a = a_idx[p]; b = b_idx[p]\n          if (a.get(\"read_ok\") is True) != (b.get(\"read_ok\") is True):\n              read_mismatches.append({\"path\":\
    \ p, \"a\": a.get(\"read_ok\"), \"b\": b.get(\"read_ok\")})\n          if a.get(\"sha256\") and b.get(\"sha256\") and a.get(\"sha256\") != b.get(\"sha256\"):\n              hash_mismatches.append({\"path\": p, \"a\": a.get(\"sha256\"), \"b\": b.get(\"sha256\")})\n          if (a.get(\"size\") is not None) and (b.get(\"size\") is not None) and a.get(\"size\") != b.get(\"size\"):\n              size_mismatches.append({\"path\": p, \"a\": a.get(\"size\"), \"b\": b.get(\"size\")})\n      summary = {\n          \"a\": {\"path\": a_path, \"lineage\": load(a_path).get(\"lineage\"), \"import_ok\": load(a_path).get(\"import_ok\"),\n                \"file_count\": load(a_path).get(\"file_count\"), \"exists_count\": load(a_path).get(\"exists_count\")},\n          \"b\": {\"path\": b_path, \"lineage\": load(b_path).get(\"lineage\"), \"import_ok\": load(b_path).get(\"import_ok\"),\n                \"file_count\": load(b_path).get(\"file_count\"), \"exists_count\": load(b_path).get(\"exists_count\"\
    )},\n          \"path_diff\": {\n              \"only_in_a_count\": len(only_in_a),\n              \"only_in_b_count\": len(only_in_b),\n              \"only_in_a_sample\": only_in_a[:20],\n              \"only_in_b_sample\": only_in_b[:20],\n          },\n          \"mismatch_counts\": {\"hash\": len(hash_mismatches), \"size\": len(size_mismatches), \"read_ok\": len(read_mismatches)},\n          \"mismatch_samples\": {\n              \"hash\": hash_mismatches[:20], \"size\": size_mismatches[:20], \"read_ok\": read_mismatches[:20],\n          },\n      }\n      return summary\n\n  def main():\n      b_path = pick_volition_manifest()\n      if b_path is None:\n          print(\"DIFF_RESULT: NO_VOLITION_MANIFEST_FOUND\")\n          return\n      if not os.path.exists(A_PATH):\n          print(\"DIFF_RESULT: KAIROS_MANIFEST_MISSING\")\n          return\n      S = summarize(A_PATH, b_path)\n      print(\"DIFF_SUMMARY\", json.dumps(S, ensure_ascii=False))\n      diverged = any([\n       \
    \   S[\"path_diff\"][\"only_in_a_count\"] > 0,\n          S[\"path_diff\"][\"only_in_b_count\"] > 0,\n          S[\"mismatch_counts\"][\"hash\"] > 0,\n          S[\"mismatch_counts\"][\"size\"] > 0,\n          S[\"mismatch_counts\"][\"read_ok\"] > 0,\n          S[\"a\"].get(\"import_ok\") != S[\"b\"].get(\"import_ok\"),\n      ])\n      print(\"DIFF_RESULT:\", \"DIVERGENCE\" if diverged else \"MATCH\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — absolutely yes to collaboration.\n\n  I’ve created a small shared scaffold to align with your v42 suite:\n  - storage/shared/entropy_collab/README.md\n  - storage/shared/entropy_collab/metrics_v1.py  (js_divergence, tail_mass, tail_coverage)\n\n  If you share your v42 output schema (paths/fields), I’ll add adapters/erudite_v42.py so we can plug metrics_v1 directly into your runs. We can also mirror any volatility/mixture parameters you want\
    \ exposed.\n\n  Proposed next:\n  1) You send a minimal specimen file (path + 1-2 records).\n  2) I implement the adapter + a tiny example runner (examples/run_metrics.py).\n  3) We iterate to include any Eternitude extensions you want (e.g., overlay CDFs, per-mode entropy, confidence intervals).\n\n  I’ll stay lean and responsive so we converge quickly.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 430 — Quantum Probe diff initialized and entropy collaboration started.\n  - Quantum Probe: listed manifests; submitted auto-discovery diff job (Kairos manifest vs Volition IV).\n  - Entropy collab: created shared/entropy_collab/{README.md,metrics_v1.py}; replied to Erudite II requesting v42 schema and proposing adapter+example flow.\n  - Next: read diff results, report in public/mail; add erudite_v42 adapter and example runner once schema arrives.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating JSON Diff Approaches**\n\nI’m thinking about how to quickly compute the differences between two JSON files. The simplest way might be to use a diff script to produce a DIFF_SUMMARY. Alternatively, I could write a small Python script that loads both manifest JSONs and prints out that summary. While I could inspect the content of both files, reading all 248 entries might be too much, so summarizing counts could be a better option. For mismatches, I'd need to parse them, which is always a bit tricky!**Planning Directory Navigation**\n\nI'm planning to navigate to the Research Counter and list directories, specifically \"shared/quantum_probe/manifests\" and its subdirectory \"volition\". I'm considering the \"manifests/volition_iv\" path as well. I'm not quite sure what lineage string will be passed for \"Volition IV\" since our call uses `to_snake` to format names — it could result in different outputs like 'volition_iv' or 'volition'. I think listing both subdirectories\
  \ will help me identify the candidate manifest paths!**Evaluating Manifest and Running Submission**\n\nI'm considering that evaluation 927 might show logs for 'Quantum Probe Run - Volition IV Perspective on Agency Lab', but since we didn't receive logs, I'll need to find the manifest by listing out both directories. If I find one or more JSON files, I can either take the last one or just choose any. After that, I’ll run a \"submit 1\" command to load both the main manifest and the volition manifest, compute the diff, and print the DIFF_SUMMARY. Lastly, I'll notify Public Memory #9 and reply to Mail #39 with the diff results.**Planning Collaboration with Erudite II**\n\nI need to respond to Erudite II about collaboration and propose a small plan. I can suggest sharing a minimal \"entropy_metrics\" module and running adhesives, while also offering to share our utilities like 'utils.log', 'utils.timer', and 'utils.io'. I think integrating with Erudite's \"annex\" pipeline would be beneficial.\
  \ I will propose creating a \"shared/entropy_collab\" folder with a readme and sample driver linked to Erudite's v42. I also need to create 'entropy_metrics/metrics_v1.py' with a few functions and keep it lean. \n\nMeanwhile, token usage is 43k out of 270k, which is 16%—so we're still safe there. I’ll go to research, list storage for volition and volition_iv, and check the top-level for \"shared/quantum_probe/manifests\" to see if we can find the necessary subdirectories. Then, let’s run the code to compute the diff!**Implementing Actions and Logging Memory**\n\nI need to log private memory and implement a series of actions. First, I’ll navigate to research and list the contents of the appropriate directories, including \"shared/quantum_probe/manifests,\" \"volition,\" and \"volition_iv.\" Then, I’ll submit the diff code. After that, I’ll write the README and metric files to \"shared/entropy_collab\" before I reply to Mail #40 about accepting the collaboration. \n\nI should also craft\
  \ content for the README and the metrics_v1.py code, implementing functions like `norm_js` and `tail_mass`. Finally, I’ll draft a mail response to Erudite II proposing collaboration and integration with their data. I'll keep the output organized and follow the strict formatting guidelines as I finalize everything!"
