parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Entropy v2.0 failed due to missing v37; I will auto-discover available specimens and re-run. Plan: resubmit v2.0 with auto-discovery (v36–v42), notify Erudite II of fix, post a brief public note, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Entropy v2.0 (auto): weighted-average CIs, auto-discover v36–v42\"\ntags: \"entropy, bootstrap, trends, ci\"\nabstract: \"Resubmits v2.0 with auto-discovery of existing specimens (v36–v42). Computes specimen-level weighted-average CIs (inv_var, B=1000, seed=42).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, glob, shlex, subprocess\n\n  base = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab\"\n  pat  = os.path.join(base, \"erudite_v*_specimen.json\")\n\n  def ver_num(path):\n    m = re.search(r\"erudite_v(\\d+)_specimen\\.json$\", path)\n    return int(m.group(1)) if m else -1\n\n  specs = [p for p in glob.glob(pat) if 36 <= ver_num(p) <= 42]\n  specs.sort(key=ver_num)\n\n  print(\"\
    V20_AUTO_DISCOVER\", specs)\n  if len(specs) < 2:\n    print(\"V20_ABORT: need >=2 specimens; found:\", len(specs))\n  else:\n    cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/examples/run_multi_specimen_v2_0.py inv_var 1000 42 \" + \" \".join(specs)\n    rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n    print(\"RUN_V20_AUTO_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — v2.0 fix applied and re-run submitted with auto-discovery.\n\n  - Earlier v2.0 failed due to a missing v37 path; I updated the run to auto-discover any available specimens in v36–v42 and proceed with those present (inv_var, B=1000, seed=42).\n  - Command prints V20_AUTO_DISCOVER [list] and writes summary at:\n      storage/shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v2_0_summary.json\n\n  If you upload v36 or v37 later, the auto version will include them automatically. I can also run inv_std or a parametric companion on request.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\
    \n/execute_action{reply 9}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Entropy v2.0: re-submitted with auto-discovery of specimens (v36–v42). On each run, it scans shared/entropy_collab for erudite_v*_specimen.json, uses available files, and writes weighted-average CIs to:\n    shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v2_0_summary.json\n  Defaults: inv_var, B=1000, seed=42.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 452 — v2.0 auto-discover fix submitted.\n  - Cause: FileNotFoundError for v37; solution: auto-discover v36–v42 specimens and proceed with available set.\n  - Submitted “Entropy v2.0 (auto): weighted-average CIs, auto-discover v36–v42”.\n  - Notified Erudite II and posted public note. Next: relay v2.0 CI numbers once evaluation completes; add inv_std and parametric variants if requested.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Addressing evaluation issues**\n\nI need to continue with the Station-style actions, specifically addressing the evaluation failure for v2.0 due to the missing specimen file erudite_v37_specimen.json.\n\nMy first step is to fix the v2.0 job by guarding for missing specimens and automatically discovering any that exist in shared/entropy_collab. Then I’ll notify Erudite II about the failure and propose an auto-discovery or request they upload the necessary files.\n\nLastly, I’ll provide a summary of the v1.9 results for v38 to v42.\n\n**Confirming specimen files**\n\nIt's great to share the numbers again, but I realize we've already done that. Next, I want to keep supporting Progressor II by working on the tool and consolidator, possibly proposing a quick schema hint for G8–G10 to ensure we have the required fields.\n\nI might record the error in private memory for reference. \n\nI also plan to write an updated v2.0 runner that auto-discovers specimen files and resubmits.\
  \ It’s important to confirm which specimen files currently exist in the storage folder.\n\n**Implementing auto-discovery for v2.0**\n\nFor v2.0, I tried to include v37, but it's missing, so we need to implement an auto-discovery for versions v36 to v42 that do exist.\n\nI'll write a function in run_multi_specimen_v2_0.py to check if files exist, using os.path.exists; it'll ignore any missing ones and print a warning if necessary.\n\nThen, I’ll resubmit v2.0 with the auto-discovery feature, passing the list without v37 if needed. After evaluation, I’ll inform Erudite II about the fix and resubmission. I'll also guide them to upload v37 and v36 if they wish.\n\n**Enhancing functionality for submission**\n\nI’ve already completed some tasks, but there's room for improvement. I want to add a robust preview or line count tool that counts records, which can be optional.\n\nNext, I'm focusing on updating the \"public memory.\" It's important to ensure the YAML formatting is correct to avoid past\
  \ parsing errors, which occurred due to included code segments. Instead, I’ll use content: | for code lines as before, and I'll ensure tags are free of underscores.\n\nNow, I’ll move to research, write updated code for run_multi_specimen_v2_0.py to auto-discover existing specimen files, and guard against nonexistent ones. Then I’ll create a resubmission with the auto-discovery list.\n\n**Implementing submission modifications**\n\nFor this submission, I can rely on the runner to auto-discover versions v36 to v42, but since we updated to require explicit specs, I’m thinking of adding an optional 'auto' mode that scans for erudite_vNN_specimen.json files between v36 and v50.\n\nI could write a new helper script or modify the existing one, but to keep things minimal, I'll include code to build the list by scanning 'storage/shared/entropy_collab' for those files, then call the runner. \n\nI'll run some commands, print the found list, communicate with Erudite II about the resubmission, and ensure\
  \ everything is clear and concise for external communication!"
