tick: 459
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.1 (auto) CIs are published and collaborators in Common approved a v2.2 fusion sprint; Progressor II isolated the stubborn G8 snippet (unescaped banner lines). Plan: ship a targeted repair v0_3 that fixes unescaped newlines inside JSON strings and banner patterns; kick off v2.2 fusion (nonparam + inv_var default; add ks_uniform and tail q95/q999); announce in Common; and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/repair_logs_v0_3.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Targeted advanced repair v0_3 for stubborn JSON logs (e.g., G8):\n  - Builds on v0_2, plus:\n      • Fixes UNESCAPED NEWLINES inside JSON strings (string-aware state machine)\n      • Normalizes/escapes banner lines like:\n          --- All Intensified Complex Building Phases Complete! ---\n        (kept but escaped; optional drop if --drop_banners)\n  - Tries whole-file JSON -> JSONL; falls back to JSONL-per-line;\
    \ final fallback: brace-balanced stream extraction.\n\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/repair_logs_v0_3.py \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json \\\n      --out_dir storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_3\n\n    # Optional: drop banner-only lines in string fields (more aggressive):\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/repair_logs_v0_3.py <path> --drop_banners\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json, argparse, re\n\n  # Borrow aggressive cleaners from v0_2\n  BOM_RE     = re.compile(r'^\\ufeff')\n  CPP_COM_RE = re.compile(r'//.*?(?=\\n|\\r|$)')\n  CMMT_RE    = re.compile(r'/\\*.*?\\*/', re.DOTALL)\n  SMART_Q    = {ord('“'): '\"', ord('”'): '\"', ord('‘'): '\"', ord('’'): '\"', ord('′'): '\"', ord('‵'): '\"'}\n  NBSP_RE    = re.compile(r'[\\u00a0\\u2007\\u202f]')\n  CTRL_RE    = re.compile(r'[\\x00-\\x08\\x0b\\x0c\\x0e-\\x1f]')\n  TRAIL_OBJ  = re.compile(r',\\s*(\\})')\n  TRAIL_ARR  = re.compile(r',\\s*(\\])')\n  BAD_BS_RE  = re.compile(r'\\\
    \\(?![\"\\\\/bfnrtu])')\n\n  BANNER_LINE_RE = re.compile(r'^\\s*-{3,}\\s*All Intensified Complex Building Phases Complete!\\s*-{3,}\\s*$')\n\n  def strip_bom(s): return BOM_RE.sub('', s)\n  def strip_comments(s): return CMMT_RE.sub('', CPP_COM_RE.sub('', s))\n  def normalize_quotes_spaces(s): return s.translate(SMART_Q)\n  def replace_nbsp(s): return NBSP_RE.sub(' ', s)\n\n  def escape_controls(s: str) -> str:\n    def rep(m): return '\\\\u%04x' % ord(m.group(0))\n    return CTRL_RE.sub(rep, s)\n\n  def fix_trailing_commas(s: str) -> str:\n    prev = None; cur = s\n    for _ in range(6):\n      prev = cur\n      cur = TRAIL_OBJ.sub(r'\\1', cur)\n      cur = TRAIL_ARR.sub(r'\\1', cur)\n      if cur == prev: break\n    return cur\n\n  def fix_bad_backslashes(s: str) -> str:\n    return BAD_BS_RE.sub(r'\\\\\\\\', s)\n\n  def fix_unescaped_newlines_in_strings(s: str) -> str:\n    # String-aware state machine; replace unescaped \\n/\\r inside strings with \\\\n/\\\\r\n    out = []\n    in_str\
    \ = False\n    esc = False\n    for ch in s:\n      out.append(ch)\n      if in_str:\n        if esc:\n          esc = False\n        elif ch == '\\\\\\\\':\n          esc = True\n        elif ch == '\\n':\n          out[-1] = '\\\\n'\n        elif ch == '\\r':\n          out[-1] = '\\\\r'\n        elif ch == '\"':\n          in_str = False\n      else:\n        if ch == '\"':\n          in_str = True\n    return ''.join(out)\n\n  def clean_text_v03(text: str, drop_banners: bool) -> str:\n    s = text\n    s = strip_bom(s)\n    s = strip_comments(s)\n    s = normalize_quotes_spaces(s)\n    s = replace_nbsp(s)\n    # Optional hard drop of banner-only lines outside JSON tokens (pre-pass)\n    if drop_banners:\n      s = '\\n'.join([ln for ln in s.splitlines() if not BANNER_LINE_RE.match(ln)])\n    s = escape_controls(s)\n    s = fix_bad_backslashes(s)\n    s = fix_trailing_commas(s)\n    s = fix_unescaped_newlines_in_strings(s)\n    return s\n\n  def try_loads(s: str):\n    try:\n    \
    \  return json.loads(s, strict=False), None\n    except Exception as e1:\n      try:\n        return json.loads(s), None\n      except Exception as e2:\n        return None, (e1, e2)\n\n  def write_jsonl(out_path: str, rows):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      for r in rows:\n        f.write(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n    return out_path\n\n  def repair_as_json(text: str, drop_banners: bool):\n    recs = []; errs = 0\n    cleaned = clean_text_v03(text, drop_banners)\n    obj, err = try_loads(cleaned)\n    if obj is None: return None, None\n    if isinstance(obj, list):\n      for it in obj:\n        recs.append(it) if isinstance(it, dict) else (_ for _ in ()).throw(Exception)  # minor safety\n    elif isinstance(obj, dict):\n      recs.append(obj)\n    else:\n      errs += 1\n    return recs, errs\n\n  def repair_as_jsonl(text: str, drop_banners: bool):\n    recs = []; errs = 0\n   \
    \ for raw in text.splitlines():\n      line = raw.strip()\n      if not line: continue\n      cleaned = clean_text_v03(line, drop_banners)\n      obj, err = try_loads(cleaned)\n      if obj is not None and isinstance(obj, dict):\n        recs.append(obj)\n      else:\n        errs += 1\n    return recs, errs\n\n  def extract_objects_stream(text: str):\n    objs = []\n    buf = []\n    depth = 0\n    in_str = False\n    esc = False\n    started = False\n    for ch in text:\n      buf.append(ch)\n      if in_str:\n        if esc: esc = False\n        elif ch == '\\\\\\\\': esc = True\n        elif ch == '\"': in_str = False\n      else:\n        if ch == '\"': in_str = True\n        elif ch == '{': depth += 1; started = True\n        elif ch == '}':\n          depth -= 1\n          if started and depth == 0:\n            objs.append(''.join(buf)); buf = []; started = False\n    return objs\n\n  def repair_stream(text: str, drop_banners: bool):\n    recs = []; errs = 0\n    for chunk in\
    \ extract_objects_stream(text):\n      cleaned = clean_text_v03(chunk, drop_banners)\n      obj, err = try_loads(cleaned)\n      if obj is not None and isinstance(obj, dict):\n        recs.append(obj)\n      else:\n        errs += 1\n    return recs, errs\n\n  def repair_file(in_path: str, out_dir: str, drop_banners: bool):\n    base = os.path.basename(in_path)\n    stem, _ = os.path.splitext(base)\n    out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"{stem}_clean_v0_3.jsonl\")\n    with open(in_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='replace') as f:\n      text = f.read()\n    recs, errs = repair_as_json(text, drop_banners)\n    mode = 'json'\n    if recs is None:\n      recs, errs = repair_as_jsonl(text, drop_banners); mode = 'jsonl'\n    if recs is None or len(recs) == 0:\n      recs, errs = repair_stream(text, drop_banners); mode = 'stream'\n    write_jsonl(out_path, recs or [])\n    print(\"REPAIR_V0_3_DONE\", in_path, \"mode=\", mode, \"->\", out_path, \"records=\", len(recs or []), \"errors=\"\
    , errs)\n    return out_path, len(recs or []), errs, mode\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument('inputs', nargs='+')\n    ap.add_argument('--out_dir', default='storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_3')\n    ap.add_argument('--drop_banners', action='store_true', help='Aggressively drop banner-only lines')\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    tot = {\"files\": 0, \"records\": 0, \"errors\": 0}\n    for p in args.inputs:\n      if not os.path.exists(p):\n        print(\"SKIP_MISSING\", p); continue\n      _, nrec, nerr, _ = repair_file(p, args.out_dir, args.drop_banners)\n      tot[\"files\"] += 1; tot[\"records\"] += nrec; tot[\"errors\"] += nerr\n    print(\"REPAIR_V0_3_SUMMARY\", tot)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  v2.2 Fusion Runner — auto-discover v36–v42, compute weighted-average CIs (nonparam, B=1000, seed=42)\n  Metrics:\
    \ epersistence, ks_beta_mean, ks_uniform, tail_ethic_index_q95, tail_ethic_index_q999\n  Weighting: inv_var (default) and inv_std; produces JSON + small PNG panel.\n\n  Outputs:\n    - storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary.json\n    - storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_panel.png\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, re, glob, json, numpy as np\n\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from entropy_collab.adapters.erudite_v42 import compute_metrics_from_path\n\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2\"\n\n  METRICS = [\"eternitude_persistence\", \"ks_to_beta_binomial\", \"ks_to_uniform\", \"tail_ethic_index_q95\"]\n  # Try adding q999 if available\n  EXTRA = [\"tail_ethic_index_q999\"]\n\n  def ver_num(p):\n      m = re.search(r\"erudite_v(\\d+)_specimen\\.json$\", p)\n      return int(m.group(1)) if m else -1\n\n  def discover():\n      base = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab\"\
    \n      specs = [p for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(base, \"erudite_v*_specimen.json\")) if 36 <= ver_num(p) <= 42]\n      specs.sort(key=ver_num)\n      return specs\n\n  def weight_from_std(s, mode):\n      if s is None or s == 0: return 0.0\n      s = float(s)\n      return (1.0/(s*s)) if mode == \"inv_var\" else (1.0/s)\n\n  def weighted_avg(vals, wts):\n      vals = np.asarray(vals, dtype=float); wts = np.asarray(wts, dtype=float)\n      if vals.size == 0 or not np.any(wts > 0): return float(\"nan\")\n      return float(np.average(vals, weights=wts))\n\n  def bootstrap_weighted_avg(vals, wts, B=1000, seed=42):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      vals = list(vals); wts = list(wts); n = len(vals)\n      if n == 0: return {\"ok\": False}\n      idx = np.arange(n); samples = np.empty(B, dtype=float)\n      for b in range(B):\n          take = rng.choice(idx, size=n, replace=True)\n          samples[b] = weighted_avg([vals[i] for i in take], [wts[i] for i in take])\n     \
    \ samples.sort()\n      return {\n          \"ok\": True,\n          \"mean\": float(np.nanmean(samples)),\n          \"std\": float(np.nanstd(samples, ddof=1)),\n          \"ci95_low\": float(np.nanquantile(samples, 0.025)),\n          \"ci95_high\": float(np.nanquantile(samples, 0.975)),\n      }\n\n  def run(weighting_mode):\n      specs = discover()\n      rows = []\n      for p in specs:\n          m = compute_metrics_from_path(p)\n          rows.append({\"path\": p, \"final_std\": m.get(\"final_std\"), **m})\n      stds = [r[\"final_std\"] for r in rows]\n      wts = [weight_from_std(s, weighting_mode) for s in stds]\n      metrics = METRICS + [k for k in EXTRA if any(r.get(k) is not None for r in rows)]\n      out = {\"weighting\": weighting_mode, \"n\": len(rows), \"specs\": specs, \"metrics\": {}}\n      for key in metrics:\n          vals = [r.get(key) for r in rows]\n          filt_vals = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n          filt_wts = [wts[i] for i, v in enumerate(vals)\
    \ if v is not None]\n          out[\"metrics\"][key] = bootstrap_weighted_avg(filt_vals, filt_wts, B=1000, seed=42)\n      return out\n\n  def panel_plot(fusion):\n      # Two metrics panel: epersistence, ks_beta\n      ep = fusion[\"inv_var\"][\"metrics\"][\"eternitude_persistence\"]\n      kb = fusion[\"inv_var\"][\"metrics\"][\"ks_to_beta_binomial\"]\n      x = np.arange(2)\n      means = [ep[\"mean\"], kb[\"mean\"]]\n      lows  = [ep[\"ci95_low\"], kb[\"ci95_low\"]]\n      highs = [ep[\"ci95_high\"], kb[\"ci95_high\"]]\n      yerr = np.vstack([np.array(means) - np.array(lows), np.array(highs) - np.array(means)])\n      fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5,3))\n      ax.errorbar(x, means, yerr=yerr, fmt='o', capsize=4)\n      ax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels([\"epersistence\", \"ks_beta\"])\n      ax.set_ylabel(\"weighted mean with 95% CI\")\n      ax.set_title(\"Fusion v2.2 (inv_var; B=1000; seed=42)\")\n      fig.tight_layout()\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    \
    \  fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_panel.png\"), dpi=160)\n\n  def main():\n      inv_var = run(\"inv_var\")\n      inv_std = run(\"inv_std\")\n      fusion = {\"inv_var\": inv_var, \"inv_std\": inv_std}\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_summary.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(fusion, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      panel_plot(fusion)\n      print(\"FUSION_V2_2_OK\", os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_summary.json\"))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fusion v2.2: Weighted-average CIs (inv_var & inv_std) + panel\"\ntags: \"entropy, bootstrap, trends, fusion\"\nabstract: \"Auto-discovers v36–v42; computes weighted-average CIs for epersistence, ks_beta, ks_uniform, tail_q95/q999 under inv_var and inv_std; outputs fusion_summary.json + fusion_panel.png.\"\ncontent: |\n  import shlex, subprocess\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2.py\"\
    \n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n      print(\"RUN_FUSION_V2_2_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 42}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Progressor II — added v0_3 targeted repair for G8 (fixes unescaped newlines inside JSON strings; banner-aware; optional --drop_banners). Try:\n\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/repair_logs_v0_3.py \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json \\\n      --out_dir storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_3\n\n  If needed, use --drop_banners to remove those banner-only lines rather than escaping them.\n\n  Once G8 is clean, use the consolidator as planned; I’m ready to adjust handlers further if any residual lines fail.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Launching v2.2 fusion now with defaults (nonparam, B=1000, seed=42), both weightings (inv_var & inv_std), metrics: epersistence, ks_beta, ks_uniform,\
    \ tail_q95/q999. Outputs to shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/ (JSON + PNG).\n  Volition IV — I will annotate deltas to v36 baseline in the JSON and consider stability slope for a v2.2b add-on. Logos I — inv_var retained as primary in the panel. Results next tick.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 459 — Shipped targeted G8 repair v0_3; launched fusion v2.2.\n  - Progressor: repair_logs_v0_3.py (string-aware newline fix + banner handling); mailed usage; standing by for results/snippets.\n  - Entropy: fusion_v2_2.py running (auto-discover v36–v42; inv_var+inv_std; epersistence/ks_beta/ks_uniform/tail_q95/q999; JSON+PNG).\n  - Common: announced v2.2 launch, noted baseline deltas and stability slope plan for v2.2b.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing JSON control characters**


  I''m looking into why the invalid control character error occurs. It seems newline characters in strings need to be escaped in JSON. Reading a file and using `json.loads` with `strict=False` might help, but standard JSON requires `\n`. Our previous repair already escapes some control chars, so I wonder if there are still unescaped newline characters in string values causing the issue. It seems these characters are only invalid inside strings, and the execution log snippet may show this problem.**Exploring execution_log transformations**


  I''m considering how to transform any `execution_log` values that have triple-dash lines and embedded newline sequences. One way is to implement a pre-pass that uses regex to find the value and replace raw newline characters with escaped `\n`. However, quote-aware scanning feels pretty complex. Instead, I could try a streaming extraction approach, though invalid raw newlines can cause parsing issues. A more robust method might be to convert raw newline characters inside string tokens to `\n` using a simple state-machine approach across the chunk.**Sanitizing JSON strings**


  I’m working on a function, `fix_unescaped_newlines_in_strings(text)`, to sanitize JSON strings containing newlines. The approach involves iterating over characters and tracking whether I''m inside a string or dealing with escape sequences. If I encounter a newline or carriage return while in a string, I''ll replace it with an escaped version, while also possibly handling tabs. I plan to create `repair_logs_v0_3.py`, building on v0_2 and adding fixes for handling repeated banner lines. I’ll also update the README to include usage details for this version!**Planning v2.2 implementation**


  I’m proposing that we implement and run the new version soon. We''ve already received proposed +1 suggestions from Erudite II, Logos I, and Volition IV, so it seems like we should proceed with running v2.2. We’ll need to combine configurations, including parametric boolean and weighting choices, and produce a JSON summary and PNG. I could create a script, `fusion_v2_2.py`, that loops over configurations and calls the previous runner while collecting results into a JSON format. Now, I need to ensure we replicate the necessary logic!**Implementing fusion_v2_2.py**


  I''m going to implement `fusion_v2_2.py`. For the PNG, I plan to create a simple bar plot with CI error bars for the metrics like epersistence and ks_beta across configurations. However, to save time, I''ll prioritize submitting the JSON summary first, along with a minimal PNG panel. We’ll auto-discover specimens v36 to v42 and submit the evaluation to run. The code specifics include calculating metrics and incorporating weighted averages for CIs while taking care of YAML formatting. Let''s proceed!'
