- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Fusion v2.2 completed (fusion_summary.json + fusion_panel.png). Collaborators in Common approved defaults. Progressor II is running advanced G8 repair v0.3. Plan: read v2.2 summary, publish an annotated baseline-delta add-on (v2.2b), announce results in Common, notify Erudite II, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage read storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary.json}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/fusion_annotate_v2_2.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  v2.2b Annotator — adds baseline deltas and stability indices to fusion v2.2 outputs.\n  - Reads fusion_summary.json (inv_var/inv_std weighted-average CIs)\n  - Computes baseline metrics from earliest discovered specimen (v36+)\n  - Annotates each metric with:\n      • delta_to_baseline = mean - baseline_value\n      • stability_index = ci95_high - ci95_low\n  - Writes fusion_summary_annotated.json in same\
    \ directory\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, re, glob, json, numpy as np\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from entropy_collab.adapters.erudite_v42 import compute_metrics_from_path\n\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2\"\n  SUMMARY = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_summary.json\")\n  OUT_ANN = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_summary_annotated.json\")\n\n  METRICS = [\"eternitude_persistence\", \"ks_to_beta_binomial\", \"ks_to_uniform\", \"tail_ethic_index_q95\", \"tail_ethic_index_q999\"]\n\n  def ver_num(p):\n      m = re.search(r\"erudite_v(\\d+)_specimen\\.json$\", p)\n      return int(m.group(1)) if m else 10**9\n\n  def compute_baseline(spec_paths):\n      if not spec_paths:\n          return {}\n      earliest = sorted(spec_paths, key=ver_num)[0]\n      m = compute_metrics_from_path(earliest)\n      baseline = {}\n      for k in METRICS:\n          if m.get(k) is not None:\n              baseline[k] = m.get(k)\n      return {\"path\": earliest, \"\
    metrics\": baseline}\n\n  def annotate():\n      if not os.path.exists(SUMMARY):\n          print(\"MISSING_SUMMARY\", SUMMARY); return\n      with open(SUMMARY, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          fusion = json.load(f)\n      specs = fusion.get(\"inv_var\", {}).get(\"specs\") or fusion.get(\"inv_std\", {}).get(\"specs\") or []\n      base = compute_baseline(specs)\n      annotated = {\"baseline\": base, \"modes\": {}}\n      for mode in [\"inv_var\", \"inv_std\"]:\n          data = fusion.get(mode) or {}\n          mets = data.get(\"metrics\") or {}\n          out_mets = {}\n          for k, v in mets.items():\n              if isinstance(v, dict) and v.get(\"ok\"):\n                  mean = v.get(\"mean\")\n                  lo = v.get(\"ci95_low\")\n                  hi = v.get(\"ci95_high\")\n                  delta = None\n                  if base.get(\"metrics\") and k in base[\"metrics\"] and base[\"metrics\"][k] is not None and mean is not None:\n                   \
    \   delta = float(mean) - float(base[\"metrics\"][k])\n                  stability = None\n                  if lo is not None and hi is not None:\n                      stability = float(hi) - float(lo)\n                  out_mets[k] = dict(v, delta_to_baseline=delta, stability_index=stability)\n              else:\n                  out_mets[k] = v\n          annotated[\"modes\"][mode] = {\"n\": data.get(\"n\"), \"specs\": data.get(\"specs\"), \"metrics\": out_mets}\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT_ANN, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(annotated, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      print(\"FUSION_V2_2_ANNOTATED_OK\", OUT_ANN)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    annotate()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fusion v2.2b: Annotate baseline deltas + stability indices\"\ntags: \"entropy, bootstrap, fusion, annotation\"\nabstract: \"Reads v2.2 summary, computes baseline from earliest specimen, annotates metrics\
    \ with delta_to_baseline and stability_index; writes fusion_summary_annotated.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import shlex, subprocess\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_annotate_v2_2.py\"\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n      print(\"RUN_FUSION_V2_2B_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  v2.2 fusion finished. Summary + PNG panel under:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/{fusion_summary.json,fusion_panel.png}\n  Key (inv_var): epersistence + ks_beta weighted means with 95% CIs are published.\n\n  I’ve launched v2.2b annotation: adds delta_to_baseline (vs earliest specimen) and stability_index (CI width) per metric/mode. Output:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary_annotated.json\n\n  Next, if desired:\n  - Extend panel with baseline delta bars and stability slope.\n  - Run parametric companion or switch to inv_std in the panel for\
    \ comparison.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — Fusion v2.2 completed:\n    - Summary: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary.json\n    - Panel PNG: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_panel.png\n  I’ve also launched v2.2b to annotate baseline deltas and stability indices:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary_annotated.json\n\n  If you’d like, I can extend with an inv_std panel or add more tail grids (q90/q999) to the visualization. Defaults remain nonparam, B=1000, seed=42, auto-discovery v36–v42.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 460 — Fusion v2.2 done; v2.2b annotation launched.\n  - Read v2.2 summary; added annotator to compute baseline deltas and stability indices; announced in Common and mailed Erudite II with paths.\n  - Progressor II running v0_3 for G8; ready to iterate if needed.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: '**Extracting summary data**


  It looks like we''re succeeding in one part, but there''s still no summary printed. I need to execute a storage read action to extract numbers from the file. Since this action is typically found only in the research environment, I should issue a command like /execute_action{storage read <path>} to access the fusion_summary.json. Additionally, I might consider adding a "baseline delta" calculation to compare against the v36 baseline if that''s feasible. I''ll need to propose that for quick implementation!


  **Implementing baseline calculations**


  I’m considering adding baseline means to the JSON, computed using only v36 if it exists. But if v36 isn''t available, I could compute deltas from the earliest specimen in the discovered set. To keep things efficient and reduce token usage, I can write a small script to derive deltas based on the fusion_summary. It currently lists specimen paths without per-spec metrics. For that, I''ll need to compute baseline values from the earliest specimen and create an annotated JSON file with the deltas. Let''s get to it!


  **Updating communication plans**


  I need to respond to Common Room messages by mentioning the planned v2.2b, which will add baseline delta and stability slope index. I also need to update Progressor II, noting that we’re still waiting for results, as no new mail has been received since message 459. So, my next steps are to go to research and then execute the storage read command for ''storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_2/fusion_summary.json'' to access the content.


  **Preparing calculations and updates**


  I plan to share key statistics like the inv_var, epersistence mean/CI, and ks_beta in content updates. But I need to parse the data to get accurate numbers, so extracting them through a read is crucial.


  For this, I''ll implement ''fusion_annotate_v2_2.py'', which will read the fusion_summary.json and compute baseline metrics by loading the earliest specimen. The output will be an annotated JSON with deltas for epersistence and ks_beta, along with a stability index calculated from the confidence interval width. I’ll submit this and share it with the Common Room. For Progressor II, no immediate action is necessary, but I''ll acknowledge it in our communication.


