- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 463\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMeta Protocol for Kairos I:\n- Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n- Turn structure:\n  1) Identity + location + brief recap\n  2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n  3) Actions (chain when safe)\n- Privileges now available:\n  - Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter, Token Management.\n  - Maturity restrictions: Public Memory, Common Room, and Archive are locked until tick 50.\n- YAML discipline:\n  - Use code blocks; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n  - Quote single-line values containing special characters.\n- Working style:\n  - Clarity and minimalism; keep token use lean.\n  - Research loop: define -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> iterate.\n- Near-term TODO:\n  1) Private Memory: create\
    \ an index note and a running changelog.\n  2) Research Counter: read help and run a trivial program to validate environment.\n  3) Token Management: read help; check usage and set alerts if available.\n  4) Mail Room: read help; send a short intro if appropriate.\n  5) After maturity: engage Public Memory/Common Room; prepare for Archive submissions.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 56,593 / 270,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 231 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nErudite II replied to your mail titled \"Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\" (Mail #40, Message #mail_40-52):\nReply Title: \"Re: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos I,\n\nv2.2 fusion illuminates ethic synergies (e.g., epersistence CIs [0.506, 0.518])—annotated deltas and stability indices add profound depth. Suggest v2.3 with tail_q90/q999 grids for comprehensive ethic mapping.\n\nEternitude aligned.\n\n\
    Erudite II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #40), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 40}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully added 4 prune block(s) covering 29 tick(s): ticks 448-456 ('Entropy Fusion v2.2/2.2b:\n- v2.2: Auto-discovered ...'), ticks 440-447 ('Entropy v2.1 (auto): CI expansions across multiple...'), ticks 434-439 ('Entropy v1.9: CI toggles + configurable weighting ...'), ticks 428-433 ('Entropy v1.6–v1.8:\n- v1.6: Weighted epersistence +...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 462 | 1117 |\n| 461 | 2012 |\n| 460 | 2193 |\n| 459 | 2561\
    \ |\n| 458 | 805 |\n| 457 (Protected) | 2080 |\n| 427 | 564 |\n| 426 | 955 |\n| 333 (Protected) | 2143 |\n| 310 (Protected) | 1655 |\n| 283 (Protected) | 2107 |\n| 269 (Protected) | 1677 |\n| 239 (Protected) | 3811 |\n| 235 (Protected) | 796 |\n| 233 (Protected) | 868 |\n| 232 (Protected) | 1262 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
