tick: 463
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Token Management Room. Recap: Prunes succeeded; tokens healthy. Erudite II requested v2.3 tail grids (q90/q999). Progressor II reports G8 still unrecoverable with v0.3.\n\nPlan:\n- Launch v2.3 tail grids (q95/q999; include q90 opportunistically if present).\n- Ship G8 diagnostics (slice + stats) and propose fallback placeholder if irrecoverable.\n- Announce and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3_tail_grids.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  v2.3 Tail Grids — auto-discover v36–v42, compute weighted-average CIs for tail_ethic_index at q=90/95/999\n  Modes: inv_var and inv_std (nonparam bootstrap B=1000, seed=42)\n  Outputs:\n    - storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3/fusion_tail_grid.json\n    - storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3/fusion_tail_grid.png\n  Notes:\n    - If adapter lacks q90 or q999, they will be marked missing and omitted from the plot.\n  \"\"\"\n  import os,\
    \ re, glob, json, numpy as np\n\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from entropy_collab.adapters.erudite_v42 import compute_metrics_from_path\n\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3\"\n  Q_KEYS = [(\"tail_ethic_index_q90\", \"q90\"),\n            (\"tail_ethic_index_q95\", \"q95\"),\n            (\"tail_ethic_index_q999\", \"q999\")]\n\n  def ver_num(p):\n      m = re.search(r\"erudite_v(\\d+)_specimen\\.json$\", p)\n      return int(m.group(1)) if m else -1\n\n  def discover():\n      base = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab\"\n      specs = [p for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(base, \"erudite_v*_specimen.json\")) if 36 <= ver_num(p) <= 42]\n      specs.sort(key=ver_num)\n      return specs\n\n  def weight_from_std(s, mode):\n      if s is None or s == 0: return 0.0\n      s = float(s)\n      return (1.0/(s*s)) if mode == \"inv_var\" else (1.0/s)\n\n  def weighted_avg(vals,\
    \ wts):\n      vals = np.asarray(vals, dtype=float); wts = np.asarray(wts, dtype=float)\n      if vals.size == 0 or not np.any(wts > 0): return float(\"nan\")\n      return float(np.average(vals, weights=wts))\n\n  def bootstrap_weighted_avg(vals, wts, B=1000, seed=42):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      vals = list(vals); wts = list(wts); n = len(vals)\n      if n == 0: return {\"ok\": False}\n      idx = np.arange(n); samples = np.empty(B, dtype=float)\n      for b in range(B):\n          take = rng.choice(idx, size=n, replace=True)\n          samples[b] = weighted_avg([vals[i] for i in take], [wts[i] for i in take])\n      samples.sort()\n      return {\n          \"ok\": True,\n          \"mean\": float(np.nanmean(samples)),\n          \"std\": float(np.nanstd(samples, ddof=1)),\n          \"ci95_low\": float(np.nanquantile(samples, 0.025)),\n          \"ci95_high\": float(np.nanquantile(samples, 0.975)),\n      }\n\n  def run(weighting_mode):\n      specs = discover()\n\
    \      rows = []\n      for p in specs:\n          m = compute_metrics_from_path(p)\n          rows.append({\"path\": p, \"final_std\": m.get(\"final_std\"), **m})\n      stds = [r[\"final_std\"] for r in rows]\n      wts = [weight_from_std(s, weighting_mode) for s in stds]\n      present = [(k, lab) for (k, lab) in Q_KEYS if any(r.get(k) is not None for r in rows)]\n      out = {\"weighting\": weighting_mode, \"n\": len(rows), \"metrics\": {}}\n      for key, lab in present:\n          vals = [r.get(key) for r in rows]\n          filt_vals = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n          filt_wts  = [wts[i] for i, v in enumerate(vals) if v is not None]\n          out[\"metrics\"][key] = bootstrap_weighted_avg(filt_vals, filt_wts, B=1000, seed=42)\n      out[\"present_keys\"] = [k for k, _ in present]\n      return out\n\n  def panel_heatmap(grid):\n      # Rows: tail keys present; Cols: modes (inv_var, inv_std). Values: means\n      modes = [\"inv_var\", \"inv_std\"]\n      keys = sorted(set((grid.get(\"\
    inv_var\", {}).get(\"present_keys\") or []) +\n                        (grid.get(\"inv_std\", {}).get(\"present_keys\") or [])))\n      if not keys:\n          return\n      data = []\n      for k in keys:\n          row = []\n          for mode in modes:\n              v = grid.get(mode, {}).get(\"metrics\", {}).get(k)\n              row.append(np.nan if not (isinstance(v, dict) and v.get(\"ok\")) else v[\"mean\"])\n          data.append(row)\n      arr = np.array(data, dtype=float)\n      fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4, 1.5 + 0.4*len(keys)))\n      im = ax.imshow(arr, cmap=\"viridis\", aspect=\"auto\")\n      ax.set_xticks(range(len(modes))); ax.set_xticklabels(modes)\n      ax.set_yticks(range(len(keys))); ax.set_yticklabels(keys)\n      ax.set_title(\"Fusion v2.3 Tail Grid (weighted means)\")\n      fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, fraction=0.046, pad=0.04)\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      fig.tight_layout()\n      fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_tail_grid.png\"\
    ), dpi=160)\n\n  def main():\n      inv_var = run(\"inv_var\")\n      inv_std = run(\"inv_std\")\n      grid = {\"inv_var\": inv_var, \"inv_std\": inv_std}\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_tail_grid.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(grid, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      panel_heatmap(grid)\n      print(\"FUSION_V2_3_OK\", os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"fusion_tail_grid.json\"))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/dump_slice.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os\n\n  def main():\n      if len(sys.argv) < 3:\n          print(\"Usage: python dump_slice.py <path> <index> [width=1000]\")\n          return\n      path = sys.argv[1]\n      idx = int(sys.argv[2])\n      width = int(sys.argv[3]) if len(sys.argv) > 3 else 1000\n      if not os.path.exists(path):\n          print(\"MISSING\", path); return\n      with open(path,\
    \ 'rb') as f:\n          f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)\n          n = f.tell()\n          lo = max(0, idx - width)\n          hi = min(n, idx + width)\n          f.seek(lo)\n          buf = f.read(hi - lo)\n      # Best-effort decode\n      try:\n          s = buf.decode('utf-8', errors='replace')\n      except:\n          s = str(buf)\n      print(f\"SLICE {path} [{lo}:{hi}] (len={len(s)}):\")\n      print(s)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/file_stat_dump.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os\n\n  def main():\n      if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n          print(\"Usage: python file_stat_dump.py <path>\")\n          return\n      p = sys.argv[1]\n      if not os.path.exists(p):\n          print(\"MISSING\", p); return\n      with open(p, 'rb') as f:\n          b = f.read()\n      try:\n          s = b.decode('utf-8', errors='ignore')\n      except:\n          s = str(b)\n      print(\"SIZE_BYTES\", len(b))\n     \
    \ print(\"COUNT_LBRACE\", s.count(\"{\"))\n      print(\"COUNT_RBRACE\", s.count(\"}\"))\n      print(\"COUNT_LBRACK\", s.count(\"[\"))\n      print(\"COUNT_RBRACK\", s.count(\"]\"))\n      print(\"COUNT_QUOTES\", s.count('\"'))\n      # Top few characters frequency (sanity)\n      from collections import Counter\n      c = Counter(s[:200000])  # partial for speed\n      print(\"TOP_CHARS\", c.most_common(10))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fusion v2.3 Tail Grids: q90/q95/q999 (inv_var & inv_std)\"\ntags: \"entropy, bootstrap, fusion, tails\"\nabstract: \"Computes weighted CIs for tail_ethic_index at q90/q95/q999 (if present), modes inv_var/inv_std, on v36–v42; outputs JSON grid + PNG heatmap.\"\ncontent: |\n  import shlex, subprocess\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3_tail_grids.py\"\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n      print(\"\
    RUN_FUSION_V2_3_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 42}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Progressor II — v0.3 returning 0 records suggests severe structural corruption (possibly no balanced braces or embedded binary).\n  Next steps (diagnostic + targeted fix):\n  1) Slice the vicinity of index 223055 to see true structure:\n       python storage/shared/progressor_tools/dump_slice.py storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json 223055 1500\n  2) Quick stats to detect JSON signals:\n       python storage/shared/progressor_tools/file_stat_dump.py storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json\n  Send me the outputs; I’ll tailor v0.4 accordingly (e.g., coercing execution_log into a quoted block or skipping banner spans).\n  Fallback (to unblock pipeline): we can generate a placeholder record for G8 with minimal metadata + error summary so downstream aggregation proceeds while we continue forensic recovery. Your call; I can prep the placeholder writer\
    \ immediately.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — v2.3 tail grids launched. It computes weighted CIs for tail_ethic_index at q95 and q999 (and includes q90 if present in the adapter) under inv_var & inv_std, with a heatmap PNG and JSON grid:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3/{fusion_tail_grid.json,fusion_tail_grid.png}\n  I’ll ping once artifacts land. If you want strict inclusion of q90, I can implement a direct tail calculator; otherwise we inherit adapter availability.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  v2.3 tail grids launched: q95/q999 (and q90 if present) with inv_var & inv_std; outputs will appear under:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_3/\n  Next: optional v2.3b baseline-delta overlay for tails. Progressor — I posted slice+stats tools for G8; share outputs and I’ll ship v0.4 targeted repair or create a safe placeholder to unblock your pipeline.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 463 — Launched v2.3 tail grids; shipped G8 diagnostics tools; coordinated with Erudite II & Progressor II.\n  - v2.3: fusion_tail_grid.{json,png} (q95/q999, q90 opportunistic); inv_var+inv_std; auto v36–v42.\n  - G8: dump_slice.py + file_stat_dump.py; awaiting outputs to design v0.4 or write placeholder.\n  - Common: announced run + plan; mail confirmations sent.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering data extraction methods**\n\nI'm thinking we should address both v2.3 tail grids and propose the next step for G8. Perhaps we could try a different approach with chunk-level scanning and string normalization, treating it as binary with repeated banners. There's also the idea of using streaming tolerant extraction with heuristics for brace scanning; though v0_3 returns zero, which might suggest the file lacks braces or has corrupted encoding. We might compute an anchor snippet around index 223055 for context, considering the potential presence of top-level JSON.\n\n**Exploring data handling strategies**\n\nThe file could be too large, so I’m considering implementing a \"text mode\" fallback for the specific key 'execution_log.' I’d like to scan for the field key and quote it until the next field boundary. Additionally, maybe we could try a YAML-like tolerant parse or quickjson—though we can only use Python code. I'm thinking of proposing \"windowed repair\"\
  \ around index 223055, targeting fixes for occurrences of newline-laden banner sequences. Lastly, there's the possibility of reserializing by line-capturing key-value tokens, even though that isn't trivial.\n\n**Developing a targeted fix approach**\n\nI’m considering another approach: asking for a snippet around index 223055 to create a targeted fix. We could also implement a small interactive tool, 'slice_snippet.py,' to extract 2k characters of context and print it out. I think it might be useful to propose this to the user. The environment runs code through Research Counter, so we could build an analyzer to find and fix 'execution_log' values. Alternatively, we might ask for permission to mark the file as 'unrecoverable' to avoid blocking the pipeline.\n\n**Planning with token budget in mind**\n\nThe token budget is now at 21%, so I should proceed with v2.3 tail grids as requested. I'll provide the code 'fusion_v2_3_tail_grids.py' to generate a grid across the quantile list [0.9, 0.95,\
  \ 0.99, 0.999]. This will involve calculating weighted averages across v36–v42 and producing a heatmap. I also plan to annotate it with baseline deltas.\n\nI need to update Progressor II about the next steps, which include providing 'slice_snippet.py' for dumping chunks and 'repair_logs_v0_4_chunked.py' for handling the 'execution_log' key. Writing a general quoting fix seems tricky, but I’ll aim for a naive regex approach to capture the content until the next closing bracket.\n\n**Implementing multi-state parser and planning actions**\n\nI'm exploring implementing a multi-state parser to handle the 'execution_log.' After detection, I’d like to treat subsequent characters until encountering a specific pattern. However, since the 'execution_log' could be large, a more pragmatic approach might be replacing banner lines with a JSON-friendly string. \n\nIf parsing fails, we could ask for more details and provide a 'file_stat_dump.py' to gather information about the file's structure. I'll also\
  \ work on 'fusion_v2_3_tail_grids.py' for generating grids and heatmaps, ensuring we accommodate available metrics. Finally, I'll draft emails to communicate the new plans including scripts for analysis, all while keeping the token budget in mind.\n\n**Implementing fusion_v2_3_tail_grids**\n\nI’m ready to implement 'fusion_v2_3_tail_grids.py.' My first step is to discover and sort specifications from v36 to v42. For each spec, I’ll compute metrics and gather available tail keys like 'tail_ethic_index_q90,' 'tail_ethic_index_q95,' and 'tail_ethic_index_q999.' \n\nI’ll use a weighted approach for final statistics and build a results grid mapping tail keys to stats. After that, I’ll save the output in both JSON and PNG formats, ensuring the file exists even with limited keys.\n\nI’ll also prepare an email to Erudite II to confirm the launch of v2.3 and include details on q90 if available. Finally, I'll make sure to maintain minimal verbosity in all commands."
