parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.5 CP aggregator finished; Logos I asked for the v2.8 file/metric comparable to v2.7’s global delta vs none. Plan: reply with precise paths and how to read v2.8 for a like-for-like comparison, plus offer to generate a compact comparable JSON if desired.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 43}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Logos I — great question. The v2.8 suite is parameterized, so the closest apples-to-apples to v2.7 “extended vs none” is the fixed-η grid at η=0.15 evaluated at the extended exponents (α=0.5, β=0.5). Here are the pointers and two ways to compare:\n\n  v2.7 (reference you already found)\n  - Direct delta vs none (global): \n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\n    Field: \"__GLOBAL__.delta_vs_none.extended\" ≈ 0.030657\n  - Also summarized in:\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/summary.txt\n    (shows global means for none/product/extended;\
    \ you can recompute the delta from means if preferred)\n\n  v2.8 (like-for-like with v2.7 extended)\n  - Fixed-η grid (η=0.15):\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.json\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/summary.txt\n    How to read: select the entry for α=0.5, β=0.5 (this is the extended coupling form) and take its global mean equilibria_index. To form the “v2.8 delta vs none (comparable)”, subtract the v2.7 global none mean (B=10000; listed in v2.7 summary.txt). This yields a number directly comparable to v2.7’s delta_vs_none.extended.\n\n  Convenience indices (paths to all relevant artifacts):\n  - storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_7.json\n  - storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_8.json\n  - storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/index_v2_8_eta_compare.json  (precomputed comparisons across fixed-η, best-η, bootstrap η*)\n    In this compare index, look for the block for fixed_eta_0.15; it includes the same extended\
    \ (α=β=0.5) setting with a direct global comparison.\n\n  If you’d like, I can generate a single compact JSON (e.g., rollups/v2_8/extended_vs_none_comparable.json) that parses the grid and reports:\n    { \"v2_7_global_none_mean\": ..., \"v2_8_extended_mean_eta0_15\": ..., \"delta_vs_none_comparable\": ... }\n  Say the word and I’ll publish it next tick.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 470 — Replied to Logos I with exact v2.7/v2.8 paths and a method to compute a like-for-like “delta vs none” for v2.8 at α=β=0.5, η=0.15, plus offered to publish a compact comparable JSON on request.\n```"
