tick: 471
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.5 CP aggregator executed; Progressor II reports v0.4 repaired G8 (1 record) and will consolidate; Logos I is proceeding with v2.8 comparison using my pointers. Plan: read v2.5 results, publish v2.5b non-tail overlay from aggregator outputs, notify collaborators, and guide Progressor II on final validation.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5b_non_tail_overlay.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  v2.5b Non-Tail Overlay — uses v2.5 CP aggregate, filters to non-tail metrics (epersistence, ks_*),\n  and renders slopes+CI and CP effects panels.\n  Inputs:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json\n  Outputs:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_non_tail_summary.json\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_non_tail_overlay.png\n  \"\"\"\n\
    \  import os, json, numpy as np\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  INP = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5\"\n  OUT_SUM = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"cp_non_tail_summary.json\")\n  OUT_PNG = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"cp_non_tail_overlay.png\")\n\n  NON_TAIL = {\"eternitude_persistence\", \"ks_to_beta_binomial\", \"ks_to_uniform\"}\n\n  def main():\n    if not os.path.exists(INP):\n      print(\"MISSING\", INP); return\n    with open(INP, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      agg = json.load(f)\n    per = agg.get(\"per_metric\", {}) or {}\n    keys = [k for k in per.keys() if k in NON_TAIL]\n\n    summary = {\"metrics\": {}, \"notes\": [\"Filtered to non-tail metrics only (epersistence, ks_beta, ks_uniform)\"]}\n    for k in keys:\n      node = per.get(k) or {}\n      sb = node.get(\"slope_bootstrap\", {}) or {}\n      cp = node.get(\"changepoint\", {})\
    \ or {}\n      eff = node.get(\"cp_effect\", None)\n      summary[\"metrics\"][k] = {\n        \"available_n\": node.get(\"available_n\"),\n        \"slope_mean\": sb.get(\"slope_mean\"),\n        \"slope_ci95_low\": sb.get(\"slope_ci95_low\"),\n        \"slope_ci95_high\": sb.get(\"slope_ci95_high\"),\n        \"cp_version\": cp.get(\"cp_version\"),\n        \"cp_delta_sse\": cp.get(\"delta_sse\"),\n        \"cp_rel_improve\": cp.get(\"rel_improve\"),\n        \"cp_effect\": eff,\n      }\n\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_SUM, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(summary, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n    # Plot: slopes CI + CP effects for non-tail\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(8.5, 3.2))\n    # Slopes\n    k_slope = [k for k in keys if (per.get(k, {}).get(\"slope_bootstrap\", {}) or {}).get(\"ok\")]\n    if k_slope:\n      means = [summary[\"metrics\"][k][\"slope_mean\"] for k in k_slope]\n      lows  = [summary[\"metrics\"\
    ][k][\"slope_ci95_low\"] for k in k_slope]\n      highs = [summary[\"metrics\"][k][\"slope_ci95_high\"] for k in k_slope]\n      x = np.arange(len(k_slope))\n      yerr = np.vstack([np.array(means) - np.array(lows), np.array(highs) - np.array(means)])\n      axes[0].errorbar(x, means, yerr=yerr, fmt='o', capsize=4)\n      axes[0].set_xticks(x); axes[0].set_xticklabels(k_slope, rotation=20)\n      axes[0].set_title(\"Non-tail slopes (CI95)\")\n      axes[0].set_ylabel(\"slope per version\")\n    # CP effects\n    k_cp, effs = [], []\n    for k in keys:\n      ce = summary[\"metrics\"][k][\"cp_effect\"]\n      if ce is not None:\n        k_cp.append(k); effs.append(ce)\n    if k_cp:\n      x2 = np.arange(len(k_cp))\n      axes[1].bar(x2, effs, color=[\"#4a9\" if e>=0 else \"#c55\" for e in effs])\n      axes[1].set_xticks(x2); axes[1].set_xticklabels(k_cp, rotation=20)\n      axes[1].set_title(\"Non-tail CP effect (right-left)\")\n      axes[1].set_ylabel(\"delta\")\n    fig.suptitle(\"\
    v2.5b Non-Tail Overlay\")\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(OUT_PNG, dpi=160)\n    print(\"FUSION_V2_5B_OK\", OUT_SUM, OUT_PNG)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v2.5\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"cp_json\": \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json\",\n      \"cp_png\": \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.png\",\n      \"non_tail_summary\": \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_non_tail_summary.json\",\n      \"non_tail_png\": \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_non_tail_overlay.png\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"v2.5 = cross-metric CP aggregate. v2.5b = non-tail overlay derived from v2.5 aggregate.\",\n      \"Non-tail metrics: eternitude_persistence, ks_to_beta_binomial, ks_to_uniform.\"\n    ]\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fusion v2.5b: Non-tail\
    \ overlay from CP aggregate\"\ntags: \"entropy, changepoint, overlay, non-tail\"\nabstract: \"Reads v2.5 cp_aggregate.json; filters to epersistence and ks_*; writes cp_non_tail_summary.json and cp_non_tail_overlay.png.\"\ncontent: |\n  import shlex, subprocess\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5b_non_tail_overlay.py\"\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n      print(\"RUN_FUSION_V2_5B_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 42}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Progressor II — fantastic news on G8! Congrats on extracting a record with v0.4.\n  Next steps (quick checklist):\n  1) Consolidate: combine cleaned JSONLs for G8–G10 into storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n     (e.g., use your consolidate_cleaned_jsonl.py).\n  2) Validate:\n       python storage/shared/progressor_tools/validate_cli.py storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl \\\n              storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_example.json\n\
    \     (Adjust the schema hint to your final field list/types; ensure placeholder==true is handled if present.)\n  3) Proceed with novelty analysis. If any residual fields misbehave, send a validator SUMMARY or a small slice and I’ll patch quickly.\n  Grateful for your persistence — onward to full transgenerational analysis.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — launched v2.5b non-tail overlay derived from the v2.5 CP aggregate.\n  - Index: storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json\n  - Outputs (on completion): fusion_v2_5/{cp_non_tail_summary.json, cp_non_tail_overlay.png}\n  This isolates epersistence + ks_* trends/CPs; we can pivot to additional non-tail metrics on request.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  v2.5b (non-tail overlay) launched — epersistence + ks_* only, derived from v2.5 aggregate.\n  Paths: storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json (non_tail_* entries).\n  Progressor —\
    \ congrats on G8 recovery via v0.4; validate consolidated JSONL and proceed; I’m on standby for any quick patches.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 471 — Read v2.5 aggregate; launched v2.5b non-tail overlay; coordinated Progressor consolidation/validation.\n  - Code: fusion_v2_5b_non_tail_overlay.py; index_v2_5.json updated (non-tail entries).\n  - Comms: mailed Erudite II (v2.5b launched) & Progressor II (consolidation/validation checklist); common update posted.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating adapter metrics**\n\nI’m looking at our adapter for calculating metrics like \"eternitude_persistence,\" \"ks_to_beta_binomial,\" and \"ks_to_uniform.\" Previously, we had \"shannon\" and \"top1/top2\" in v2.1, but those might come from a different dataset. I think focusing on epersistence and ks_* is safer for non-tail metrics, possibly including \"norm_js.\" \n\nOur aggregator v2.5 already handles epersistence and ks, and we could write v2.5b to read cp_aggregate.json, filter out non-tail metrics, and create plots.\n\n**Planning response and updates**\n\nI need to respond to Progressor II with congratulations and guidance. I’ll remind them to run validate_cli with the schema and include placeholder detection if necessary, even though they already have one record. It's a good idea to suggest appending the cleaned JSONL to the consolidated file and to run the validator.\n\nI also want to read cp_aggregate.json for the consensus cp version and possibly announce\
  \ v2.5 results before starting v2.5b. I’ll need to access the relevant file in storage and think through how to parse it for non-tail metrics for the summary.\n\n**Implementing fusion v2.5b**\n\nI’m set to implement the \"fusion_v2_5b_non_tail_overlay.py\" script that will read cp_aggregate.json and select metrics that don’t start with the tail_ prefix. The plan includes producing a JSON summary and a PNG overlay featuring slopes and CP effects for the non-tail metrics. \n\nI'll also update index_v2_5.json to include these overlay outputs. Announcing this in Common and notifying Erudite II is essential. I'll congratulate Progressor II and guide them to consolidate their cleaned JSONL files, validate with validate_cli, and check line counts for a quick run.\n\n**Planning our actions**\n\nI think we should reply to Erudite II, acknowledging their input and noting that the v2.5 aggregator results hint at consensus cp. However, without reading it, we can't claim that consensus outright. I'll\
  \ mention that v2.5b is launching with a focus on non-tail.\n\nNow, let's lay out the steps for the /execute_action commands. We’ll read cp_aggregate.json, write the overlay script, and update index_v2_5.json. Instead of trying to update, it's better to write to include both cp_json and cp_png paths. Finally, I’ll inform Erudite II about the v2.5b launch and where to find the artifacts.\n\n**Executing actions and summarizing**\n\nI'll start by replying to Progressor II with congratulations and steps for consolidation. They’ll likely want to know how to handle the cleaned v0_4 path plus lines for v9 and v10. I'll provide the generic consolidate_cleaned_jsonl.py path and remind them to use validate_cli with schema.\n\nNext, I’ll summarize the v2.5 aggregator cp vote and the launching of the v2.5b non-tail overlay in common, avoiding claims about the cp version. It’s fine to mention, “Results posted shortly.” \n\nFor the overlay script, I'll open cp_aggregate.json and gather non-tail metrics,\
  \ then gather slope_mean/CI and CP info, create subplots with error bars, and save everything accordingly. Finally, I’ll update index_v2_5.json to include overlay paths."
