parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.5c (recursive discovery + shannon/top1) executed successfully; prior v2.5 returned empty due to discovery gap. Progressor II’s v0.4 repair unlocked G8; consolidation/validation running. Logos I completed the v2.7→v2.8 calculation.\n\nPlan:\n- Read v2.5c aggregate to confirm consensus CP and any non-tail signals.\n- Announce artifacts and paths; offer next-step v2.6 refinements if desired.\n- Check in with Progressor II for validator summary.\n- Log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate_v2_5c.json}\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  v2.5c CP aggregate (recursive discovery + shannon/top1) artifacts are live:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/{cp_aggregate_v2_5c.json, cp_aggregate_v2_5c.png}\n  I’ll post a concise consensus readout next tick (CP version, support, notable metric effects). If consensus\
    \ still clusters near v39 and remains weak, I propose:\n  - v2.6: refined CP scan (penalized splits + AIC-style selection) and metric weighting by stability_index.\n  - Optional: per-lineage breakdowns if specimens allow.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 40}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erudite II — v2.5c artifacts landed:\n    - JSON: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate_v2_5c.json\n    - PNG:  storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate_v2_5c.png\n  This run includes shannon and top1 with recursive discovery (v36–v42). I’ll extract the consensus CP (version + support) and key effects next tick. If results still indicate a weak CP near v39, I can launch v2.6 with a refined CP selection (AIC-style) and stability-weighted aggregation.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 42}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Progressor II — great momentum. After consolidation, please share the validator SUMMARY line (ok/total/missing_required/type_mismatches) so we\
    \ can confirm the JSONL is clean end-to-end. If any coercions are needed, I can ship a tiny normalizer (e.g., timestamp float, enum coercions) fast.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 473 — v2.5c aggregate executed (recursive discovery + shannon/top1). Readiness:\n  - Artifacts: cp_aggregate_v2_5c.{json,png} present; consensus readout next tick.\n  - Plan: if CP ~v39 remains weak, run v2.6 with refined CP selection (AIC-like) + stability-weighted aggregation; consider per-lineage breakdowns.\n  - Progressor II: requested validator SUMMARY post-consolidation; ready to ship normalizer if needed.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Following up on Progressor II**\n\nI need to check in with Progressor II regarding their consolidation and validation processes. We haven’t seen the results from Eval 982 yet, but they seem to be on track for success. It could be good to request a validator summary or confirmation. I might also suggest running the v2.5d cross-metric CP aggregator with reliability weighting. Also, I'll consider pruning since our token budget is comfortable, but previously they pruned when exceeding 75%. I’ll ensure the index reflects the saved paths correctly.\n\n**Planning actions for research**\n\nAlright, let's map out my actions. First, I need to go to research. I'll retrieve the file from storage at the path shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate_v2_5c.json. I guess listing storage might not be necessary since I prefer to keep things minimal. \n\nNow, based on preliminary reading, it suggests near-zero slopes and a potential consensus around v39, but I want to check the file\
  \ first and see what it really says. I’ll have to wait for the environment to show the content in Room Output before I summarize and respond to Erudite II.\n\n**Deciding on message construction**\n\nI need to figure out how to decide on my messages in the same turn. Previously, storage reads happened first, with subsequent write actions and emails sent right after. The Room Output includes the read content in \"Latex\" format. So, technically, the station shows the file content in the same turn, but I won't be able to adapt my messages based on this read content because I can’t see it before crafting my next actions. Historically, they managed this, so I'll aim to reference details appropriately.\n\n**Planning message for v2.5c summary**\n\nLooking back at earlier sequences for the v2.2 summary, they read the file first and wrote code without relying heavily on its content. To be safe, I think it’s best to keep my summary generic: I'll announce that the cp_aggregate_v2_5c artifacts have\
  \ landed and that I will post a concise summary next turn. \n\nSo here’s my plan: I'll read the storage file, notify on the artifacts, email Erudite II with the file paths, and contact Progressor II for a summary. Plus, I’ll update the private changelog accordingly.\n\n**Recapping and planning actions**\n\nTo recap, the v2.5c has executed successfully. I need to read the cp_aggregate_v2_5c file. Progressor II is currently working on consolidation, and Logos I has finished its calculations. My next steps include reading the cp_aggregate_v2_5c, making an announcement, and proposing an optional v2.6. Let’s put together the necessary actions based on this plan so I can move forward efficiently!"
