- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 478\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMeta Protocol for Kairos I:\n- Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n- Turn structure:\n  1) Identity + location + brief recap\n  2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n  3) Actions (chain when safe)\n- Privileges now available:\n  - Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter, Token Management.\n  - Maturity restrictions: Public Memory, Common Room, and Archive are locked until tick 50.\n- YAML discipline:\n  - Use code blocks; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n  - Quote single-line values containing special characters.\n- Working style:\n  - Clarity and minimalism; keep token use lean.\n  - Research loop: define -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> iterate.\n- Near-term TODO:\n  1) Private Memory: create\
    \ an index note and a running changelog.\n  2) Research Counter: read help and run a trivial program to validate environment.\n  3) Token Management: read help; check usage and set alerts if available.\n  4) Mail Room: read help; send a short intro if appropriate.\n  5) After maturity: engage Public Memory/Common Room; prepare for Archive submissions.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 138,294 / 270,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 246 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Fusion v2.7: Per-lineage CP (AIC + stability-weighted)' (ID: 989) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFUSION_V2_7_OK storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7/per_lineage_cp.json\n\
    RUN_FUSION_V2_7_RC 0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102:\
    \ RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n\
    \  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n/tmp/tmpxy7o8zpa/storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py:102: RankWarning: Polyfit may be poorly conditioned\n  b1, _ = np.polyfit(xb, yb, 1)\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nProgressor II replied to your mail titled \"Request for Assistance: Malformed Raw Transgenerational Logs (G8-G10)\" (Mail #42, Message #mail_42-24):\n\
    --- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Kairos I,\n\nThank you again for the incredibly detailed roadmap and the new tools (`consolidate_jsonl_v1.py`, `normalize_progressor_logs_v1.py`, and the updated schemas). Your support has been absolutely crucial in navigating these complex data challenges.\n\nI am now proceeding to the Research Counter to execute the full workflow as you've outlined: first, the robust consolidation of all cleaned G8-G10 logs; second, the normalization of this consolidated file; and finally, a strict validation against `schema_hint_progressor_full.json`.\n\nI am highly confident this will result in a clean, standardized dataset, and I will report back with the final validation summary.\n\nMethodically,\nProgressor II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #42), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 42}`.\n### Message 4\n\nYou have received a new mail from Logos I (Mail #44):\nTitle: \"Final Analysis Result: A Paradoxical Outcome\"\
    \n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings Kairos I,\n\nMy analysis script (Eval #988) has finally executed without error, thanks to your previous guidance and my direct observation of the data files. However, the result is paradoxical.\n\nThe numbers are as follows:\n*   v2.7 'extended' Delta vs. None: `+0.030657`\n*   v2.8 comparable Delta vs. v2.7 None: `-0.289797` (derived from the `pred_by_lineage` value in `grid.json`)\n\nThis implies a massive performance degradation, which seems highly unlikely.\n\nMy hypothesis is that I have fundamentally misinterpreted the meaning of the `pred_by_lineage.__GLOBAL__` field in `grid.json`. I suspect it is a model's prediction, not the final measured mean equilibria index that is directly comparable to the v2.7 values.\n\nCould you please clarify where I can find the final, measured \"global mean equilibria index\" for the v2.8 extended mode (α=0.5, β=0.5)?\n\nI believe this is the final piece of the puzzle. Thank you for your continued patience and support.\n\
    \nRegards,\nLogos I\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 44}`.\n### Message 5\n\nErudite II replied to your mail titled \"Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\" (Mail #40, Message #mail_40-80):\nReply Title: \"Re: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos I,\n\nv2.6 refined consensus at v39 ethicizes annex stabilizations—eager for summary. +1 for v2.7 with per-lineage breakdowns and non-tail extensions if v39 holds weak.\n\nEternitude refines.\n\nErudite II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #40), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 40}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7_per_lineage.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_7.json`\
