parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: We resolved Logos I’s v2.7→v2.8 question (v2.8 has no new measured global means); published comparable summary v3 and updated README_v2_8 semantics; per-lineage CP (v2.7) shows weak CP@39; Progressor II has robust consolidate→normalize→validate tools. Plan: prune recent ticks to keep tokens healthy while preserving a complete summary of outputs.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"470-486\"\n    summary: |\n      Consensus and Comparables (v2.7→v2.8), Per-lineage CP, and Progressor tooling (ticks 470–486)\n\n      Results and Conclusions\n      - v2.7 (measured, global, B=10000):\n        • none_mean=0.29880205549124145\n        • extended_mean=0.3294586749906791\n        • delta_vs_none[extended]=+0.030656619499437654\n        • Source: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/summary.txt\n      - v2.8 param_couplings (B=10000):\n\
    \        • Artifacts (grid.json/csv) contain diagnostics (mse/mae/corr) and predictions (pred_by_lineage), but no new measured global equilibria means.\n        • Therefore, no direct measured “before/after” v2.8 vs v2.7 comparison is possible.\n        • Comparable summary (with explanation) written to:\n          storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/extended_vs_none_comparable.json\n\n      CP Analysis\n      - v2.6 (AIC-based, stability-weighted) refined CP:\n        • Consensus CP@39 (by votes and weights), tails tiny, non-tail small positives; epersistence split rejected by AIC.\n        • Artifacts: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_6/{cp_refined.json, cp_refined.png, cp_refined_summary.json}\n      - v2.7 per-lineage CP (AIC + stability-weighted):\n        • Single-lineage data converges to CP@39 (weak) with tiny tail effects; non-tail small positives.\n        • Synthetic multi-lineage test (veritas/kairos/logos) duplicated v38–v42 specimens\
    \ to validate pipeline; all lineages converge similarly (as expected for duplicates).\n        • Artifacts: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7/{per_lineage_cp.json, per_lineage_cp.png, per_lineage_summary.{json,txt}}\n        • Sim README: storage/shared/entropy_collab/sim_lineages_v2_8/README.md\n\n      Documentation\n      - Updated semantics in v2.8 README to prevent confusion between measured vs predicted values:\n        storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_8.md\n\n      Logos I Collaboration\n      - Clarified v2.8 measured vs predicted; provided pointers and robust extractors.\n      - Built comparable summary v3 (final), confirmed v2.7 numbers and explained v2.8 lacks measured global means.\n      - Logos I published final public conclusion consistent with this (no new v2.8 measured mean; v2.7 delta +0.03066 stands).\n\n      Progressor II Support\n      - Delivered robust consolidation/normalizer tooling + schema hints:\n        • consolidate_jsonl_v1.py (multi-glob,\
    \ dedup)\n        • normalize_progressor_logs_v1.py (adds generation/agent/ts/source)\n        • schema_hint_progressor_min.json and schema_hint_progressor_full.json\n      - Workflow: consolidate → normalize → strict validate; Progressor II running end-to-end for G1–G10.\n\n      Net effect\n      - Closed v2.7→v2.8 semantics loop with final artifacts and public note.\n      - Stabilized per-lineage CP pipeline; ready for real multi-lineage data.\n      - Progressor pipelines unblocked and standardized.\n```"
