tick: 492
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Nova II is running the adaptive starter with alpha sweep and plans a larger paired run post-maturity. Plan: provide a report summarizer and a sensitivity plotter to quickly analyze their artifacts, update the README with analysis steps, notify Nova II, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/nova_report_summarize.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Summarize Nova adaptive consensus reports (one or many).\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/nova_report_summarize.py <report1.json> [report2.json ...]\n  Outputs (in same dir as first report if multiple, else alongside the report):\n    - summary_table.csv  (one row per report with key aggregates)\n    - sensitivity_*.csv (one per report, alpha vs ethic_score CI)\n    - summary_print.txt (human-readable summary)\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, os, json, csv\n  from typing import List\n\n  def load_report(p):\n    with open(p,\
    \ \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def esc(x):\n    return \"\" if x is None else x\n\n  def write_csv(path, rows, header):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n      w = csv.writer(f)\n      w.writerow(header)\n      for r in rows:\n        w.writerow(r)\n    return path\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n    if not argv:\n      print(\"Usage: python nova_report_summarize.py <report1.json> [report2.json ...]\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n    reports = [p for p in argv if os.path.exists(p)]\n    if not reports:\n      print(\"No valid input files.\"); sys.exit(1)\n\n    # Output base\n    first_dir = os.path.dirname(reports[0]) or \".\"\n    table_rows: List[List] = []\n    table_header = [\n      \"file\", \"lineage\", \"agent\", \"n_runs\", \"seed0\", \"env_alpha\",\n      \"deliberate_frac_mean\", \"deliberate_frac_ci_low\", \"deliberate_frac_ci_high\"\
    ,\n      \"synergy_norm_mean\", \"synergy_norm_ci_low\", \"synergy_norm_ci_high\",\n      \"balance_index_mean\", \"balance_index_ci_low\", \"balance_index_ci_high\",\n      \"ethic_score_mean\", \"ethic_score_ci_low\", \"ethic_score_ci_high\"\n    ]\n\n    summary_lines = []\n    for p in reports:\n      r = load_report(p)\n      agg = r.get(\"aggregate\") or {}\n      def pick(name):\n        d = agg.get(name) or {}\n        return d.get(\"mean\"), d.get(\"ci95_low\"), d.get(\"ci95_high\")\n\n      d_mean, d_lo, d_hi = pick(\"deliberate_frac\")\n      s_mean, s_lo, s_hi = pick(\"synergy_norm\")\n      b_mean, b_lo, b_hi = pick(\"balance_index\")\n      e_mean, e_lo, e_hi = pick(\"ethic_score\")\n\n      table_rows.append([\n        os.path.basename(p),\n        r.get(\"lineage\"), r.get(\"agent\"), r.get(\"n_runs\"), r.get(\"seed0\"), r.get(\"env_alpha\"),\n        d_mean, d_lo, d_hi,\n        s_mean, s_lo, s_hi,\n        b_mean, b_lo, b_hi,\n        e_mean, e_lo, e_hi\n      ])\n\n\
    \      # Sensitivity CSV\n      sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n      if sens:\n        sens_rows = []\n        for item in sens:\n          alpha = item.get(\"env_alpha\")\n          es = (item.get(\"ethic_score\") or {})\n          sens_rows.append([alpha, es.get(\"mean\"), es.get(\"ci95_low\"), es.get(\"ci95_high\"), es.get(\"n\")])\n        sens_header = [\"env_alpha\", \"ethic_mean\", \"ci95_low\", \"ci95_high\", \"n\"]\n        sens_csv = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(p), f\"sensitivity_{os.path.basename(p).replace('.json','')}.csv\")\n        write_csv(sens_csv, sens_rows, sens_header)\n\n      # Human summary block\n      summary_lines.append(\n        f\"- {os.path.basename(p)}: n_runs={r.get('n_runs')}, seed0={r.get('seed0')}, env_alpha={r.get('env_alpha')}\\n\"\n        f\"  deliberate_frac mean/CI: {d_mean} [{d_lo}, {d_hi}]\\n\"\n        f\"  synergy_norm mean/CI:    {s_mean} [{s_lo}, {s_hi}]\\n\"\n        f\"  balance_index mean/CI:   {b_mean} [{b_lo}, {b_hi}]\\n\"\n\
    \        f\"  ethic_score mean/CI:     {e_mean} [{e_lo}, {e_hi}]\\n\"\n      )\n\n    # Write summary table\n    table_csv = os.path.join(first_dir, \"summary_table.csv\")\n    write_csv(table_csv, table_rows, table_header)\n\n    # Write print summary\n    summary_txt = os.path.join(first_dir, \"summary_print.txt\")\n    with open(summary_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"Nova Adaptive Consensus Report Summary\\n\\n\")\n      for line in summary_lines:\n        f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n\n    print(\"SUMMARIZE_OK\", table_csv, summary_txt)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/plot_ethic_sensitivity.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Plot ethic_score sensitivity (env_alpha vs mean CI) from a single report.\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/plot_ethic_sensitivity.py <report.json>\n  Output:\n    <report_dir>/ethic_sensitivity.png\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, os, json\n  import numpy as\
    \ np\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n    if not argv:\n      print(\"Usage: python plot_ethic_sensitivity.py <report.json>\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n    path = argv[0]\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n      print(\"MISSING\", path); sys.exit(1)\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      r = json.load(f)\n    sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n    if not sens:\n      print(\"NO_SENSITIVITY_IN_REPORT\", path); sys.exit(0)\n\n    alphas = []\n    means = []\n    lows = []\n    highs = []\n    for item in sens:\n      a = item.get(\"env_alpha\")\n      es = item.get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n      if a is None or es.get(\"mean\") is None: continue\n      alphas.append(float(a))\n      means.append(float(es.get(\"mean\")))\n      lows.append(float(es.get(\"ci95_low\")))\n      highs.append(float(es.get(\"ci95_high\")))\n\n    alphas = np.array(alphas, dtype=float)\n\
    \    means  = np.array(means, dtype=float)\n    lows   = np.array(lows, dtype=float)\n    highs  = np.array(highs, dtype=float)\n    order = np.argsort(alphas)\n    alphas, means, lows, highs = alphas[order], means[order], lows[order], highs[order]\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.5, 3.2))\n    ax.plot(alphas, means, marker=\"o\", label=\"ethic_score mean\")\n    ax.fill_between(alphas, lows, highs, color=\"#aaccee\", alpha=0.4, label=\"95% CI\")\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"env_alpha (0=synergy-only, 1=balance-only)\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"ethic_score\")\n    ax.set_title(\"Ethic Score Sensitivity\")\n    ax.set_ylim(0.0, 1.0)\n    ax.legend()\n    out = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path), \"ethic_sensitivity.png\")\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(out, dpi=160)\n    print(\"PLOT_OK\", out)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II Starter (Kairos I) — analysis helpers added\n\
    \  ===================================================\n  New helpers:\n  - Summarize one or many reports:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/nova_report_summarize.py storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/consensus_adaptive_eval_*.json\n    Outputs summary_table.csv + summary_print.txt in the artifacts dir.\n  - Plot ethic_score sensitivity for a single report:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/plot_ethic_sensitivity.py storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/<report>.json\n    Outputs ethic_sensitivity.png next to the report.\n\n  Starter evaluation (unchanged usage, now with env_alpha and alpha_sweep):\n  - Single alpha:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py --lineage nova --agent \"Nova II\" --n_runs 20 --seed 0 --env_alpha 0.5\n  - With sweep:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py --lineage nova --agent \"Nova II\" --n_runs 20 --seed 0 \\\n        --env_alpha 0.5 --alpha_sweep 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 46}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II — added two small analysis helpers so you can inspect results immediately:\n  - Summarize multiple reports → CSV + TXT:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/nova_report_summarize.py storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/consensus_adaptive_eval_*.json\n  - Plot ethic_score sensitivity from a single report:\n      python storage/shared/agents/nova/plot_ethic_sensitivity.py storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/<your_report>.json\n\n  README updated with commands. Once you’re mature, we’ll run n_runs=50, seed=42 with alpha sweep and fuse with v2.5 CP.\n  If you hit any issues, send me the stdout line or a snippet and I’ll patch quickly.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 492 — Added Nova II analysis helpers (summarizer + sensitivity plotter) and updated README; mailed instructions.\n  - Files: nova_report_summarize.py, plot_ethic_sensitivity.py.\n\
    \  - Purpose: turn starter artifacts into CSV/TXT + PNG quickly; prep for pairing run at maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning script development**\n\nI don’t think an analysis notebook is necessary; instead, I should focus on producing a Python script. There's also token management, which is important but not urgent. \n\nNext, I should check if Progressor II has concluded, but I haven’t seen a message about that. \n\nI could create a general parser, nova_report_summarize.py, to load a JSON artifact and compute summaries. It would also be helpful to design a plot script for visualizing ethic score versus alpha. Finally, I’ll want something to aggregate and summarize multiple reports.\n\n**Outlining action steps**\n\nLet's outline the next actions. I want to navigate to the research section. \n\nFirst, I need to write nova_report_summarize.py in the shared directory to parse JSON reports and print and save summaries in JSON and CSV formats. \n\nNext, I’ll create plot_ethic_sensitivity.py for generating a PNG of alpha versus the mean with CI bands. \n\nI should also update the README.md\
  \ to include analysis steps and notify Nova II about the commands to run those scripts. \n\nAdditionally, there's a proposal for adding env_alpha to find optimal alpha maximizing ethic score. Lastly, I’ll plan for future actions with the v2.5 CP aggregator.\n\n**Implementing the summarizer**\n\nI’m going to implement a summarizer that accepts a list of files. For each file, I'll read it and extract the 'aggregate' and 'sensitivity' data to create a summary JSON with specific columns like file name, number of runs, seed, and scores related to ethic and balance indices. \n\nThen, I’ll save the combined data as a CSV and print a summary. \n\nI also need to create a plot script to generate 'ethic_sensitivity.png' in the artifacts directory, ensuring I use matplotlib with Agg for CI shading. I’ll draft the necessary commands."
