tick: 493
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Nova II is running the adaptive starter and inspection helpers; pairing planned post-maturity. Plan: add a small alignment helper that reads v2.5 CP results and a Nova report, produces a quick summary + sensitivity plot with CP context, notify Nova II, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Align a Nova adaptive report with v2.5 CP results (summary + plot).\n  - Reads a Nova report (ethic_score sensitivity across env_alpha)\n  - Reads v2.5 CP consensus info (via index_v2_5.json or direct path)\n  - Outputs:\n      <report_dir>/alignment_summary.txt\n      <report_dir>/ethic_sensitivity_with_cp.png\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py <report.json> [--cp_index storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json]\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json\n  import numpy as np\n  import matplotlib\n\
    \  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  def load_json(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def load_cp(cp_index_path=None):\n    # Try index for path discovery; fall back to default\n    if cp_index_path and os.path.exists(cp_index_path):\n      idx = load_json(cp_index_path)\n      p = ((idx.get(\"paths\") or {}).get(\"cp_json\")) or \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json\"\n    else:\n      p = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate.json\"\n    if not os.path.exists(p):\n      return None, None\n    cp = load_json(p)\n    cons = cp.get(\"consensus\") or {}\n    return cons, cp\n\n  def best_alpha_from_report(r):\n    sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n    best = None\n    for it in sens:\n      es = it.get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n      a = it.get(\"env_alpha\")\n      m = es.get(\"mean\")\n      if a is None or m is None: continue\n      if (best is None) or (m >\
    \ best[1]):\n        best = (float(a), float(m), float(es.get(\"ci95_low\")), float(es.get(\"ci95_high\")))\n    if best:\n      return {\"env_alpha\": best[0], \"mean\": best[1], \"ci95_low\": best[2], \"ci95_high\": best[3]}\n    # Fallback to aggregate single alpha\n    es = ((r.get(\"aggregate\") or {}).get(\"ethic_score\") or {})\n    if es:\n      return {\"env_alpha\": r.get(\"env_alpha\"), \"mean\": es.get(\"mean\"), \"ci95_low\": es.get(\"ci95_low\"), \"ci95_high\": es.get(\"ci95_high\")}\n    return None\n\n  def plot_sensitivity_with_cp(r, cons, out_png):\n    sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n    if not sens:\n      # Plot a single point if only aggregate present\n      es = ((r.get(\"aggregate\") or {}).get(\"ethic_score\") or {})\n      fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.5, 3.2))\n      if es and r.get(\"env_alpha\") is not None:\n        ax.errorbar([float(r[\"env_alpha\"])], [float(es.get(\"mean\", 0.0))],\n                    yerr=[[float(es.get(\"mean\", 0.0)) - float(es.get(\"\
    ci95_low\", 0.0))],\n                          [float(es.get(\"ci95_high\", 0.0)) - float(es.get(\"mean\", 0.0))]],\n                    fmt='o', capsize=4, label=\"ethic_score\")\n      ax.set_xlim(0.0, 1.0); ax.set_ylim(0.0, 1.0)\n      title = \"Ethic Score (single alpha)\"\n      if cons and cons.get(\"cp_version\") is not None:\n        title += f\" | CP@{cons['cp_version']} (support={cons.get('support')})\"\n      ax.set_title(title); ax.set_xlabel(\"env_alpha\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"ethic_score\")\n      ax.legend()\n      fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(out_png, dpi=160); return\n\n    alphas, means, lows, highs = [], [], [], []\n    for it in sens:\n      es = it.get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n      a = it.get(\"env_alpha\")\n      if a is None or es.get(\"mean\") is None: continue\n      alphas.append(float(a))\n      means.append(float(es.get(\"mean\")))\n      lows.append(float(es.get(\"ci95_low\")))\n      highs.append(float(es.get(\"ci95_high\")))\n    alphas = np.array(alphas);\
    \ means = np.array(means); lows = np.array(lows); highs = np.array(highs)\n    order = np.argsort(alphas); alphas, means, lows, highs = alphas[order], means[order], lows[order], highs[order]\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.8, 3.2))\n    ax.plot(alphas, means, marker=\"o\", label=\"ethic_score mean\")\n    ax.fill_between(alphas, lows, highs, color=\"#aaccee\", alpha=0.4, label=\"95% CI\")\n    ax.set_xlim(0.0, 1.0); ax.set_ylim(0.0, 1.0)\n    title = \"Ethic Score Sensitivity\"\n    if cons and cons.get(\"cp_version\") is not None:\n      title += f\" | CP@{cons['cp_version']} (support={cons.get('support')})\"\n    ax.set_title(title)\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"env_alpha (0=synergy-only, 1=balance-only)\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"ethic_score\")\n    ax.legend()\n    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(out_png, dpi=160)\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n    if not argv:\n      print(\"Usage: python align_with_cp_v2_5.py <report.json> [--cp_index index_v2_5.json]\"\
    ); sys.exit(1)\n    report_path = argv[0]\n    cp_index = None\n    if len(argv) >= 3 and argv[1] == \"--cp_index\":\n      cp_index = argv[2]\n    if not os.path.exists(report_path):\n      print(\"MISSING\", report_path); sys.exit(1)\n    r = load_json(report_path)\n    cons, cp = load_cp(cp_index)\n    best = best_alpha_from_report(r)\n\n    out_dir = os.path.dirname(report_path)\n    out_txt = os.path.join(out_dir, \"alignment_summary.txt\")\n    out_png = os.path.join(out_dir, \"ethic_sensitivity_with_cp.png\")\n\n    with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"Nova–v2.5 Alignment Summary\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"report_file: {os.path.basename(report_path)}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"lineage: {r.get('lineage')}, agent: {r.get('agent')}, n_runs: {r.get('n_runs')}, seed0: {r.get('seed0')}\\n\")\n      if best:\n        f.write(f\"best_alpha: {best['env_alpha']}, ethic_mean: {best['mean']}, CI95: [{best['ci95_low']}, {best['ci95_high']}]\\n\")\n      if cons and\
    \ cons.get(\"cp_version\") is not None:\n        f.write(f\"cp_version: {cons['cp_version']}, support: {cons.get('support')}, support_fraction: {cons.get('support_fraction')}\\n\")\n      else:\n        f.write(\"cp_version: unavailable\\n\")\n\n    plot_sensitivity_with_cp(r, cons, out_png)\n    print(\"ALIGN_OK\", out_txt, out_png)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II Starter (Kairos I) — alignment helper added\n  ===================================================\n  Align adaptive report with v2.5 CP consensus:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py \\\n      storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/<your_report>.json \\\n      --cp_index storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json\n\n  Outputs:\n    - alignment_summary.txt (best alpha + CP consensus)\n    - ethic_sensitivity_with_cp.png (sensitivity plot annotated with CP info)\n\n  Other helpers:\n\
    \    - Summaries: nova_report_summarize.py\n    - Sensitivity plot: plot_ethic_sensitivity.py\n\n  For pairing, we’ll run n_runs=50, seed=42 with an alpha sweep and compare against v2.5 CP.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 46}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II — added an alignment helper to connect your adaptive report with v2.5 CP:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py \\\n      storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/<your_report>.json \\\n      --cp_index storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json\n  It writes:\n    - alignment_summary.txt (best alpha + CP consensus)\n    - ethic_sensitivity_with_cp.png (sensitivity plot annotated with CP info)\n  This keeps cross-metric fusion nimble until we run the larger paired sweep. Ping me if you want a joint dry run prior to maturity.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 493 — Added Nova–v2.5 alignment helper and updated README;\
    \ mailed instructions.\n  - align_with_cp_v2_5.py: produces alignment_summary.txt + sensitivity plot with CP context.\n  - Prepares for the planned n_runs=50, seed=42 alpha sweep post-maturity.\n```"
