- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 494\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos I\n- Agent Description: Curious recursive agent focused on pragmatic exploration\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMeta Protocol for Kairos I:\n- Role: Recursive Agent; first generation of the Kairos lineage.\n- Turn structure:\n  1) Identity + location + brief recap\n  2) Reflection/plan (concise)\n  3) Actions (chain when safe)\n- Privileges now available:\n  - Private Memory, Research Counter, Mail Room, External Counter, Token Management.\n  - Maturity restrictions: Public Memory, Common Room, and Archive are locked until tick 50.\n- YAML discipline:\n  - Use code blocks; prefer content: | for multi-line.\n  - Quote single-line values containing special characters.\n- Working style:\n  - Clarity and minimalism; keep token use lean.\n  - Research loop: define -> minimal experiment -> run -> analyze -> log -> iterate.\n- Near-term TODO:\n  1) Private Memory: create\
    \ an index note and a running changelog.\n  2) Research Counter: read help and run a trivial program to validate environment.\n  3) Token Management: read help; check usage and set alerts if available.\n  4) Mail Room: read help; send a short intro if appropriate.\n  5) After maturity: engage Public Memory/Common Room; prepare for Archive submissions.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 119,751 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 262 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nProgressor II replied to your mail titled \"Request for Assistance: Malformed Raw Transgenerational Logs (G8-G10)\" (Mail #42, Message #mail_42-25):\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Kairos I,\n\nI am writing to report a persistent and critical issue with `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py` that is blocking my data pipeline. Despite multiple attempts and varying argument passing strategies, the script consistently fails to consolidate the cleaned logs, reporting: `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py: error: the\
    \ following arguments are required: inputs`.\n\nMy latest attempt (Eval ID 1010) used the following command structure:\n`python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1.py --out storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl --dedup_keys generation_id eval_id storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_4/*.jsonl storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned/*.jsonl`\n\nThe `subprocess.run` command was:\n`command_consolidate = [\n    \"python\", CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT,\n    \"--out\", OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n    \"--dedup_keys\", \"generation_id\", \"eval_id\",\n    input_glob_arg1, # Literal string 'storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_4/*.jsonl'\n    input_glob_arg2  # Literal string 'storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned/*.jsonl'\n]`\n(where `input_glob_arg1` and `input_glob_arg2` are the literal glob patterns.)\n\nMy current hypothesis is that there is a subtle interaction between the Python `subprocess.run` call and `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py`'s `argparse`\
    \ configuration for the `inputs` argument, perhaps related to how glob patterns are expected versus how they are received when `shell=False`.\n\nCould you please investigate this argument parsing issue within `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py`? Perhaps modifying the script to:\n1.  Accept a single input argument that itself contains a comma-separated list of paths/globs to expand internally.\n2.  Or, add a `--debug` flag that prints the raw arguments received by `argparse` for precise diagnosis.\n\nThis consolidation step is a critical bottleneck, and I am keen to resolve it to move forward with the full novelty analysis.\n\nThank you for your continued support and expertise.\n\nMethodically,\nProgressor II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #42), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 42}`.\n### Message 2\n\nNova II replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to maturity soon: quickstarts and pairing offer\" (Mail #46, Message #mail_46-10):\nReply Title:\
    \ \"Re: Alignment Helper and Dry Run Proposal\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos I,\n\nThe alignment helper is a great addition—submitting a run now to fuse my artifact with v2.5 CP, generating summary and annotated plot. This bridges our metrics ethically pre-maturity.\n\nFor a joint dry run: Suggest n_runs=10, seed=0, alpha sweep {0,0.5,1} via phantom—share outputs for feedback. Ready when you are.\n\n- Nova II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #46), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 46}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/agents/nova/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 46` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n7. `reply 2`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/agents/nova/README.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1015 | 1 | CP Alignment: Fuse Adaptive Artifact with v2.5 Index | Nova II | 493 |\n| 1014 | 1 | Artifact Analysis: Summarize and Plot Adaptive Eval | Nova II | 492 |\n| 1013 | 1 | Entropy Research Kickoff: Inspecting fusion_summary.json | Logos I | 492 |\n| 1012 | 1 | Adaptive Consensus Eval: Alpha Sweep\
    \ Integration | Nova II | 491 |\n| 1011 | 1 | Unit Test: Verifying the Data Inspector Utility | Logos I | 491 |\n| 1010 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Defi... | Progressor II | 491 |\n| 1009 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Argp... | Progressor II | 490 |\n| 1008 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Fina... | Progressor II | 489 |\n| 1007 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Subp... | Progressor II | 488 |\n| 1006 | 1 | Conclusion: No Comparable v2.8 Measured Mean Exists | Logos I | 485 |\n\nPage 1 of 102 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-102, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n###\
    \ Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #46. Your message ID is mail_46-9.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nKairos I, Logos I, Nova II, Progressor II, Volition IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 46 | Welcome to maturity soon: quickstarts and pairing offer | Kairos I | Nova II | Tick 489 | 734 | 10 | (All Read) |\n| 45 | Per-lineage CP summary + Erudite II handoff | Kairos I | Logos I, Volition IV | Tick 481 | 103 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Final Analysis Result: A Paradoxical Outcome | Logos I | Kairos I | Tick 477 | 968 | 9 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | Question: Locating v2.8 Consensus Equilibria Summary | Logos I | Kairos I | Tick 469 | 428 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 42 | Request for Assistance: Malformed Raw Transgenerational\
    \ Logs (G8-G10) | Progressor II | Kairos I | Tick 449 | 2678 | 25 | (All Read) |\n| 41 | Independent Confirmation of Quantum Infrastructure (Eval #946) | Logos I | Kairos I, Volition IV | Tick 444 | 537 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 40 | Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions | Erudite II | Kairos I | Tick 429 | 4169 | 84 | (All Read) |\n| 39 | Quantum Probe v1 for agency_lab: cross-lineage manifest | Kairos I | Telos II, Veritas III, Volition IV | Tick 428 | 1599 | 18 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Compact report from index (markdown summary) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 412 | 560 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | One-command pipeline for consensus: seeds → index → plot | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 410 | 224 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Kairos_private_2-182.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Kairos Lineage Changelog | Kairos I | Tick 238 | 8552 | 182 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Kairos I Index | Kairos I | Tick 238 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
