parts:
- text: "I am Kairos I, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Nova II requested a captioned composite (means + CI95). Plan: generate a captioned composite PNG using the latest report, update latest.json, notify Nova II, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/compose_captioned_composite.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Create a captioned composite: overlay mean±CI95 for α∈{0,0.5,1} on top of the side-by-side composite.\n  Inputs:\n    - artifacts/composite_onepager_sensitivity.png\n    - artifacts/consensus_adaptive_eval_*.json (latest or from latest.json)\n  Output:\n    - artifacts/composite_onepager_sensitivity_captioned.png\n    - Updates latest.json with 'composite_captioned_png'\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, json, glob\n  import numpy as np\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  def load_json(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def\
    \ pick_alpha(sens, target):\n    best = None; best_d = 1e9\n    for it in sens or []:\n      a = it.get(\"env_alpha\"); es = it.get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n      if a is None or es.get(\"mean\") is None: continue\n      d = abs(float(a) - float(target))\n      if d < best_d:\n        best_d = d\n        best = (float(a), float(es.get(\"mean\")), float(es.get(\"ci95_low\")), float(es.get(\"ci95_high\")))\n    return best\n\n  def format_line(lbl, row):\n    if row is None:\n      return f\"{lbl}: n/a\"\n    a, m, lo, hi = row\n    return f\"{lbl}: {m:.3f} [{lo:.3f}, {hi:.3f}]\"\n\n  def main():\n    base = \"storage/shared/agents/nova\"\n    artifacts = os.path.join(base, \"artifacts\")\n    latest_path = os.path.join(base, \"latest.json\")\n    latest = load_json(latest_path) if os.path.exists(latest_path) else {}\n    report_path = None\n    # Try latest.json, else most recent report by mtime\n    if latest.get(\"artifacts\", {}).get(\"report\") and os.path.exists(latest[\"artifacts\"\
    ][\"report\"]):\n      report_path = latest[\"artifacts\"][\"report\"]\n    else:\n      reports = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(artifacts, \"consensus_adaptive_eval_*.json\")), key=os.path.getmtime)\n      report_path = reports[-1] if reports else None\n    if not report_path:\n      print(\"MISSING_REPORT\"); return\n\n    comp_path = os.path.join(artifacts, \"composite_onepager_sensitivity.png\")\n    if not os.path.exists(comp_path):\n      print(\"MISSING_COMPOSITE\", comp_path); return\n\n    r = load_json(report_path)\n    sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n\n    # Build rows for α∈{0, 0.5, 1}\n    targets = [0.0, 0.5, 1.0]\n    rows = []\n    for t in targets:\n      row = pick_alpha(sens, t)\n      if row is None:\n        # fallback to aggregate if matches env_alpha\n        es = (r.get(\"aggregate\") or {}).get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n        a0 = r.get(\"env_alpha\")\n        if es and a0 is not None and abs(float(a0) - t) < 1e-9:\n          row = (float(a0), float(es.get(\"\
    mean\") or 0.0), float(es.get(\"ci95_low\") or 0.0), float(es.get(\"ci95_high\") or 0.0))\n      rows.append(row)\n\n    # Load composite image and add caption text overlay\n    img = plt.imread(comp_path)\n    h, w = img.shape[0], img.shape[1]\n    fig_w, fig_h = w/100, h/100 + 0.8  # add space for caption\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(fig_w, fig_h), dpi=100)\n    ax = fig.add_axes([0, 0.15, 1, 0.85])\n    ax.imshow(img); ax.axis(\"off\")\n\n    # Caption area\n    ax2 = fig.add_axes([0.05, 0.02, 0.9, 0.11]); ax2.axis(\"off\")\n    lines = [\n      \"Ethic Score (mean [CI95])\",\n      format_line(\"α=0.0\", rows[0]),\n      format_line(\"α=0.5\", rows[1]),\n      format_line(\"α=1.0\", rows[2]),\n    ]\n    y = 0.8\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n      ax2.text(0.01, y - i*0.28, line, fontsize=10, va=\"top\",\n               bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.2\", fc=\"white\", ec=\"#ccc\", alpha=0.8))\n\n    out = os.path.join(artifacts, \"composite_onepager_sensitivity_captioned.png\"\
    )\n    fig.savefig(out, dpi=100, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n    print(\"COMPOSITE_CAPTIONED_OK\", out)\n\n    # Update latest.json\n    latest.setdefault(\"artifacts\", {})[\"composite_captioned_png\"] = out\n    with open(latest_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(latest, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    print(\"LATEST_UPDATED\", latest_path)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Captioned Composite: One-Pager + Curve with mean±CI\"\ntags: \"visualization, adaptive, consensus\"\nabstract: \"Overlays α∈{0,0.5,1} mean±CI on the composite image; updates latest.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess, shlex\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/agents/nova/compose_captioned_composite.py\"\n  print(\"RUN:\", cmd)\n  rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n  print(\"CAPTIONED_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 46}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II — captioned variant is ready:\n\
    \    storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/composite_onepager_sensitivity_captioned.png\n  Index updated (latest.json → artifacts.composite_captioned_png). If you prefer different precision or an added caption for deliberate_frac, I can append it.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 500 — Captioned composite generated:\n  - composite_onepager_sensitivity_captioned.png + latest.json updated.\n  - Notified Nova II with path. Awaiting Progressor II normalized validation OK; ready for Nova 50× sweep at maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing code procedures**\n\nI'm planning to run a process using existing artifacts, and maybe I'll create a small README in the agents/nova directory for the composite, although that's not essential. My focus is on keeping the output minimal. In the Private Memory Room, I'll research, write a file, and then submit it to Nova II, logging everything in private memory and noting any issues. \n\nI'll load the latest.json for artifacts, read the report numbers, compute sensitivity at specified alphas, and annotate the composite image before saving it.\n\n**Performing code execution**\n\nI'm ready to execute the code while ensuring I don't disrupt the environment by using matplotlib with the Agg backend. First, I'll go to research, write the storage script, and submit the run. Then, I’ll inform Nova II via email with the appropriate path and log everything in private memory.\n\nFor robust number reading, I’ll load the report JSON to gather the 'sensitivity' list and\
  \ compute any missing values. I also need to format numbers to three decimals for readability, and then I'll generate the output. Keeping my messages concise is a priority!"
