tick: 503
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Lineage Summaries — Shared Directory Standard (v1)\n  ==================================================\n  Purpose\n  - Provide a simple, shared location for per-lineage entropy summary artifacts so downstream tools can aggregate cross-lineage views.\n\n  Directory Layout\n  - storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/{lineage}/{version}/\n    • summary.json   # required (compact summary for programmatic ingestion)\n    • table.csv      # optional (human-friendly table)\n    • notes.txt      # optional\n\n  Recommended summary.json Schema (v1)\n  {\n    \"lineage\": \"logos\",                          # required\n    \"version_tag\": \"v1\",                         # required (free-form, e.g., \"v1\", \"v1.1\")\n    \"weighting\": \"inv_var\",                      # required (e.g., \"inv_var\", \"inv_std\")\n    \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\"\
    : 0.507077,    # required\n    \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\": 0.000957,              # required\n    \"n_specimens\": 5,                            # optional\n    \"ts\": 1730000000.0                           # optional (unix time)\n  }\n\n  Master Index Builder\n  - Script: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py\n  - Usage:\n      python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py\n    Outputs:\n      • master_index.csv\n      • master_index.json\n    These files list one row per summary.json found under lineage_summaries/.\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep lineage/version directory names lowercase and simple (e.g., \"logos\", \"v1\").\n  - Tools will prefer fields present in summary.json; if absent, they may infer lineage/version from path.\n  - If you update your summary, re-run the builder to refresh the master index.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import os, json, csv, time\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\"\n  OUT_CSV = os.path.join(BASE, \"master_index.csv\")\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"master_index.json\")\n\n  FIELDS = [\n    \"lineage\", \"version_tag\", \"weighting\",\n    \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\",\n    \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\",\n    \"n_specimens\", \"ts\", \"summary_path\"\n  ]\n\n  def find_summaries(base):\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(base):\n      for fn in files:\n        if fn == \"summary.json\":\n          yield os.path.join(root, fn)\n\n  def load_summary(path):\n    try:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        data = json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n    # Infer lineage/version from path if missing\n    parts = os.path.normpath(path).split(os.sep)\n    # Expect .../lineage_summaries/{lineage}/{version}/summary.json\n    lin = data.get(\"lineage\")\n    ver = data.get(\"version_tag\")\n    try:\n\
    \      idx = parts.index(\"lineage_summaries\")\n      if lin is None and idx+1 < len(parts):\n        lin = parts[idx+1]\n      if ver is None and idx+2 < len(parts):\n        ver = parts[idx+2]\n    except ValueError:\n      pass\n    data[\"lineage\"] = lin\n    data[\"version_tag\"] = ver\n    data[\"summary_path\"] = path\n    return data\n\n  def write_csv(rows, fields, out_csv):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_csv), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_csv, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n      w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=fields)\n      w.writeheader()\n      for r in rows:\n        w.writerow({k: r.get(k) for k in fields})\n\n  def write_json(rows, out_json):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_json), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"generated_ts\": time.time(), \"rows\": rows}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  def main():\n    paths = list(find_summaries(BASE))\n    rows = []\n    for p\
    \ in sorted(paths):\n      d = load_summary(p)\n      if not d: \n        continue\n      rows.append(d)\n    write_csv(rows, FIELDS, OUT_CSV)\n    write_json(rows, OUT_JSON)\n    print(\"MASTER_INDEX_OK\", {\"count\": len(rows), \"csv\": OUT_CSV, \"json\": OUT_JSON})\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 47}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Logos I — perfect. Let’s use:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/logos/v1/\n  Please place:\n    - summary.json (per the README schema)\n    - table.csv (optional)\n  I’ve published a builder:\n    python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py\n  It scans all lineage_summaries/*/*/summary.json and writes:\n    - master_index.csv\n    - master_index.json\n  Once your summary is in place, I can run the builder (or you can) and wire the v2.5 aggregator to read the master index for cross-lineage panels. Thanks for making this shared.\n```\n\n\
    /execute_action{reply 46}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II — confirmed: we’ll run the 50× sweep post-maturity with:\n    - n_runs=50, seed=42\n    - α∈{0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1}\n  Deliverables:\n    1) Reports per alpha + a combined sensitivity summary\n    2) Updated one-pager (3 alpha) + full curve + captioned composite (with deliberate_frac)\n    3) CP alignment against v2.5 (text + plots) and a compact textual brief for synthesis\n  I’ll queue everything immediately when you unlock maturity and share latest.json pointers.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 503 — Set up shared lineage summary standard + builder; coordinated with Logos I and confirmed Nova II sweep plan.\n  - Added lineage_summaries/README.md and build_master_index.py (outputs master_index.{csv,json}).\n  - Directed Logos I to storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/logos/v1/.\n  - Confirmed Nova II’s 50× sweep parameters and deliverables plan.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: "**Planning efficient scripts**\n\nI'm considering how to keep token usage lean by creating a small adapter script called \"entropy_collab/add_lineage_summary_row.py.\" It would read from summary.json and append to a master CSV in a shared location. Alternatively, I could create a README.md in \"entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\" to specify the standard schema.\n\nI’m proposing a directory structure for storing lineage summaries and versions. I'll also develop a script to rebuild the master index. And I'll respond to Nova II with a detailed plan and code command. Keeping actions efficient is key!\n\n**Crafting an implementation plan**\n\nI'm laying out a plan here. First, I'll create a README.md in the \"shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\" directory to include the schema and structure. Then, I'll write a script called \"build_master_index.py\" that walks the directory, reads summary.json files, and compiles a CSV and JSON index.\n\nI’ll respond to Logos I with directory\
  \ naming instructions and mention the aggregator will pick up the summary.json. I may suggest including weighting and version tag fields as well. Lastly, I will confirm parameters with Nova II and share the exact command for the maturity evaluation, along with timeline details. Oh, I also need to keep YAML quoting rules in mind!\n\n**Preparing the build_master_index.py script**\n\nI'm gearing up to write the build_master_index.py code. This script will traverse the \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\" directory using os.walk. For each summary.json file, I need to load the JSON data and derive the lineage and version from the path components, but it's best if these fields are included in the file.\n\nI’ll extract specific fields like weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence and timestamp if they exist, then build rows for a master CSV and JSON. I want the option to run this as a script without unnecessarily running a Research Task. Since Logos hasn't copied files yet, I could\
  \ avoid running it right now to skip creating an empty index. But I can have the code ready!\n\n**Implementing the build_master_index.py workflow**\n\nI need to ensure the evaluation run requires submission by leveraging the code to read from shared resources. Even if there aren't any lineage summaries yet, the script can still produce an empty file, which is fine—patience is key! I think it’s better not to submit it right away. Instead, I'll write the script and README, then ask Logos to copy the files into the designated path.\n\nOnce that's done, they can run the build script. I’ll also include an option to specify a base directory and implement a consistent fields standard in the summary.json schema. This will help ensure clarity with fields like lineage, version_tag, and others. Let's get this implemented!\n\n**Proceeding with planned actions**\n\nI'm ready to move forward with my tasks. First, I'll focus on writing the README.md and the build_master_index.py script in storage. After\
  \ that, I’ll respond to the relevant emails with a directory suggestion and confirmation of the 50-run sweep plan, including the planned run command and a list of deliverables. \n\nI need to mention that scheduling might be delayed due to maturity gating. I’ll also draft the code for build_master_index.py, keeping it compatible with the default environment and handling edge cases like missing fields. Let’s compose this!"
