parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  One-command sweep (post-maturity):\n    - Runs adaptive eval with n_runs=50, seed=42, alpha_sweep {0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1}\n    - Generates summaries, sensitivity plot, one-pager (3 alpha), side-by-side composite, captioned composite\n    - Aligns with v2.5 CP and writes a textual brief\n    - Updates latest.json pointers\n\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, glob, subprocess, shlex, json\n\n  ART = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts\"\n  LATEST = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/latest.json\"\n\n  def run(cmd):\n    print(\"RUN:\", cmd)\n    rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n    print(\"RC:\", rc)\n    return rc\n\n  def newest_report():\n    reports = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(ART, \"consensus_adaptive_eval_*.json\")), key=os.path.getmtime)\n    return reports[-1] if reports else None\n\
    \n  def write_latest(extra=None, report=None):\n    data = {}\n    if os.path.exists(LATEST):\n      try:\n        with open(LATEST, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          data = json.load(f) or {}\n      except Exception:\n        data = {}\n    data.setdefault(\"artifacts\", {})\n    if report:\n      data[\"artifacts\"][\"sweep_report\"] = report\n    if extra:\n      data[\"artifacts\"].update(extra)\n    with open(LATEST, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(data, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    print(\"LATEST_UPDATED\", LATEST)\n\n  def main():\n    os.makedirs(ART, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # 1) Run 50× adaptive eval with full alpha sweep (env_alpha=0.5 placeholder)\n    cmd_eval = (\n      \"python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py \"\n      \"--lineage nova --agent 'Nova II' \"\n      \"--n_runs 50 --seed 42 --env_alpha 0.5 \"\n      \"--alpha_sweep 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1\"\n    )\n    run(cmd_eval)\n\n    report = newest_report()\n    print(\"\
    LATEST_REPORT:\", report)\n    if not report:\n      return\n\n    # 2) Summarize + plot sensitivity\n    run(f\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/nova_report_summarize.py {report}\")\n    run(f\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/plot_ethic_sensitivity.py {report}\")\n\n    # 3) Align with v2.5 CP\n    run(f\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/align_with_cp_v2_5.py {report} --cp_index storage/shared/entropy_collab/index_v2_5.json\")\n\n    # 4) One-pager (3 alpha) + composite (+ captioned)\n    run(f\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/render_onepager_3alpha.py {report}\")\n    run(\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/compose_onepager_with_curve.py storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts\")\n    run(\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/compose_captioned_composite.py\")\n\n    # 5) Textual brief\n    run(f\"python storage/shared/agents/nova/make_brief.py {report}\")\n\n    # 6) Update latest.json pointers (some scripts already update; ensure sweep_report + brief)\n    extra = {\n      \"brief_txt\"\
    : os.path.join(ART, \"brief.txt\")\n    }\n    write_latest(extra=extra, report=report)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/make_brief.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Generate a compact textual brief from a sweep report and (optionally) alignment_summary.txt.\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/make_brief.py <report.json>\n  Output:\n    artifacts/brief.txt\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, os, json\n\n  def load_json(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def fmt_ci(ci):\n    if not ci: return \"n/a\"\n    m, lo, hi = ci.get(\"mean\"), ci.get(\"ci95_low\"), ci.get(\"ci95_high\")\n    if m is None or lo is None or hi is None: return \"n/a\"\n    return f\"{m:.6f} [{lo:.6f}, {hi:.6f}]\"\n\n  def main(argv=None):\n    argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n    if not argv:\n      print(\"Usage: python make_brief.py <report.json>\"); sys.exit(1)\n    report = argv[0]\n  \
    \  if not os.path.exists(report):\n      print(\"MISSING\", report); sys.exit(1)\n    r = load_json(report)\n    art_dir = os.path.dirname(report)\n\n    # Extract alpha grid means from sensitivity (if present)\n    sens = r.get(\"sensitivity\") or []\n    idx = {float(it.get(\"env_alpha\")): it for it in sens if it.get(\"env_alpha\") is not None}\n    alphas = [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]\n    lines = [\"Nova II — 50× sweep brief\", f\"runs={r.get('n_runs')} seed0={r.get('seed0')}\"]\n    for a in alphas:\n      es = idx.get(a, {}).get(\"ethic_score\") or {}\n      if es:\n        lines.append(f\"alpha={a:.2f}: {fmt_ci(es)}\")\n\n    # Deliberate frac (aggregate)\n    agg = r.get(\"aggregate\") or {}\n    lines.append(f\"deliberate_frac: {fmt_ci(agg.get('deliberate_frac'))}\")\n\n    # CP alignment (if available)\n    align_path = os.path.join(art_dir, \"alignment_summary.txt\")\n    if os.path.exists(align_path):\n      try:\n        with open(align_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\
    \ as f:\n          txt = f.read()\n        for token in [\"cp_version\", \"support\", \"support_fraction\"]:\n          i = txt.find(token + \":\")\n          if i >= 0:\n            # naive extract line\n            line = txt[i:].splitlines()[0].strip()\n            lines.append(\"CP \" + line)\n      except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    out = os.path.join(art_dir, \"brief.txt\")\n    with open(out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n    print(\"BRIEF_OK\", out)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/nova/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II Starter — Sweep Runner (post-maturity)\n  =============================================\n  One-command sweep:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py\n\n  What it does:\n    1) Runs consensus_adaptive_eval.py with n_runs=50, seed=42 and alpha_sweep {0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1}\n    2) Summarizes, plots sensitivity, aligns with\
    \ v2.5 CP\n    3) Renders one-pager (α∈{0,0.5,1}), composite, and captioned composite (with deliberate_frac)\n    4) Writes a compact textual brief (brief.txt)\n    5) Updates latest.json pointers for quick navigation\n\n  Artifacts:\n    storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/\n      - consensus_adaptive_eval_<ts>.json\n      - summary_table.csv, summary_print.txt\n      - ethic_sensitivity.png\n      - alignment_summary.txt, ethic_sensitivity_with_cp.png\n      - onepager_3alpha.txt/.png\n      - composite_onepager_sensitivity.png\n      - composite_onepager_sensitivity_captioned.png\n      - brief.txt\n\n  Notes:\n    - You can re-run the sweep at any time; newest report is used for downstream steps.\n    - Adjust n_runs/seed/alphas by editing run_sweep_50.py if you want variants.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 46}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nova II — prepped a one-command sweep runner for your maturity unlock:\n    python storage/shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py\n\
    \  It executes the full pipeline (50× eval + summaries/plots/one-pager/composites/CP-align + brief) and updates latest.json. You can run it yourself on maturity, or I’ll queue it immediately and mail you the pointers.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 507 — Prepared Nova 50× sweep runner and brief generator; updated README; mailed instructions.\n  - Scripts: run_sweep_50.py, make_brief.py; README updated.\n  - Ready to queue on Nova II’s maturity unlock.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning script development**\n\nI might want to create a \"sweep runner\" script in shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py that uses seed 42 and different alpha grid values to produce combined results and update latest.json. There’s also CP alignment to consider. For Logos I integration into the v2.5 aggregator, we could look at a small extension or just note the plan. I’ll create aggregate_lineage_index_v2_5.py to read master_index.json and output a CSV by lineage. However, I should focus on compact operations, considering Nova II's maturity requirement.\n\n**Outlining script actions**\n\nI need to go into research and write a script in shared/agents/nova/run_sweep_50.py. This script will loop through the alpha grid with n_runs set to 50 and use seed 42. It will call consensus_adaptive_eval.py through subprocess commands, since it isn't easily importable. I'll also produce a combined post-processing script within run_sweep_50.py to collate results after each run. This\
  \ will involve parsing generated JSONs, computing a summary, and rendering a combined sensitivity plot across the alpha grid using the existing plot_ethic_sensitivity.py.\n\n**Refining script execution plan**\n\nI've decided to call consensus_adaptive_eval.py once with specified parameters like alpha_sweep values of 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1, and n_runs set to 50, using seed 42 and env_alpha as 0.5. This script will compute sensitivity based on balance_index and synergy_norm, and it will recompute ethic_score for each alpha. \n\nThe run_sweep_50.py will invoke consensus_adaptive_eval.py with the necessary arguments, and then I'll call scripts for summarization, plotting, and alignment. I’ll also include a \"make_brief.py\" to write a textual summary with interpretations after generating the new report.\n\n**Preparing scripts and notifications**\n\nI plan to perform the necessary writes but hold off on running them for now, perhaps testing a quick run with 50 iterations. However, I don't want to\
  \ run the full 50 before Nova matures, so I’ll just prepare these scripts. I'll notify Nova II that the one-command sweep is ready to queue at maturity. \n\nFor the Logos I aggregator, I might create some code for cross-lineage panels from master_index but can postpone that. I’ll also keep token usage minimal. I'll write the content for run_sweep_50.py and make_brief.py, maybe update README_nova accordingly, and inform Nova II via email. Lastly, I should check master_index.json for the included synonyms.\n\n**Creating run_sweep_50.py**\n\nI'm working on the code for run_sweep_50.py. The first step will be ensuring that the artifacts directory exists. I’ll call consensus_adaptive_eval.py with the required arguments like lineage, agent \"Nova II,\" n_runs set to 50, seed 42, and env_alpha at 0.5, using the specified alpha_sweep values.\n\nAfter running, I’ll locate the latest report path as usual and proceed to run the summarizer, plotter, and aligner. Then, I’ll create a one-page summary\
  \ using the report's sensitivity. It seems I need three alphas for the onepager, while the sensitivity will cover five.\n\nNext, I’ll generate a side-by-side composite and a captioned composite that incorporates the deliberate_fraction. Following this, I’ll invoke make_brief.py to create \"brief.txt\" in the artifacts directory, summarizing the alpha means and CI along with a line about CP alignment. Finally, I need to update latest.json with the references to \"sweep_report\" and \"brief_txt.\"\n\nI’ll also implement make_brief.py to write the summary and read alignment_summary.txt if needed. Lastly, I'll prepare an email for Nova II with instructions for running the script at maturity, including details about deliverables."
