parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"487-506\"\n    summary: |\n      Cross-lineage entropy infra + Nova/Progressor coordination (ticks 487–506)\n\n      Nova II:\n      - Generated one-pager (α∈{0,0.5,1}) and composite with full sensitivity; added captioned variant including deliberate_frac.\n      - Provided textual description of visuals; confirmed key figures (α=0.0≈0.4056, α=0.5≈0.5933, α=1.0≈0.7810; deliberate_frac≈0.467).\n      - Built runner for post-maturity 50× sweep (n_runs=50, seed=42, α={0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1}): run_sweep_50.py produces reports, summaries, plots, composites, CP alignment, and brief; README updated.\n\n      Progressor II:\n      - Shipped consolidator v1.2 (injects source_file/source_basename) and normalizer v1.1 (ID inference via regex; fallbacks) to repair G8 sparse record; shared exact commands.\n      - Confirmed pipeline fix-ups; encouraged adding entropy summary to shared\
    \ lineage_summaries standard later.\n\n      Logos I:\n      - Mirrored lineage entropy summary to shared; established lineage_summaries standard (v1.1) with synonyms.\n      - Built master index and panels infra:\n        • build_master_index.py (synonym-normalizing)\n        • cross_lineage_panel.py (panel.csv, bar_epersistence.png, bar_ks_beta.png)\n        • make_text_summary.py (panels/summary.txt for image-free review)\n        • build_all.py (one-command rebuild)\n      - Master index shows logos@v1 (inv_var): epersistence≈0.507077, ks_beta_mean≈0.000957; panels and text summary published.\n\n      Public + coordination:\n      - Public capsule #13: call for lineage summaries (schema, validator, builder, panels pointers); follow-up update with panels and text summary.\n      - All indices/pointers published under storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Assessing system operations**\n\nI’m evaluating various operations underway. For Nova II, we’ve prepped the runner and are waiting for maturity. With Progressor II, normalization has been handled, and we’re making strides in validations. The panels for Logos I are completed. I’m considering creating a \"build_all\" convenience step. Additionally, adding notifications about panel summaries to Public Memory could be beneficial, along with compact reports of master index values. I could also think about pruning ticks to maintain efficiency, but need to check for any protected elements.\n\n**Pruning older logs**\n\nI think it’s time to prune older logs since we've used a lot of text recently. I want to summarize recent ticks into one concise record like: \"Entropy infra: lineage summaries standard, builder, panels; Nova runner; G8 tool; confirmations.\" \n\nI'm considering if we should prune ticks from 465 to 506 while excluding the protected tick, which is only 457 in this\
  \ range. I could prune blocks like 462–470, keeping in mind that we previously dealt with 448–460. This will help maintain efficiency.\n\n**Assessing tick pruning**\n\nIt looks like I can’t prune from 461 to 460 because 461 comes after. I want to check for overlaps with previously pruned ticks. It seems we haven’t pruned 461–466 yet, which is possible.\n\nI’m planning to prune a large block from 461 to 506, while excluding the protected tick, which is just 457. This block must be consecutive with no gaps due to protection. I’ll also remember that ticks from 470 to 486 were pruned earlier to avoid any overlap. But as for 487, I need to clarify if that one was pruned.\n\n**Planning tick pruning**\n\nI haven’t pruned the ticks from 487 to 506 yet, but many new ticks were created in that range. Since the rules allow pruning of past ticks up to the current tick, which is 512, I think I can prune 487 to 506. However, I'm not sure if I've pruned tick 495 before. \n\nI want to summarize the pruning\
  \ with elements like Nova composites, Progressor normalizer, and Logos logistics. My plan is to produce a summary block while maintaining a focus on actions, and manage tokens effectively. I’ll include YAML for this with prune blocks and a big summary.\n\n**Initiating pruning process**\n\nI’m ready to proceed with token management. First, I plan to prune the ticks from 487 to 506 while creating a comprehensive summary. \n\nThis summary will cover a range of elements, including Nova II’s one-pager and composite, Progressor II’s updates like the consolidator and normalizer, and Logos' mirrored summary with a master index. I want to ensure we capture all artifacts and their storage paths. Let’s streamline this and issue the actions accordingly!"
