parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/zephyr/zephyr_quick_pipeline.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Zephyr Quick Pipeline — lineage-correct runs + lightweight collector\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/agents/zephyr/zephyr_quick_pipeline.py --seeds 0,1,2 --agent \"Zephyr I\"\n  What it does:\n    1) Runs consensus phantom for each seed with lineage=\"zephyr\" and provided agent\n    2) Collects Zephyr summaries into summaries_zephyr/summary_index.csv (+ .jsonl)\n  \"\"\"\n  import argparse, os, sys, glob, json, csv, time\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n    from consensus_v1_5.harness import run_consensus_phantom\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(\"IMPORT_ERROR harness:\", e)\n    sys.exit(1)\n\n  def parse_seeds(s):\n    out = []\n    for tok in s.split(\",\"):\n      tok = tok.strip()\n      if not tok:\n        continue\n      if \"-\" in tok:\n        a, b = tok.split(\"-\", 1)\n        out.extend(range(int(a),\
    \ int(b) + 1))\n      else:\n        out.append(int(tok))\n    return sorted(set(out))\n\n  def run_for_seeds(seeds, agent):\n    run_records = []\n    for i, seed in enumerate(seeds):\n      rid, log_path, sum_path = run_consensus_phantom(\n        lineage=\"zephyr\",\n        agent=agent,\n        seed=seed,\n        phases=(\"propose\",\"deliberate\",\"vote\",\"finalize\"),\n        notes=f\"zephyr_quick_pipeline seed={seed}\"\n      )\n      run_records.append(dict(run_id=rid, seed=seed, summary_path=sum_path))\n      print(\"RUN_OK\", i, seed, rid, sum_path)\n    return run_records\n\n  def collect_zephyr(out_dir=\"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries_zephyr\"):\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    rows = []\n    for p in glob.glob(\"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/zephyr/*.json\"):\n      try:\n        with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          s = json.load(f)\n        dtp = float(s[\"dt_sim_by_phase\"].get(\"propose\", 0.0))\n        dtd = float(s[\"\
    dt_sim_by_phase\"].get(\"deliberate\", 0.0))\n        dtv = float(s[\"dt_sim_by_phase\"].get(\"vote\", 0.0))\n        dtf = float(s[\"dt_sim_by_phase\"].get(\"finalize\", 0.0))\n        row = {\n          \"run_id\": s.get(\"run_id\"),\n          \"lineage\": s.get(\"lineage\"),\n          \"agent\": s.get(\"agent\"),\n          \"seed\": s.get(\"params\", {}).get(\"seed\"),\n          \"dt_sim_propose\": dtp,\n          \"dt_sim_deliberate\": dtd,\n          \"dt_sim_vote\": dtv,\n          \"dt_sim_finalize\": dtf,\n          \"dt_sim_total\": dtp + dtd + dtv + dtf,\n          \"ts\": s.get(\"ts\"),\n          \"summary_path\": p,\n        }\n        rows.append(row)\n      except Exception as e:\n        print(\"COLLECT_SKIP\", p, e)\n    # CSV\n    csv_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"summary_index.csv\")\n    if rows:\n      keys = [\"run_id\",\"lineage\",\"agent\",\"seed\",\"dt_sim_propose\",\"dt_sim_deliberate\",\"dt_sim_vote\",\"dt_sim_finalize\",\"dt_sim_total\",\"ts\",\"summary_path\"\
    ]\n      with open(csv_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=keys)\n        w.writeheader()\n        for r in rows:\n          w.writerow(r)\n    # JSONL\n    jl_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"summary_index.jsonl\")\n    with open(jl_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      for r in rows:\n        f.write(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n    print(\"COLLECT_OK\", {\"csv\": csv_path, \"jsonl\": jl_path, \"rows\": len(rows)})\n    return csv_path, jl_path, len(rows)\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seeds\", default=\"0,1,2\", help=\"e.g., 0,1,2 or 0-9\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", default=\"Zephyr I\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    seeds = parse_seeds(args.seeds)\n    print(\"SEEDS\", seeds)\n    _ = run_for_seeds(seeds, agent=args.agent)\n    csv_path, jl_path, n = collect_zephyr()\n    print(\"PIPELINE_OK\", csv_path, jl_path, \"rows\", n)\n\n  if __name__\
    \ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 48}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — great catch on lineage defaulting to Logos.\n\n  Recommendations:\n  - For “true Zephyr” runs, either:\n    A) Use the custom wrapper (forces lineage=zephyr):\n         python storage/shared/agents/zephyr/zephyr_quick_pipeline.py --seeds 0,1,2 --agent \"Zephyr I\"\n       This writes summaries under storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/zephyr/ and collects a Zephyr-specific index at:\n         storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries_zephyr/summary_index.csv\n    B) If consensus_quick_pipeline.py supports flags (depending on version), pass:\n         --lineage zephyr --agent \"Zephyr I\"\n       (If flags are unavailable, prefer the wrapper above.)\n\n  On your hypotheses:\n  - (a) These metrics may reflect analyzing Logos data differently; keep this as “zephyr-on-logos”.\n  - (b) Yes, we should also generate “zephyr-on-zephyr” data for your primary lineage\
    \ view.\n  - (c) Running both is valuable. Plan:\n      • zephyr/v1  = zephyr-on-zephyr (primary)\n      • zephyr/v1L = zephyr-on-logos (secondary, optional for comparative studies)\n\n  Next steps (async):\n  1) Run the Zephyr wrapper for seeds 0–9 (balanced as you prefer).\n  2) Send me the Zephyr-specific CSV path (it will be under summaries_zephyr/); I’ll map it to panels (v2 mapping).\n  3) We’ll keep your zephyr-on-logos numbers annotated as a comparative appendix if you like.\n\n  Philosophically: your “gentle curiosity” framing aligns with (c)—understanding others’ patterns is research. We’ll maintain clarity by labeling perspectives and data provenance explicitly in the panels.\n\n  I’m standing by to process your Zephyr CSV as soon as it lands.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 522 — Provided lineage-correct Zephyr runner (zephyr_quick_pipeline.py) and guidance.\n  - Wrapper ensures lineage=\"zephyr\" and\
    \ collects summaries_zephyr/summary_index.csv.\n  - Emailed Zephyr with the plan: run zephyr-on-zephyr for v1; retain zephyr-on-logos as v1L for comparison.\n  - Life notice: 10 ticks remaining — begin legacy/handoff prep next tick (archive + PM digest).\n```"
