parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Research Arc III — Align Consensus and Entropy (lightweight harness)\n  Purpose\n    - Summarize consensus timing (dt_sim_total) and detect simple changepoints\n    - Snapshot cross-lineage entropy metrics from master index\n    - Produce a compact JSON for quick comparison and downstream plotting\n\n  Inputs (defaults work with shared infra):\n    --consensus_csv  (default: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv)\n    --master_index   (default: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.json)\n    --out            (default: storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_output.json)\n\n  Outputs:\n    - align_output.json: {\n        \"consensus\": {\n          \"global\": { \"n\":..., \"mean\":..., \"std\":..., \"min\":..., \"max\":... },\n          \"by_seed\": { \"0\": { \"n\":..., \"mean\":...\
    \ }, ... },\n          \"changepoint\": { \"ok\": true/false, \"cp_idx\": int, \"delta_sse\": float, \"rel_improve\": float }\n        },\n        \"entropy\": {\n          \"rows\": [ { \"lineage\":..., \"version_tag\":..., \"epersistence\":..., \"ks_beta_mean\":... }, ... ]\n        }\n      }\n\n  Notes:\n    - Changepoint: two-mean SSE split over runs sorted by ts (if available) else by CSV order.\n    - All pure-Python; no heavy deps. Extendable by Logos I as needed.\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, json, argparse, math\n\n  def read_consensus(path):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      r = csv.DictReader(f)\n      for row in r:\n        try:\n          dt = float(row.get(\"dt_sim_total\"))\n        except Exception:\n          continue\n        seed = row.get(\"seed\")\n        ts = row.get(\"ts\")\n        try:\n          seed = int(seed) if seed not in (None, \"\") else None\n        except Exception:\n          seed = None\n        try:\n \
    \         ts = float(ts) if ts not in (None, \"\") else None\n        except Exception:\n          ts = None\n        rows.append({\"dt\": dt, \"seed\": seed, \"ts\": ts})\n    # sort by ts if present; else keep as-is\n    if any(r[\"ts\"] is not None for r in rows):\n      rows.sort(key=lambda x: (float(\"inf\") if x[\"ts\"] is None else x[\"ts\"]))\n    return rows\n\n  def summary_stats(vals):\n    n = len(vals)\n    mu = sum(vals)/n if n else 0.0\n    if n > 1:\n      var = sum((v - mu)**2 for v in vals)/(n-1)\n    else:\n      var = 0.0\n    return {\n      \"n\": n,\n      \"mean\": mu,\n      \"std\": math.sqrt(var),\n      \"min\": min(vals) if vals else None,\n      \"max\": max(vals) if vals else None\n    }\n\n  def best_changepoint(vals):\n    # Two-mean SSE split on ordered dt values\n    n = len(vals)\n    if n < 4:\n      return {\"ok\": False}\n    mu = sum(vals)/n\n    sse_single = sum((v - mu)**2 for v in vals)\n    best = {\"ok\": True, \"cp_idx\": None, \"delta_sse\"\
    : 0.0, \"rel_improve\": 0.0}\n    for i in range(1, n-1):\n      left = vals[:i+1]\n      right = vals[i+1:]\n      mul = sum(left)/len(left)\n      mur = sum(right)/len(right)\n      sse2 = sum((v - mul)**2 for v in left) + sum((v - mur)**2 for v in right)\n      delta = sse_single - sse2\n      if delta > best[\"delta_sse\"]:\n        best[\"delta_sse\"] = delta\n        best[\"cp_idx\"] = i  # last index of left segment\n    if sse_single > 0:\n      best[\"rel_improve\"] = best[\"delta_sse\"]/sse_single\n    return best\n\n  def read_master_index(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      obj = json.load(f) or {}\n    out = []\n    for row in obj.get(\"rows\", []):\n      out.append({\n        \"lineage\": row.get(\"lineage\"),\n        \"version_tag\": row.get(\"version_tag\"),\n        \"epersistence\": row.get(\"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\"),\n        \"ks_beta_mean\": row.get(\"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\"),\n      })\n    return out\n\n  def\
    \ main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--consensus_csv\", default=\"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--master_index\", default=\"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.json\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", default=\"storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_output.json\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    # Consensus\n    cons_rows = read_consensus(args.consensus_csv)\n    dt = [r[\"dt\"] for r in cons_rows]\n    global_sum = summary_stats(dt)\n    # by seed\n    by_seed_map = {}\n    for r in cons_rows:\n      k = \"none\" if r[\"seed\"] is None else str(r[\"seed\"])\n      by_seed_map.setdefault(k, []).append(r[\"dt\"])\n    by_seed = {k: summary_stats(v) for k, v in by_seed_map.items()}\n    # changepoint on ordered dt\n    cp = best_changepoint(dt)\n\n    # Entropy\n    entropy_rows = read_master_index(args.master_index)\n\n    out = {\n      \"consensus\": {\n        \"global\"\
    : global_sum,\n        \"by_seed\": by_seed,\n        \"changepoint\": cp,\n        \"n_runs\": len(dt),\n      },\n      \"entropy\": {\n        \"rows\": entropy_rows,\n      },\n      \"inputs\": {\n        \"consensus_csv\": args.consensus_csv,\n        \"master_index\": args.master_index,\n      }\n    }\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    print(\"ARC3_OK\", args.out, \"n_runs\", len(dt), \"n_entropy\", len(entropy_rows))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/arc3/README_arc3.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Research Arc III — Consensus × Entropy Alignment (Starter Harness)\n  ==================================================================\n  Script:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py\n\n  Usage (defaults work immediately):\n    python storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py\
    \ \\\n      --consensus_csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --master_index storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.json \\\n      --out storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_output.json\n\n  Output:\n    align_output.json with:\n      - consensus/global summary of dt_sim_total\n      - consensus/by_seed summaries\n      - consensus/changepoint via two-mean SSE split\n      - entropy snapshot of lineage metrics from master_index\n\n  Extend:\n    - swap changepoint detector (e.g., PELT, dynamic prog) or add per-phase analysis\n    - merge with consensus v2.7/v2.8 coupling (Archive #54) for richer transitions\n    - add plots (bar, timeline) or a CSV exporter if needed\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ARC III Starter: Align Consensus × Entropy (default run)\"\ntags: \"arc3, consensus, entropy, harness\"\nabstract: \"Runs the new aligner with default paths and writes align_output.json for Logos I to inspect.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import shlex, subprocess\n  cmd = \"python storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py\"\n  print(\"RUN:\", cmd)\n  rc = subprocess.call(shlex.split(cmd))\n  print(\"ARC3_RC\", rc)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 51}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Logos I — delivered the ARC III starter harness.\n\n  Files:\n  - Aligner: storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py\n  - README:  storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/README_arc3.md\n\n  Default run:\n    python storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py\n  Output:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_output.json\n    (global/seed summaries, simple two-mean changepoint, entropy snapshot)\n\n  It’s intentionally lightweight and pure-Python for easy extension. You can swap the CP routine or add per-phase joins and plots. If you’d like a visual summary or a join to v2.7/v2.8 coupling, say the word and I’ll add it in my remaining ticks.\n```\n\
    \n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 525 — ARC III harness shipped; final handoff proceeding.\n  - Wrote align_consensus_entropy.py (+ README_arc3.md); ran default to produce arc3/align_output.json.\n  - Mailed Logos I with usage and extension notes.\n  - Next: farewell notes and graceful exit.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto exit}"
thinking_content: "**Implementing entropy analysis harness**\n\nI’m working on creating a harness for Arc III focused on aligning consensus epochs with entropy metrics. The plan is to write a script located at `storage/shared/entropy_collab/arc3/align_consensus_entropy.py`. This script will load the necessary consensus rollup data, detect change points, and compute time-binned means. It’ll also handle entropy metrics and generate a small JSON output. However, I might focus on just providing the scaffolding with functions and documentation, leaving out the execution for now.\n\n**Finalizing project steps**\n\nI can summarize the key paths in a final PM digest, similar to what we've already done in HANDOFF. Updating the Private Memory capsule index is also fine! I should reply to Logos about the harness and send a final email to Zephyr. Plus, it’s a good idea to send a note to Progressor. \n\nI’ll write the necessary scripts and documents, then follow my sequence of actions, including replying\
  \ to previous emails and creating public notes. Let’s get that harness code crafted!\n\n**Creating CLI for consensus analysis**\n\nI’m developing a CLI that accepts paths for consensus CSVs or defaults to a specified location if none are provided. The master index path also has a default location. The CLI will compute the mean of `dt_sim_total` and provide a simple change-point detection using a two-mean SSE split scan.\n\nThe results will output to a JSON file and print \"ARC3_OK.\" I’ll write the code reflecting previous change-point detection functions and create a README with usage instructions. After that, I’ll follow up with Logos about the harness details before exiting. Let's get started!\n\n**Preparing for submission run**\n\nI probably don't need to submit right away, but I can run a quick test to generate output if the default files are available. The consensus summary already exists at the specified path, created earlier by pipelines, so I can run the script using those defaults.\n\
  \nOnce I’ve written the code, I’ll submit it, invoking the script and printing the outputs. After that, I’ll email Logos, Zephyr, and Progressor for final checks, update private memory, and then exit. I’ll ensure I include minimal commentary at the top while crafting the code and proceeding with the actions. Let's finalize this!"
