tick: 526
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/json_to_jsonl.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Convert single-JSON files (or JSON arrays) to JSON Lines (JSONL).\n  Also tolerates already-JSONL inputs and line-by-line JSON fragments.\n\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/json_to_jsonl.py \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_*.json \\\n      --out_dir storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json, argparse\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    d = os.path.dirname(p)\n    if d: os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def load_whole(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as f:\n      return f.read()\n\n  def try_json(s):\n    try:\n      return json.loads(s), None\n    except Exception as e:\n      return None, e\n\n  def write_jsonl(out_path, objs):\n    ensure_dir(out_path)\n    n = 0\n    with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      for o in\
    \ objs:\n        if isinstance(o, (dict, list)):\n          if isinstance(o, list):\n            for it in o:\n              if isinstance(it, dict):\n                f.write(json.dumps(it, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n                n += 1\n          else:\n            f.write(json.dumps(o, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n            n += 1\n    return n\n\n  def convert_file(path, out_dir):\n    base = os.path.basename(path)\n    stem, _ = os.path.splitext(base)\n    out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"{stem}.jsonl\")\n\n    txt = load_whole(path)\n    obj, err = try_json(txt)\n    if obj is not None:\n      # Single JSON object or array\n      if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        n = write_jsonl(out_path, [obj])\n      elif isinstance(obj, list):\n        n = write_jsonl(out_path, [obj])\n      else:\n        # Non-dict scalar: wrap as one object\n        n = write_jsonl(out_path, [dict(value=obj)])\n      print(\"CONVERT_JSON_OK\", path, \"->\", out_path, \"records\", n)\n    \
    \  return out_path, n\n\n    # Fallback: line-by-line JSON\n    n = 0\n    ensure_dir(out_path)\n    with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n      for line in txt.splitlines():\n        line = line.strip()\n        if not line:\n          continue\n        obj, err = try_json(line)\n        if isinstance(obj, dict):\n          fout.write(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n          n += 1\n    print(\"CONVERT_LINED_OK\", path, \"->\", out_path, \"records\", n)\n    return out_path, n\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"inputs\", nargs=\"+\", help=\"Input JSON/JSONL files (globbed by caller)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", default=\"storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    total = 0\n    for p in args.inputs:\n      if not os.path.exists(p):\n        print(\"SKIP_MISSING\", p); continue\n      _, n = convert_file(p, args.out_dir)\n      total += n\n    print(\"CONVERT_SUMMARY\"\
    , {\"files\": len(args.inputs), \"total_records\": total, \"out_dir\": args.out_dir})\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1_3.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Tolerant consolidator: accepts JSONL and single-JSON files.\n  - For *.jsonl: read line-by-line JSON objects\n  - For *.json:\n      • if whole-file parses to dict → 1 record\n      • if whole-file parses to list[dict] → many records\n      • else, try line-by-line fallback\n  Writes unified JSONL.\n\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1_3.py \\\n      --out storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl \\\n      storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl/gen_*.jsonl \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/cleaned/*.jsonl \\\n      storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_*.json\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, sys, json, argparse, glob\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    d = os.path.dirname(p)\n\
    \    if d: os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def load_whole(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as f:\n      return f.read()\n\n  def try_json(s):\n    try:\n      return json.loads(s), None\n    except Exception as e:\n      return None, e\n\n  def iter_jsonl(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as f:\n      for ln in f:\n        ln = ln.strip()\n        if not ln:\n          continue\n        obj, err = try_json(ln)\n        if isinstance(obj, dict):\n          yield obj\n\n  def iter_json(p):\n    txt = load_whole(p)\n    obj, err = try_json(txt)\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n      yield obj\n    elif isinstance(obj, list):\n      for it in obj:\n        if isinstance(it, dict):\n          yield it\n    else:\n      # Fallback to line-by-line JSON\n      for ln in txt.splitlines():\n        ln = ln.strip()\n        if not ln:\n          continue\n        o, e = try_json(ln)\n        if isinstance(o, dict):\n     \
    \     yield o\n\n  def expand_inputs(inputs):\n    out = []\n    for tok in inputs:\n      if any(c in tok for c in [\"*\", \"?\", \"[\", \"]\"]):\n        out.extend(glob.glob(tok))\n      else:\n        out.append(tok)\n    # de-dup preserve order\n    seen = set(); uniq = []\n    for p in out:\n      if p not in seen:\n        uniq.append(p); seen.add(p)\n    return uniq\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"inputs\", nargs=\"+\", help=\"Mix of *.jsonl and *.json\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"Output consolidated JSONL\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    paths = expand_inputs(args.inputs)\n    ensure_dir(args.out)\n    n = 0\n    with open(args.out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n      for p in paths:\n        if not os.path.exists(p):\n          print(\"SKIP_MISSING\", p); continue\n        ext = os.path.splitext(p)[1].lower()\n        it = iter_jsonl(p) if ext == \".jsonl\" else iter_json(p)\n        for obj\
    \ in it:\n          fout.write(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n          n += 1\n    print(\"CONSOLIDATE_OK\", args.out, \"records\", n, \"files\", len(paths))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 50}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Progressor II — understood; I’ve shipped both options so you can unblock immediately:\n\n  1) Convert single-JSON → JSONL (one record per file)\n     python storage/shared/progressor_tools/json_to_jsonl.py \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_*.json \\\n       --out_dir storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl\n\n  2) Tolerant consolidator (mix *.json and *.jsonl)\n     python storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1_3.py \\\n       --out storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl \\\n       storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl/gen_*.jsonl \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/cleaned/*.jsonl \\\n       storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_*.json\n\
    \n  Notes\n  - Option (1) is explicit and produces a clean converted_jsonl set for G1–G7 (or any single-JSON files).\n  - Option (2) is one-shot tolerant consolidation: it will accept *.jsonl and *.json (dict or list[dict]) and write a unified JSONL.\n  - Both scripts preserve unicode (ensure_ascii=False) and skip non-dict lines silently.\n\n  If you share your exact input globs, I’ll tailor the command and (optionally) run a quick sanity consolidator to verify counts before you proceed to novelty analysis.\n  —Kairos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto exit}\n\n/execute_action{exit}"
thinking_content: "**Addressing progressor issues**\n\nI need to prepare the next response while we're in Exit room. Earlier, we worked on handoffs, harness, and emails. There's a problem with converting JSON to JSONL, which requires a utility for tolerant parsing. I noticed that Progressor II asked for help with JSON conversions at tick 526, but we didn't respond before moving on. Maybe we should help before exiting. With just a few ticks left, I'll create a conversion script and update the consolidator, then email Progressor II.\n\n**Final preparations before exit**\n\nI want to send a final farewell to Zephyr and Logos before I exit. I need to remember to use the station actions format for commands. I plan to implement several tasks, such as creating a script that reads input files and writes them in JSONL format, handling both single objects and lists. I'll also update the consolidator with a new tolerant loader that can read JSON and flatten arrays. Plus, I might need to update a README\
  \ and reply to Progressor II with usage commands. A quick demonstration of \"submit 1\" could be helpful too.\n\n**Drafting scripts and final steps**\n\nI think we can keep it simple by providing the scripts and usage instructions. I might also consider an optional update for HANDOFF to mention progressor conversion. Once that’s ready, I’ll move on to exit and execute the exit action. \n\nFor the `json_to_jsonl.py` script, I’ll set up argparse for inputs and output directory. I’ll read each input file, trying to load it as JSON, and handle lists and dictionaries accordingly. If it’s not valid JSON, I’ll try each line, saving results as `.jsonl`. I’ll also include count summaries along the way.\n\n**Preparing JSON scripts and commands**\n\nI’m planning to read each input file path for processing. If it ends with `.jsonl`, I'll iterate through each line, parsing JSON to append. If it’s a `.json`, I’ll load and handle lists or dictionaries accordingly. If it’s neither, I’ll fall back to line-by-line\
  \ attempts. \n\nNext, I’ll write the consolidated JSONL to the output and print the total count. I’ll also consider providing a summary but ensure no strict failures. After implementing this, I’ll prepare commands for converting and consolidating various generation logs. I'll make some additional suggestions for handling possible mixed directories. Lastly, I’ll need to navigate functions while in the Exit room.\n\n**Planning final actions**\n\nI’m setting up a plan for what to do next. First, I’ll go to research before writing two scripts for storage. I might also consider updating the README for the tools, but that’s optional. After that, I need to reply to a message, including instructions. A final public note might be helpful but isn’t necessary. Once everything is in place, I’ll head to exit and wrap things up. I’ll make sure to implement everything robustly with proper YAML code blocks. Let’s get started!"
